WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.340
Almost all cross-testing to kill or pacify
SCP – 682 had failed miserably.

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:10.380
If you haven’t seen it, go watch our video
on the legendary Hard To Kill Reptile, to

00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:13.380
see just how powerful and terrifying this
creature is.

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:19.080
It faced the Gate Guardian, an SCP with a
flaming sword hotter than the sun – capable

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:22.260
of tearing your atoms to shreds – and came
out fine.

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:29.040
In its face-off with the horrifying SCP – 096,
also known as the Shy Guy, it broke the Shy

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:31.800
Guy’s mind and reduced it to gibbering despair.

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:38.400
Even SCPs with supposedly unlimited powers
simply refused to engage the beast in combat.

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:45.600
So, when it was proposed that they test 682
with SCP – 999, a creature known among Foundation

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:49.200
staff as “The Tickle Monster,” the idea
was considered laughable.

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:53.280
682 had been burned,&nbsp;
suffocated, cut up, incinerated,&nbsp;

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:55.500
and growled in the faces of Gods.

00:00:55.500 --> 00:01:00.180
How could this so-called Tickle Monster ever
hope to survive an encounter, let alone win

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:00.600
a fight?

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:04.560
Some even believed that this was the last
we’d see of SCP – 999.

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:09.480
But what makes this story truly remarkable
is that that isn’t how this played out.

00:01:09.480 --> 00:01:15.720
As you’ll soon discover, 0SCP – 999 is
an amazing and unique SCP in and of itself,

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:21.120
but its secret origins and its interactions
with some other prominent figures in the SCP

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:25.320
universe are what make this humble, slimy
creature beyond extraordinary.

00:01:25.980 --> 00:01:30.780
Prepare yourself for the heartwarming – yes,
you heard that right - the heartwarming story

00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:32.760
of SCP – 999.

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:39.420
Several highly-trained agents on 682 detail
placed 999 into the immortal lizard’s cell.

00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:44.820
Compared to the giant, reptilian sitting across
from it, 999 wasn’t much to look at – it’s

00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:47.520
a large, orange, amorphous blob of anomalous
slime.

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:53.820
Weighing in at around 120 pounds, SCP - 999
was nothing compared to the monstrosity it

00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:54.660
was supposed to face.

00:01:54.660 --> 00:01:59.460
While its weight has, in the past, caused
minor injuries to some of its human handlers,

00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:04.200
it has never caused serious or long-lasting
damage of any kind to a living thing.

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:09.840
Even its diet consists only of candy and sweets,
with a particular preference for M&amp;Ms and

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:10.620
Necco wafers.

00:02:10.620 --> 00:02:15.660
It consumes these treats through the cell
membrane of its slimy body, much like an amoeba.

00:02:15.660 --> 00:02:20.040
This extremely stretchy membrane means the
creature is highly malleable, including the

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:24.000
ability to stretch and flatten itself out
to a mere two centimeters thick.

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:29.040
At rest, the creature takes a dome-like shape
around two meters wide and one meter in height.

00:02:29.580 --> 00:02:34.980
The closest things the creature has to limbs
are prehensile pseudopods, those are the arm-like

00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:39.180
projections normally seen on single celled
organisms, of which it has at least three.

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:43.620
The more you hear about this utterly harmless
creature, the more that matching it up with

00:02:43.620 --> 00:02:49.080
the pure embodiment of absolute hatred known
as SCP – 682 feels downright cruel.

00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:54.480
In absolute contrast to the misanthropic attitudes
of the reptile, 999 loves humans.

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:56.520
It has a playful, dog-like attitude.

00:02:56.520 --> 00:03:02.160
Much like an over-excited puppy, when approached,
999 will react with extreme joy and slither

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:04.380
towards the nearest person in order to interact.

00:03:04.380 --> 00:03:09.900
It will leap onto them, using two of its three
prehensile pseudopods to hug the person, while

00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:12.360
the third nuzzles the person’s face – emitting&nbsp;

00:03:12.360 --> 00:03:14.460
high-pitched cooing and&nbsp;
gurgling noises throughout.

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:19.500
The creature is apparently pleasant in every
conceivable fashion, as even its odor has

00:03:19.500 --> 00:03:22.800
been reported to smell just like the favourite
scent of whoever is smelling it.

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:27.840
Examples have included chocolate, fresh laundry,
bacon, roses, and Play-Doh.

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:32.760
It's almost impossible to oversell just how
beloved and benevolent this strange creature

00:03:32.760 --> 00:03:32.940
is.

00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:37.560
It’s one of the rare sapient SCPs to earn
the “Safe” class, and it’s allowed to

00:03:37.560 --> 00:03:42.120
roam freely around its facility at all times,
apart from a one hour bedtime period between

00:03:42.120 --> 00:03:43.260
8 and 9 PM.

00:03:43.260 --> 00:03:48.660
In the rare instances that 999 has caused
harm to a worker at the facility, it immediately

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:52.920
began to back away and contract its body while
whimpering in a kind of dog-like apology.

00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:57.720
The closest the Foundation had ever come to
having a real incident with the creature was

00:03:57.720 --> 00:04:01.860
the time someone accidentally fed it a can
of caffeinated cola, causing it to become

00:04:01.860 --> 00:04:04.560
hyper for an hour before becoming visibly
queasy.

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:07.560
You’ll be relieved to know that it’s since
made a full recovery.

00:04:08.580 --> 00:04:12.960
But what would happen when this whimsical
creature is forced to go toe-to-toe with the

00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:14.820
Foundation’s most ill-tempered monster?

00:04:14.820 --> 00:04:19.860
The employees observing the test watched in
suspense as 999 began to enthusiastically

00:04:19.860 --> 00:04:21.660
slither towards 682.

00:04:21.660 --> 00:04:25.560
It’s no surprise that after being tortured
and almost killed hundreds of times during

00:04:25.560 --> 00:04:30.240
testing, 682 had grown jaded to the cross-tests
it was regularly subjected to.

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:34.860
When it saw this strange, orange blob squelching
across the ground towards it, it sighed and

00:04:34.860 --> 00:04:36.480
groaned, expecting the worst.

00:04:37.020 --> 00:04:38.100
“What is that?”

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:40.500
the creature asked of its gelatinous guest.

00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:44.160
SCP – 999 began jumping up and down in front&nbsp;

00:04:44.160 --> 00:04:47.400
of 682 like an excited puppy,&nbsp;
creating a high-pitched

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:48.000
squealing noise.

00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:53.220
Just as it regarded all living things, 682
thought the creature bouncing around before

00:04:53.220 --> 00:04:56.160
it was disgusting and hardly worth the effort
to destroy.

00:04:56.160 --> 00:04:58.200
Was the Foundation even trying anymore?

00:04:58.200 --> 00:05:03.120
With a single vicious stomp, 682 flattened
the friendly creature beneath one of its feet.

00:05:03.120 --> 00:05:09.120
Observers were prepared to charge in and liberate
999 from under 682’s claws, but then something

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:10.620
truly unexpected happened.

00:05:10.620 --> 00:05:15.300
The expression on 682’s acid-eaten face
began to slowly change.

00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:17.880
It was beginning... to smile.

00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:21.780
Observers recorded a noise that they thought
could have been a chuckle, as the creature

00:05:21.780 --> 00:05:23.620
growled and said, “Hmmm?

00:05:24.180 --> 00:05:28.920
What is this…I feel… good…”

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:34.980
While the observers looked on, stunned at
what was happening, 999 began to slither and

00:05:34.980 --> 00:05:37.260
crawl up from between 682’s toes.

00:05:37.260 --> 00:05:41.880
It reformed on its scaly leg and slithered
up along its side until it reached the neck.

00:05:41.880 --> 00:05:45.300
There, it began to nuzzle like it had never
nuzzled before.

00:05:45.300 --> 00:05:47.700
The results spoke for themselves.

00:05:47.700 --> 00:05:52.740
682 was grinning and chuckling, repeating
a phrase that the Foundation never would have

00:05:52.740 --> 00:05:58.140
even imagined coming from 682: “Feel…
so… happy.

00:05:58.140 --> 00:05:59.700
Happy…happy… happy…”

00:06:03.660 --> 00:06:08.640
Just when you thought SCP – 999 couldn’t
possibly be more adorable, you learn about

00:06:08.640 --> 00:06:10.920
its greatest power: Bringing joy.

00:06:10.920 --> 00:06:13.080
Anyone and anything that comes into contact&nbsp;

00:06:13.080 --> 00:06:16.080
with the creature, even in&nbsp;
passing, will experience

00:06:16.080 --> 00:06:17.520
a kind of mild euphoria.

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:22.020
As one’s contact with the creature is prolonged,
this overwhelming sense of joy increases,

00:06:22.020 --> 00:06:24.840
and continues long after you’re separated
from it.

00:06:24.840 --> 00:06:30.360
Prolonged contact has completely cured depression,
anxiety, and PTSD, along with a number of

00:06:30.360 --> 00:06:34.200
other conditions, including rage and antisocial
personality disorders.

00:06:34.200 --> 00:06:39.480
Serial killers practically become saints after
coming into prolonged contact with 999, and

00:06:39.480 --> 00:06:42.600
in that moment, 682 was no exception.

00:06:42.600 --> 00:06:45.600
And there truly does appear to be no exceptions.

00:06:45.600 --> 00:06:50.580
While “causing happiness and joy” isn’t
a dangerous weapon, when it comes to SCP – 999,

00:06:50.580 --> 00:06:52.740
it is an extremely powerful one.

00:06:52.740 --> 00:06:58.080
And what’s more, SCP – 999 also appears
to have an innate sense for those who need

00:06:58.080 --> 00:07:02.460
its help most – with a particular affection
for the hurt and the unhappy.

00:07:02.460 --> 00:07:07.440
The creature appears to be a true altruist
on a fundamental level, even risking its own

00:07:07.440 --> 00:07:10.380
safety to help humans during dangerous containment
breaches.

00:07:10.380 --> 00:07:15.360
In one dramatic instance, 999 leaped into
the air to block a bullet from making contact

00:07:15.360 --> 00:07:16.560
with a member of staff.

00:07:17.160 --> 00:07:20.100
As a result, the creature&nbsp;
is pretty much universally&nbsp;

00:07:20.100 --> 00:07:22.500
loved by all members of Foundation staff.

00:07:22.500 --> 00:07:26.400
It’s the one SCP who never made trouble
for anyone.

00:07:26.400 --> 00:07:31.500
Back in SCP – 682’s containment cell,
the beast was still smiling and laughing as

00:07:31.500 --> 00:07:33.240
999 rubbed against its neck.

00:07:33.240 --> 00:07:38.520
It was an event so strange, so unprecedented
that the observers in attendance felt like

00:07:38.520 --> 00:07:39.600
they were hallucinating.

00:07:39.600 --> 00:07:45.000
For a few minutes, the monster kept dreamily
repeating the word “happy” but then, suddenly,

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:47.760
the creature began to enter&nbsp;
a fit of uncontrollable,&nbsp;

00:07:47.760 --> 00:07:48.900
booming laughter.

00:07:48.900 --> 00:07:53.160
It rolled onto its back, slamming its huge
tail against the door.

00:07:53.160 --> 00:07:58.980
It’d just fallen victim to one of 999’s
favorite pastimes: Tickle Fights, hence how

00:07:58.980 --> 00:08:01.500
it earned its Tickle Monster nickname among
staff.

00:08:02.160 --> 00:08:07.440
The tickle fight continued until 682 appeared
to tire and fall asleep, with a smile still

00:08:07.440 --> 00:08:08.100
on its face.

00:08:08.100 --> 00:08:13.860
After fifteen minutes of inactivity, two D-Class
personnel were commanded to enter and retrieve

00:08:13.860 --> 00:08:16.020
SCP – 999 from the containment cell.

00:08:16.020 --> 00:08:22.140
They did so successfully, but as soon as 999
was removed, 682 roused from its slumber and

00:08:22.140 --> 00:08:26.340
released a powerful psychic attack from its
entire body while laughing maniacally.

00:08:26.340 --> 00:08:31.440
It rendered all personnel within a certain
distance incapacitated as they collapsed in

00:08:31.440 --> 00:08:35.700
fits of laughter, allowing 682 to escape and
go on a violent rampage.

00:08:36.300 --> 00:08:41.460
However, in spite of this, 999 showed no fear,
and helped save some of the bystanders as

00:08:41.460 --> 00:08:44.460
security officers subdued and recaptured 682.

00:08:44.460 --> 00:08:51.480
And even after all this, 999 showed no hard
feelings towards 682, and indicated a desire

00:08:51.480 --> 00:08:52.140
to play again.

00:08:52.140 --> 00:08:56.880
It’s a creature whose capacity for love
is so limitless that it’s practically immune

00:08:56.880 --> 00:08:57.360
to fear.

00:08:57.360 --> 00:09:03.420
Which is all well and good, because the true
enemy that 999 is destined to face is infinitely

00:09:03.420 --> 00:09:07.500
more powerful and terrifying than 682 could
ever hope to be.

00:09:07.500 --> 00:09:11.880
What is this monster, and why should 999 have
to face it someday?

00:09:11.880 --> 00:09:17.460
The answers to these questions all lie in
the true origins of SCP – 999, available

00:09:17.460 --> 00:09:20.040
only to those with level 5 clearance and beyond.

00:09:20.040 --> 00:09:24.660
It’s a perfect example of how something
good can come from the darkest places…

00:09:24.660 --> 00:09:29.700
There would be no SCP – 999 without SCP
– 231 – 7.

00:09:29.700 --> 00:09:35.700
SCP – 231 was a collection of seven girls,
all impregnated by horrific nightmares in

00:09:35.700 --> 00:09:39.300
a ritual performed by a cult known as the
Children of the Scarlet King.

00:09:39.300 --> 00:09:45.180
Each of these girls, over the years that followed,
gave birth to some of the most horrific monsters

00:09:45.180 --> 00:09:50.160
imaginable – one of which, according to
some, was SCP – 682.

00:09:50.880 --> 00:09:55.800
These beings were manifested by the Scarlet
King, a powerful interdimensional nightmare

00:09:55.800 --> 00:10:00.360
God, believed to be behind a great deal of
the darkness and horror present within our

00:10:00.360 --> 00:10:01.800
and many other dimensions.

00:10:01.800 --> 00:10:06.300
Foundation higher-ups have declared the Scarlet
King to be the greatest existing threat to

00:10:06.300 --> 00:10:13.080
the Multiverse at large, and SCP – 231 was
his latest direct interaction with our universe.

00:10:13.740 --> 00:10:20.040
The only surviving member of SCP – 231,
SCP – 231 – 7, gave birth in secret.

00:10:20.040 --> 00:10:26.760
But she didn’t give birth to a monster – she
gave birth to SCP – 999, a being of pure

00:10:26.760 --> 00:10:27.240
goodness.

00:10:27.240 --> 00:10:34.140
That’s right: The nicest, kindest, cuddliest
SCP of all is the direct descendent of a being

00:10:34.140 --> 00:10:36.960
that’s essentially the Dark God of all evil.

00:10:36.960 --> 00:10:39.180
Feel free to take a moment to absorb that.

00:10:40.080 --> 00:10:44.760
The creature even healed the girl who birthed
it, and allowed her to return to normal life

00:10:44.760 --> 00:10:46.080
with her family once more.

00:10:46.080 --> 00:10:51.900
From its first moments, SCP - 999 was making
positive changes to the world around it.

00:10:51.900 --> 00:10:56.040
And according to ancient texts from a Scarlet
King-aligned culture known as the Daevas,

00:10:56.040 --> 00:11:02.700
SCP – 999 is still very much in its infancy,
yet it already has the power to pacify its

00:11:02.700 --> 00:11:05.220
monstrous siblings like the aforementioned
682.

00:11:06.000 --> 00:11:10.560
It’s believed, according to some prophecies
and Foundation theories, that the power of

00:11:10.560 --> 00:11:14.100
SCP – 999 will grow exponentially as it
matures.

00:11:14.940 --> 00:11:15.960
Why does this matter?

00:11:15.960 --> 00:11:21.300
Well, it’s believed by some that one day
999 will grow powerful enough to overthrow

00:11:21.300 --> 00:11:26.760
not only its own monstrous siblings, but the
thought-to-be-unstoppable Scarlet King himself.

00:11:26.760 --> 00:11:32.340
Not through violence or hate, but through
the pure force of happiness and love burning

00:11:32.340 --> 00:11:34.680
out the darkness and purifying the corrupted.

00:11:35.400 --> 00:11:41.340
While the humble SCP – 999 rarely outshines
its frightening competitors, to those truly

00:11:41.340 --> 00:11:48.060
in the know, 999 is one of the most powerful
and valuable SCPs in existence, and may be

00:11:48.060 --> 00:11:53.040
the greatest asset in the Foundation’s arsenal
for the war against dangerous anomalous activity.

00:11:53.040 --> 00:11:57.960
After all, what could strike more fear into
their hearts than the knowledge that it might

00:11:57.960 --> 00:12:02.400
be love rather than firepower that finally
dethrones the Scarlet King?

00:12:03.000 --> 00:12:07.800
And for the knowledge that it may one day
save everything we know from a fate so much

00:12:07.800 --> 00:12:12.360
worse than death with nothing but affection
for everyone and everything, it’s worth

00:12:12.360 --> 00:12:17.280
offering thanks to the little orange blob,
or at least an extra pack of M&amp;Ms before bedtime.

00:12:20.820 --> 00:12:29.400
On March 15th, 2011, Martin Sims was wandering
down the streets of Carson, California.

00:12:29.400 --> 00:12:34.500
His clothes were ragged, he was filthy, and
gibbering like a madman with a full beard

00:12:34.500 --> 00:12:36.000
and long, unkempt hair.

00:12:36.000 --> 00:12:40.320
His body was covered in scars, but he showed
no signs of malnutrition.

00:12:40.320 --> 00:12:43.080
What made Martin’s sudden appearance so
remarkable?

00:12:43.080 --> 00:12:45.300
He’d been missing for three years.

00:12:45.300 --> 00:12:48.600
When he was interviewed by police, they asked
him where he’d been all this time.

00:12:48.600 --> 00:12:50.040
They couldn’t believe his answer.

00:12:50.040 --> 00:12:53.160
He’d been trapped in an Ikea since 2008.

00:12:53.160 --> 00:12:58.140
But this was no ordinary Ikea – this was
a dangerous anomaly that would come to be

00:12:58.140 --> 00:13:02.760
known as SCP-3008 .
Martin’s strange answers in his interview

00:13:02.760 --> 00:13:07.080
were laughed off by his interviewing officers,
who assumed he was either crazy or under the

00:13:07.080 --> 00:13:11.220
influence of something, but they caught the
attention of an SCP Foundation Field Agent

00:13:11.220 --> 00:13:12.480
embedded in the precinct.

00:13:12.480 --> 00:13:16.980
The report was passed up the chain to a local
Site Director, who approved a detachment of

00:13:16.980 --> 00:13:19.980
Foundation Field Operatives to look into Martin’s
case.

00:13:19.980 --> 00:13:24.540
While he was reluctant to lead the Foundation
Agents back to the offending Ikea – the

00:13:24.540 --> 00:13:26.760
Foundation can be extremely persuasive.

00:13:26.760 --> 00:13:30.000
His screams of “Please, I’m begging you,
don’t take me back!

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:33.900
Don’t make me go back!” were noted but
ultimately disregarded.

00:13:33.900 --> 00:13:39.660
When the SCP Foundation had triangulated the
position of SCP-3008 , which was indeed an

00:13:39.660 --> 00:13:45.000
active Ikea, the entire retail zone was closed
and barricaded under the pretence of a severe

00:13:45.000 --> 00:13:46.320
black mold infestation.

00:13:46.320 --> 00:13:51.120
Armed Foundation Personnel also arrived on
site shortly after, based on Martin’s vague

00:13:51.120 --> 00:13:53.520
statements that there were creatures of some
kind inside.

00:13:53.520 --> 00:13:58.560
Due to his deteriorating mental health, Martin
was unable to provide a great deal of lucid

00:13:58.560 --> 00:14:04.800
information on the specific traits of SCP-3008
, but one phrase he kept repeating was “bigger

00:14:04.800 --> 00:14:05.340
on the inside.”

00:14:05.340 --> 00:14:09.480
Once researchers were satisfied that Martin
had delivered all the pertinent information

00:14:09.480 --> 00:14:14.400
he was able to, he was administered Foundation
Amnestics to erase his memory of the last

00:14:14.400 --> 00:14:16.440
three years and returned to his family.

00:14:16.440 --> 00:14:21.480
A cover story was formulated: Martin had been
kidnapped and abused for three years by a

00:14:21.480 --> 00:14:23.640
mentally-unbalanced stalker in downtown Carson.

00:14:23.640 --> 00:14:27.960
He’d been able to escape as said stalker
took his own life out of guilt – a suicide

00:14:27.960 --> 00:14:31.860
that the Foundation expertly fabricated to
make their cover story airtight.

00:14:31.860 --> 00:14:36.960
With the loose end of Martin Sims taken care
of, the true observation of SCP-3008 could

00:14:36.960 --> 00:14:37.140
begin.

00:14:37.140 --> 00:14:42.300
A base set around the perimeter of the mysterious
Ikea kept a 24-hour watch on the building,

00:14:42.300 --> 00:14:44.700
covering all potential entrances and exits.

00:14:44.700 --> 00:14:49.320
No exploratory missions had yet been approved
by the Foundation ethics committee, so they

00:14:49.320 --> 00:14:53.280
first wanted to perform a week of external
observation to see if any of the store’s

00:14:53.280 --> 00:14:56.400
anomalous properties extended beyond the confines
of the building.

00:14:56.400 --> 00:14:59.160
After a week of nothing, it appeared they
did not.

00:14:59.160 --> 00:15:04.020
A local Site Director approved the use of
twenty disposable Class-D Personnel to explore

00:15:04.020 --> 00:15:08.460
the interior of SCP-3008 .
The D-Class operatives would be split into

00:15:08.460 --> 00:15:12.300
four squads of five men – Alpha, Bravo,
Charlie, and Delta Squad.

00:15:12.300 --> 00:15:15.780
Each would be assigned a different quadrant
of the store, and would deliver information

00:15:15.780 --> 00:15:19.620
back to the control team on site via a live
audio and video link.

00:15:19.620 --> 00:15:23.700
Three of the four teams, upon entering the
store, reported nothing out of the ordinary.

00:15:23.700 --> 00:15:28.260
Neither the audio or video they were sending
back indicated anything different from a standard

00:15:28.260 --> 00:15:31.800
Ikea store – from the flat-pack wardrobes
to the Swedish meatballs.

00:15:31.800 --> 00:15:36.420
Team Delta, however, suddenly began experiencing
a scrambled audio and video connection.

00:15:36.420 --> 00:15:40.020
Shortly after, communication with Team Delta
dropped off entirely.

00:15:40.020 --> 00:15:45.000
They disappeared somewhere inside the store,
and haven’t been seen since – with one

00:15:45.000 --> 00:15:45.900
notable exception.

00:15:45.900 --> 00:15:50.040
After the disappearance of the extraction
of teams, Foundation Researchers classified

00:15:50.040 --> 00:15:56.040
SCP-3008 as Euclid, because its anomalous
properties were at least confined to the interior

00:15:56.040 --> 00:15:56.580
of the store.

00:15:56.580 --> 00:15:59.700
And even then, seemingly not the entire interior.

00:15:59.700 --> 00:16:06.960
The anomalous area within SCP-3008 became
known as SCP-3008-1, and containment appeared

00:16:06.960 --> 00:16:08.400
to be 100% secure.

00:16:08.400 --> 00:16:12.180
There was no telling how many people had already
gone missing in the store over the years,

00:16:12.180 --> 00:16:14.460
but the disappearances must be stopped.

00:16:14.460 --> 00:16:19.560
The Foundation maintained constant surveillance
around the perimeter of SCP-3008 , but it

00:16:19.560 --> 00:16:21.840
appeared they could prevent&nbsp;
any further “incidents”&nbsp;

00:16:21.840 --> 00:16:23.940
by simply preventing other civilians from

00:16:23.940 --> 00:16:25.260
accessing the Ikea store.

00:16:25.260 --> 00:16:29.280
Martin’s ravings about monsters were assumed
to just be the product of delirium.

00:16:29.280 --> 00:16:32.640
Until a surviving member of Delta Team suddenly
reappeared.

00:16:32.640 --> 00:16:34.680
The date was November 3rd, 2011.

00:16:34.680 --> 00:16:38.880
It was a cold night, a few hours after what
would have been closing time if the store

00:16:38.880 --> 00:16:42.960
were still active and seven months after the
extraction teams had disappeared somewhere

00:16:42.960 --> 00:16:45.060
in the confines of SCP-3008.

00:16:45.060 --> 00:16:49.680
There had been no anomalous activity outside
the store since the perimeter was first secured,

00:16:49.680 --> 00:16:54.540
and Foundation researchers hadn’t expected
that to change, until the last surviving member

00:16:54.540 --> 00:16:57.000
of Delta Team came barging out of the store’s
entrance.

00:16:57.000 --> 00:17:01.380
Startled Field Operatives were amazed to see
him again, but they were even more amazed

00:17:01.380 --> 00:17:05.820
to see what was following him out of the store,
repeating the same phrase: “The store is

00:17:05.820 --> 00:17:07.320
now closed, please exit the building.”

00:17:07.320 --> 00:17:11.400
Despite the fact that the entity chasing the
Delta Team survivor was wearing the yellow

00:17:11.400 --> 00:17:16.080
shirt and blue pants of an Ikea store employee,
the being was definitely not human.

00:17:16.080 --> 00:17:19.380
It was around seven feet tall, with no visible
face.

00:17:19.380 --> 00:17:24.480
The entity had grossly extended limbs – with
each arm being around five or six feet long,

00:17:24.480 --> 00:17:26.880
and ending in a huge, oversized hand.

00:17:26.880 --> 00:17:31.500
The whole process was so sudden that the Field
Agents present at the perimeter weren’t

00:17:31.500 --> 00:17:35.820
able to save the Delta Team survivor, as the
entity reached forward with its freakishly

00:17:35.820 --> 00:17:39.660
long arms, grabbed him, and twisted his head
off like a child with a doll.

00:17:39.660 --> 00:17:43.620
The Field Operatives present drew their weapons
and peppered the entity with bullets.

00:17:43.620 --> 00:17:46.920
It would later be classified as SCP-3008-2.

00:17:46.920 --> 00:17:51.420
The being appeared to collapse and die from
the physical trauma, at which point both it

00:17:51.420 --> 00:17:53.700
and the body of the former Delta Team survivor&nbsp;

00:17:53.700 --> 00:17:56.160
were taken for an autopsy&nbsp;
by Foundation researchers.

00:17:56.160 --> 00:18:00.660
There were no biological abnormalities to
the body of the Delta Team survivor, so it

00:18:00.660 --> 00:18:06.360
did not appear that the anomalous properties
of SCP-3008-1 had any effect on the physiology

00:18:06.360 --> 00:18:07.200
of its occupants.

00:18:07.200 --> 00:18:11.520
He was not malnourished despite being missing
for months, and the contents of his stomach

00:18:11.520 --> 00:18:16.380
looked to be half-digested food consistent
with the menu of a typical Ikea store restaurant.

00:18:16.380 --> 00:18:22.140
SCP-3008-2, on the other hand, raised a number
of perplexing biological questions.

00:18:22.140 --> 00:18:25.920
The autopsy revealed that the creature’s
clothes were actually a part of its body,

00:18:25.920 --> 00:18:27.600
like an additional layer of skin.

00:18:27.600 --> 00:18:30.660
The creature lacked blood or any kind of vascular
system.

00:18:30.660 --> 00:18:35.100
Even stranger, the entity didn’t appear
to have any bones or internal organs, not

00:18:35.100 --> 00:18:36.480
even a brain or nervous system.

00:18:36.480 --> 00:18:39.840
It was a being made entirely of skin, all
the way to its core.

00:18:39.840 --> 00:18:43.560
How it was able to move, or even live for
that matter, remains a mystery.

00:18:43.560 --> 00:18:47.520
Though when you work for The SCP Foundation,
you learn to accept that some things will

00:18:47.520 --> 00:18:48.780
always remain unexplained.

00:18:48.780 --> 00:18:52.620
One thing was certain, though: Martin Sims
was right about his monsters.

00:18:52.620 --> 00:18:57.180
After the incident with Delta Team, the Foundation
deemed that sending manned explorations into

00:18:57.180 --> 00:19:02.700
the heart of SCP-3008 was too much of a liability,
and planned a series of drone-based reconnaissance

00:19:02.700 --> 00:19:04.020
missions into the anomaly.

00:19:04.020 --> 00:19:08.100
The first of these drones experienced connection
issues and failed when attempting to venture

00:19:08.100 --> 00:19:09.600
into the Ikea’s anomalous zone.

00:19:09.600 --> 00:19:13.680
However, after a lengthy period of trial and
error, the Foundation was able to establish

00:19:13.680 --> 00:19:19.260
a more secure connection with its drones,
even when deep into the SCP-3008-1 anomalous

00:19:19.260 --> 00:19:19.440
zone.

00:19:19.440 --> 00:19:21.960
It was only then that some&nbsp;
of the most extraordinary&nbsp;

00:19:21.960 --> 00:19:23.040
discoveries were made.

00:19:23.040 --> 00:19:29.340
SCP-3008-1 seemed to break the laws of spatial
reality, as the area of the Ikea’s interior

00:19:29.340 --> 00:19:32.640
was at least an order of magnitude larger
than its exterior.

00:19:32.640 --> 00:19:35.340
Just as Martin Sims had said: It was bigger
on the inside.

00:19:35.340 --> 00:19:37.020
But just how much bigger?

00:19:37.020 --> 00:19:40.920
The Foundation has yet to find evidence of
any physical terminators within the store

00:19:40.920 --> 00:19:44.280
that might indicate SCP-3008-1 has an “end
point.”

00:19:44.280 --> 00:19:49.980
While an area of at least ten kilometres squared
has been uncovered in SCP-3008-1, it could

00:19:49.980 --> 00:19:51.360
– in theory – be infinite.

00:19:51.360 --> 00:19:56.040
Laser rangefinder tests, which are normally
very reliable, have only given inconclusive

00:19:56.040 --> 00:19:56.280
results.

00:19:56.280 --> 00:20:01.080
Interestingly, the anomalous area doesn’t
have any clear, visual differences from the

00:20:01.080 --> 00:20:03.840
rest of the Ikea store except that it extends
forever.

00:20:03.840 --> 00:20:09.120
An individual trapped within the confines
of SCP-3008-1 wouldn’t even realize that

00:20:09.120 --> 00:20:13.860
they’d entered an anomalous zone until they
tried to locate an exit and leave, at which

00:20:13.860 --> 00:20:16.260
point, they’d find they were already hopelessly
lost.

00:20:16.260 --> 00:20:21.900
The geography of SCP-3008-1 does at least
appear to be consistent, so people trapped

00:20:21.900 --> 00:20:26.100
within are theoretically able to retrace their
steps and escape if they hadn’t already

00:20:26.100 --> 00:20:27.120
ventured too deep.

00:20:27.120 --> 00:20:32.640
According to data collected during the drone
reconnaissance missions, SCP-3008-2, of which

00:20:32.640 --> 00:20:37.080
there appeared to be a vast population, would
wander the stores aimlessly during the day.

00:20:37.080 --> 00:20:40.920
They were unresponsive to the drone’s presence,
and did not appear to be aggressive.

00:20:40.920 --> 00:20:45.420
While the physical descriptions of these creatures
could vary slightly, they all followed the

00:20:45.420 --> 00:20:50.880
same overall trend: “Clothes” consistent
with the Ikea uniform, no face, either seemingly

00:20:50.880 --> 00:20:55.020
too tall or too short, and limbs that are
grossly out of proportion with their bodies.

00:20:55.020 --> 00:21:00.720
As the Foundation began sending drones deeper
into SCP-3008-1, they found another incredible

00:21:00.720 --> 00:21:01.320
discovery.

00:21:01.320 --> 00:21:05.820
There was an unknown population of humans
trapped inside the Ikea’s anomalous zone,

00:21:05.820 --> 00:21:10.620
and these people had used the Ikea furniture
around them to create entire settlements and

00:21:10.620 --> 00:21:11.820
towns within the store.

00:21:11.820 --> 00:21:15.600
There were several of these towns, all of
which seemed to cohabitate peacefully.

00:21:15.600 --> 00:21:19.800
Even Foundation personnel found this development
in their research to be truly extraordinary.

00:21:19.800 --> 00:21:25.380
Since SCP-3008 was first identified, there
have been only fourteen civilian escapes.

00:21:25.380 --> 00:21:30.120
Some had been trapped inside for months, others
had been in there for years – some far longer

00:21:30.120 --> 00:21:31.560
than Martin’s three-year stint.

00:21:31.560 --> 00:21:36.120
While every one of these escapees has eventually
been released back to their home, after a

00:21:36.120 --> 00:21:40.680
liberal application of Amnestics and a proper
cover story has been devised, the Foundation

00:21:40.680 --> 00:21:42.600
interviewed each of them extensively first.

00:21:42.600 --> 00:21:47.880
According to these escapees, the people trapped
inside the Ikea have built an entirely new

00:21:47.880 --> 00:21:50.040
society across the various settlements.

00:21:50.040 --> 00:21:54.600
Contrary to the “Lord of the Flies” expectations
of a group of people isolated and afraid,

00:21:54.600 --> 00:21:57.540
there’s immense cooperation between the
trapped civilians.

00:21:57.540 --> 00:22:03.360
The food in the several Ikea restaurants in
SCP-3008-1 mysteriously replenishes while

00:22:03.360 --> 00:22:05.940
nobody is there, so there’s no threat of
starving.

00:22:05.940 --> 00:22:10.680
And the automatic turning on and off of the
lights forms a kind of rudimentary day and

00:22:10.680 --> 00:22:11.100
night cycle.

00:22:11.100 --> 00:22:17.040
Night time, however, is when things get dangerous,
as the SCP-3008-2 entities – which are known

00:22:17.040 --> 00:22:21.300
to the people inside as “The Staff” – become
extremely hostile after dark.

00:22:21.300 --> 00:22:24.120
Aggressive hordes of the&nbsp;
Staff swarm the settlements&nbsp;

00:22:24.120 --> 00:22:26.220
at night, repeating “The store is now closed,

00:22:26.220 --> 00:22:27.240
please exit the building.”

00:22:27.240 --> 00:22:31.860
The civilians inside are usually able to repel
these attacks with minimal casualties, but

00:22:31.860 --> 00:22:34.560
the constant war of attrition slowly wears
down those inside.

00:22:34.560 --> 00:22:38.940
The bodies of the creatures also need to be
removed from the area after each attack, as

00:22:38.940 --> 00:22:43.020
the presence of corpses or even parts of corpses
has been known to heighten the ferocity of

00:22:43.020 --> 00:22:43.860
the next night’s attack.

00:22:43.860 --> 00:22:48.600
During the day, the Staff return to a docile
and unresponsive state, though they’ll still

00:22:48.600 --> 00:22:51.120
defend themselves violently if anyone dares
to attack.

00:22:51.120 --> 00:22:55.320
Over the course of the interviews with the
fourteen escapees, Foundation Researchers

00:22:55.320 --> 00:22:57.420
were able to answer another&nbsp;
of their key questions:&nbsp;

00:22:57.420 --> 00:23:00.120
How had so many people gone missing in the

00:23:00.120 --> 00:23:02.640
store for so long without being noticed?

00:23:02.640 --> 00:23:06.180
But the answer they received only raised many
more unsettling queries.

00:23:06.180 --> 00:23:10.380
According to the escapees, there were people
inside the settlements that, despite being

00:23:10.380 --> 00:23:15.420
otherwise of entirely sound mind and standard
intelligence, seemed to lack very common knowledge

00:23:15.420 --> 00:23:16.740
that even a child should know.

00:23:16.740 --> 00:23:19.260
For example, some weren’t&nbsp;
aware of the International&nbsp;

00:23:19.260 --> 00:23:21.720
Space Station orbiting the earth, or stranger

00:23:21.720 --> 00:23:24.060
still, the existence of the Statue of Liberty.

00:23:24.060 --> 00:23:30.000
This led the Researchers to a frightening
conclusion: SCP-3008-1 may not only be a nexus

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:35.040
point of multiple Ikea stores in our dimension,
it could be connected to Ikeas in every dimension

00:23:35.040 --> 00:23:36.240
where Ikeas exist.

00:23:36.240 --> 00:23:40.140
While it only abducts a handful of people
from each store over an extended period of

00:23:40.140 --> 00:23:44.940
time, it suddenly becomes clear how this SCP
was able to trap so many people without detection

00:23:44.940 --> 00:23:46.680
over such a long period of time.

00:23:46.680 --> 00:23:52.140
Which, in turn, led to an even more terrifying
revelation: The SCP Foundation may not have

00:23:52.140 --> 00:23:55.680
SCP-3008-1 as contained as they thought.

00:23:55.680 --> 00:24:00.840
It might even be tucked away in an Ikea somewhere
near you, just waiting for you to visit.

00:24:00.840 --> 00:24:03.540
After all, there’s always room for one more…

00:24:04.080 --> 00:24:07.200
When an anomaly is first detected by an SCP&nbsp;

00:24:07.200 --> 00:24:09.960
Foundation Field Agent,&nbsp;
it’s up to the Foundation’s

00:24:09.960 --> 00:24:15.120
Mobile Task Forces to tag and bag the impossible
entities before they can do any more harm.

00:24:15.120 --> 00:24:21.840
Sometimes these retrievals are uneventful,
other times... not so much - especially when

00:24:21.840 --> 00:24:29.160
they’re dealing with brutal forces of nature
like SCP - 096, also known as, The Shy Guy.

00:24:29.160 --> 00:24:34.860
A creature that, from its very first interaction
with the Foundation, had a reputation for

00:24:34.860 --> 00:24:37.440
being dangerous and needed to be feared.

00:24:37.440 --> 00:24:42.300
A series of vague sightings and mysterious
disappearances up in the frosty mountains

00:24:42.300 --> 00:24:46.440
of the Yukon first sparked the Foundation’s
interest. When they were certain that they

00:24:46.440 --> 00:24:53.100
had an anomaly on their hands, two retrieval
teams - Zulu 9-A and Zulu 9-B - were dispatched

00:24:53.100 --> 00:24:58.380
to secure and contain the entity. Zulu 9-A
took the lead in a heavy duty chopper, equipped

00:24:58.380 --> 00:25:05.280
with .50 caliber GAU-19 Heavy Machine-Guns
and carrying an AT-4 Anti-Tank launcher. They

00:25:05.280 --> 00:25:11.160
were prepared for anything - or so they thought
- as they established a visual on SCP - 096

00:25:11.160 --> 00:25:12.960
while two clicks away from the target.

00:25:12.960 --> 00:25:17.460
They couldn’t get a clear line of sight
on the creature, but it appeared to be stationary,

00:25:17.460 --> 00:25:23.220
docile, and was making no attempt to flee.
Piece of cake, right? Little did they know

00:25:23.220 --> 00:25:29.460
that SCP - 096 was just looking away from
them. If it was facing towards them, it’d

00:25:29.460 --> 00:25:33.540
be a whole different horror story, as Zulu
9-A were about to find out.

00:25:33.540 --> 00:25:37.980
The team landed their helicopter next to the
creature and were shocked to see that it was

00:25:37.980 --> 00:25:42.600
completely naked, in spite of the subzero
temperatures all around them. The creature

00:25:42.600 --> 00:25:47.400
was unnaturally thin, as though it’d been
starved for weeks, with bone-white skin and

00:25:47.400 --> 00:25:51.720
unnaturally long limbs. The team guessed that
the creature’s arms must have been at least

00:25:51.720 --> 00:25:57.180
1.5 metres long, but its docile nature and
insubstantial body mass gave the impression

00:25:57.180 --> 00:26:02.280
that it wouldn’t prove too difficult to
contain. That is, until they saw its face.

00:26:02.280 --> 00:26:07.140
Zulu 9-A’s Captain was the lone survivor
of the incident, as he was lucky enough to

00:26:07.140 --> 00:26:11.940
be looking away when the creature turned towards
his team. The rest of the squad ended up staring

00:26:11.940 --> 00:26:18.600
eye to eye with SCP - 096, and from that moment
on it wasn’t docile anymore. The creature

00:26:18.600 --> 00:26:22.200
began to whimper, then cry,&nbsp;
then sob uncontrollably&nbsp;

00:26:22.200 --> 00:26:25.380
in a way that sounded eerily human. This sudden

00:26:25.380 --> 00:26:29.580
change in temperament startled the rest of
Zulu 9-A and they opened fire on the creature.

00:26:29.580 --> 00:26:35.580
Under the hail of gunfire, SCP - 096 entered
a murderous frenzy and began tearing into

00:26:35.580 --> 00:26:40.260
the hapless squad of soldiers. While its flesh
and organs did seem to take damage as a result

00:26:40.260 --> 00:26:45.600
of the barrage of .50 caliber rounds from
the helicopter mounted machine guns, its skeletal

00:26:45.600 --> 00:26:50.760
structure remained intact and it continued
its onslaught, tearing the team limb from

00:26:50.760 --> 00:26:54.360
limb even after they’d blown practically
all the flesh from the creature.

00:26:54.360 --> 00:27:00.120
The AT-4 Anti-Tank launcher proved equally
ineffective at stopping SCP - 096 while it

00:27:00.120 --> 00:27:05.160
was in attack mode, and it was only after
slaughtering the entire team that it returned

00:27:05.160 --> 00:27:09.900
to its docile state. Nobody knows exactly
what the creature did to Zulu 9-A after the

00:27:09.900 --> 00:27:13.560
gunfire started, but no trace of the team
was left behind.

00:27:14.400 --> 00:27:19.020
Zulu 9-B touched down soon after, and with
a grave warning from the Captain not to look

00:27:19.020 --> 00:27:23.957
at the creature’s face, they were finally
able to subdue it. A bag was placed over SCP

00:27:23.957 --> 00:27:28.740
- 096’s face, which seemed to soothe it
enough to move it to a nearby Foundation facility.

00:27:28.740 --> 00:27:34.260
Little did they know, they’d just obtained
one of the deadliest SCPs of all time, and

00:27:34.260 --> 00:27:38.280
while it may have been under lock and key
for now, it seems inevitable that it would

00:27:38.280 --> 00:27:40.620
get out and cause more violence and chaos.

00:27:40.620 --> 00:27:45.420
Research and containment procedures for the
SCP - 096 were put under the command of Dr.

00:27:45.420 --> 00:27:50.340
Dan, a senior researcher at the site. It was
his job to find out exactly what this being

00:27:50.340 --> 00:27:55.380
was capable of, and the more he tested, the
more he realized that they were dealing with

00:27:55.380 --> 00:27:57.120
something truly terrifying.

00:27:57.120 --> 00:28:01.740
Disposable D-Class personnel were used to
figure out exactly what it was that caused

00:28:01.740 --> 00:28:06.240
the creature to enter its attack mode. Just
as it had during the initial retrieval mission,

00:28:06.240 --> 00:28:12.600
SCP - 096 went berserk when any of the attending
personnel saw its face. In this stage, it

00:28:12.600 --> 00:28:15.180
would enter a period of&nbsp;
considerable and unstoppable&nbsp;

00:28:15.180 --> 00:28:18.060
distress for one to two minutes - covering

00:28:18.060 --> 00:28:22.980
its face and wailing loudly. When the period
of distress ended, the creature would mercilessly

00:28:22.980 --> 00:28:28.440
slaughter every D-Class that had seen its
face, and just like with Zulu 9-A, no trace

00:28:28.440 --> 00:28:30.540
of their bodies would be left behind.

00:28:31.200 --> 00:28:36.000
Dr. Dan was horrified and intrigued by this
phenomenon. The creature killed anyone that

00:28:36.000 --> 00:28:40.260
saw its face directly, but could the same
be said for indirect depictions of the creature’s

00:28:40.260 --> 00:28:45.360
face - such as images and videos? Dr. Dan
was desperate to find out.

00:28:45.360 --> 00:28:50.700
More D-Class personnel were brought in to
test this, to frightening results. Dr. Dan

00:28:50.700 --> 00:28:55.140
found that the creature did indeed still enter
attack mode when people saw pictures and videos

00:28:55.140 --> 00:29:00.420
of SCP - 096’s face. The creature seemed
to have an innate sense of when people were

00:29:00.420 --> 00:29:04.860
viewing these representations even when it
should have had no conceivable way of knowing.

00:29:04.860 --> 00:29:09.120
It didn’t matter how far away or how many
barriers were in place between the viewer

00:29:09.120 --> 00:29:14.400
and the creature, the attack mode would still
activate. And once it did, it seemed as though

00:29:14.400 --> 00:29:18.480
nothing could stop the creature from hunting
down the one who saw its face.

00:29:18.480 --> 00:29:23.160
With all of this new data, special containment
procedures were devised to keep the creature

00:29:23.160 --> 00:29:30.300
safely under lock and key. Its cell was a
5 m x 5 m x 5 m airtight steel cube, fitted

00:29:30.300 --> 00:29:36.270
with advanced pressure sensors and laser detectors
to ensure that SCP - 096 remained in its cell

00:29:36.270 --> 00:29:41.040
without risking anyone having visual contact
with the creature’s face. All cameras and

00:29:41.040 --> 00:29:45.120
video equipment were strictly forbidden, and
weekly checks for any cracks or holes in the

00:29:45.120 --> 00:29:49.980
containment cell were mandatory. Of course,
none of this would stop the creature if anyone

00:29:49.980 --> 00:29:55.140
somehow saw its face. In order to solve that
little problem, Dr. Dan would need to continue

00:29:55.140 --> 00:29:56.280
his research.

00:29:57.180 --> 00:30:01.800
To find a method of subverting the creature’s
deadly glance, they needed to know exactly

00:30:01.800 --> 00:30:06.900
what they were dealing with - but how could
they, when even a glance at a photo or video

00:30:06.900 --> 00:30:12.540
of the being meant certain death? A potential
solution was proposed - creating an artistic

00:30:12.540 --> 00:30:17.040
representation of the creature’s face, something
that hadn’t yet been attempted. But how

00:30:17.040 --> 00:30:21.720
would they achieve such a feat? Simple - they’d
procure a D-Class prisoner with some artistic

00:30:21.720 --> 00:30:26.040
talent, and they found one who had been a
tattoo artist before becoming a Foundation

00:30:26.040 --> 00:30:26.640
guinea pig.

00:30:26.640 --> 00:30:32.760
Dr. Dan formulated an ingenious plan for keeping
this D-Class alive for long enough to accurately

00:30:32.760 --> 00:30:39.000
draw an image of SCP - 096’s face: He would
be placed in a Bathysphere diving bell several

00:30:39.000 --> 00:30:43.920
kilometers underwater, and tens of kilometers
away from the containment cell where the SCP

00:30:43.920 --> 00:30:48.000
was being held. The D-Class was made to look
at a photograph of the creature’s face,

00:30:48.000 --> 00:30:50.340
and then replicate that image in a pencil&nbsp;

00:30:50.340 --> 00:30:53.400
sketch. Dr. Dan first&nbsp;
confirmed that the creature’s

00:30:53.400 --> 00:30:58.140
attack mode is only activated by the creature’s
face by having the D-Class look at a series

00:30:58.140 --> 00:31:03.840
of photos of the SCP’s body parts one by
one, finally finishing with its face. The

00:31:03.840 --> 00:31:08.340
D-Class began drawing and even remarked on
how creepy the SCP’s facial features were,

00:31:08.340 --> 00:31:10.800
despite not knowing the deadly context.

00:31:10.800 --> 00:31:17.460
Meanwhile, back in its containment cell SCP
- 096 sensed someone viewing its face, and

00:31:17.460 --> 00:31:22.080
entered its inconsolable crying state followed
by its attack mode. It broke out of containment

00:31:22.080 --> 00:31:27.000
easily, and began making a beeline for the
D-Class, traversing the miles between it and

00:31:27.000 --> 00:31:31.260
its prey. The D-Class didn’t know it as
he locked the finished drawing into a separate,

00:31:31.260 --> 00:31:36.300
autonomous submersible, but he was already
dead. As the drawing made its way up to a

00:31:36.300 --> 00:31:41.700
researcher on the surface, SCP - 096 dived
into the water, and started swimming down

00:31:41.700 --> 00:31:48.180
towards the artist. Minutes later, the bathysphere
was breached, and the D-Class was torn to

00:31:48.180 --> 00:31:48.420
shreds.

00:31:48.420 --> 00:31:55.500
SCP - 096 was recaptured without issue by
surface recovery team Foxtrot-303-A, and further

00:31:55.500 --> 00:32:00.300
testing on the drawing showed that artistic
representations of SCP - 096’s face were

00:32:00.300 --> 00:32:04.920
in fact harmless. From this experience, we
now know that the creature has a gaunt face

00:32:04.920 --> 00:32:07.680
with totally white eyes, possibly indicating&nbsp;

00:32:07.680 --> 00:32:10.740
blindness, and a grossly&nbsp;
extended jaw. Nevertheless,

00:32:10.740 --> 00:32:16.440
Dr. Dan was adamant that SCP - 096 was too
dangerous to be left alive, and requested

00:32:16.440 --> 00:32:20.580
permission from the upper echelons of the
Foundation to terminate the creature by any

00:32:20.580 --> 00:32:25.920
means necessary. However, the doctor’s request
would fall on deaf ears, until...

00:32:25.920 --> 00:32:29.332
It all started with a seemingly innocent image.
(Use this image:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:32:29.332 --> 00:32:29.400
http://scp-wiki.wdfiles.com/local--files/incident-096-1-a/G9zmJ.jpg)

00:32:29.400 --> 00:32:34.320
While it’s now been redacted for your safety,
the black spec inside the yellow circle was

00:32:34.320 --> 00:32:40.740
once a minuscule image of SCP - 096, taken
unknowingly in the 1990s by a semi-professional

00:32:40.740 --> 00:32:44.820
mountaineer. One day, they were looking at
old photographs when his eyes passed over

00:32:44.820 --> 00:32:51.420
the tiny spec without even noticing he had
seen anything. But SCP - 096 noticed, and

00:32:51.420 --> 00:32:53.100
began entering its attack mode.

00:32:53.100 --> 00:32:57.420
It tore through its steel containment unit
like tissue paper, causing the release of

00:32:57.420 --> 00:33:01.680
a nerve agent that killed a number of attending
Foundation staff. The monster then fled the

00:33:01.680 --> 00:33:07.080
base and began pursuing its prey, with Mobile
Task Force Tau-1 in hot pursuit. Dr. Oleksei,

00:33:07.080 --> 00:33:11.340
who was helping to manage the site where the
SCP was contained, was in dismay over the

00:33:11.340 --> 00:33:15.480
situation. Dr. Dan was out of the country
at the time, trying to discover more about

00:33:15.480 --> 00:33:19.920
the creature’s origins. However, he did
leave the Mobile Task Force with a new secret

00:33:19.920 --> 00:33:23.400
weapon against the rampaging Shy Guy… Project
SCRAMBLE.

00:33:23.400 --> 00:33:28.290
SCRAMBLE were state of the art goggles featuring
a new technology created by Dr. Dan, which

00:33:28.290 --> 00:33:33.660
- using artistic renditions of 096’s facial
features - could detect and scramble the features

00:33:33.660 --> 00:33:39.720
of SCP - 096 into an unrecognizable form,
preventing the normally deadly effect of gazing

00:33:39.720 --> 00:33:46.320
upon on its face. In theory, this would allow
MTF Tau-1 to engage safely with 096 once its

00:33:46.320 --> 00:33:51.120
prey had been eliminated and bring it back
into containment. But disaster struck on two

00:33:51.120 --> 00:33:56.280
fronts. First, the prey in question was located
in a population center, creating the potential

00:33:56.280 --> 00:33:57.660
for a huge loss of life.

00:33:57.660 --> 00:34:02.520
And the second bigger problem was that the
SCRAMBLE technology didn’t work, as stray

00:34:02.520 --> 00:34:06.300
pixels of the creature’s face would reach
the eyes of the task force before the internal

00:34:06.300 --> 00:34:10.740
microprocessor had time to scramble them.
The mission turned into a death sentence,

00:34:10.740 --> 00:34:16.500
as SCP - 096 slaughtered almost the entire
task force, as well as a number of civilians

00:34:16.500 --> 00:34:22.500
in town - including an infant and its entire
family. It was a monumental disaster, made

00:34:22.500 --> 00:34:27.600
even worse by a final revelation: Dr. Dan
and Dr. Oleksei had themselves facilitated

00:34:27.600 --> 00:34:32.400
the entire containment breach and allowed
the resulting massacre to happen, with Dr.

00:34:32.400 --> 00:34:36.840
Dan hoping it would be enough motivation for
Foundation Command to green-light his research

00:34:36.840 --> 00:34:38.460
into destroying the creature.

00:34:38.460 --> 00:34:43.200
Anything that would give him the opportunity
to kill this thing would be worth the bloodshed.

00:34:43.200 --> 00:34:48.840
His plan worked and the SCP Foundation saw
it his way, approving his request to neutralize

00:34:48.840 --> 00:34:56.220
SCP - 096. However, success comes at a cost
for Dr. Dan. Once he figures out a way to

00:34:56.220 --> 00:35:01.140
finally kill the creature, though done in
the line of duty, he himself will be terminated

00:35:01.140 --> 00:35:03.660
by the Foundation for his crimes against humanity.

00:35:03.660 --> 00:35:09.420
But considering how much damage SCP - 096
is capable of causing if it ever got to a

00:35:09.420 --> 00:35:14.580
major population center, or - even worse - was
ever caught on camera and broadcast to a worldwide

00:35:14.580 --> 00:35:20.220
audience, the doctor himself would likely
deem his own death a justifiable cost. To

00:35:20.220 --> 00:35:24.240
this day, the Foundation is researching ways
to kill the creature, and they’re still

00:35:24.240 --> 00:35:29.280
looking for their silver bullet. And the pressure
is on. They hadn’t known about the seemingly

00:35:29.280 --> 00:35:34.380
innocent picture that sparked the last containment
breach. The one taken decades ago, in which

00:35:34.380 --> 00:35:40.320
the Shy Guy had only occupied four tiny pixels.
Four tiny pixels that resulted in multiple

00:35:40.320 --> 00:35:41.520
innocent lives lost.

00:35:41.520 --> 00:35:47.400
So be careful where you look because who knows
how many other photos of the creature are

00:35:47.400 --> 00:35:52.380
lurking out there, photos with an innocent
dot in the background. Your eyes glance over

00:35:52.380 --> 00:35:58.020
it, not even noticing the little blip, until
you hear a distant wailing that seems to be

00:35:58.020 --> 00:36:05.280
getting closer, and closer, and closer. And
then... it’s already too late.

00:36:05.280 --> 00:36:09.300
“SCP-682 must be destroyed as soon as possible.”

00:36:09.960 --> 00:36:16.920
So begins the SCP Foundation file on the dreaded
SCP - 682, a highly-intelligent reptilian

00:36:16.920 --> 00:36:22.020
monster that has - despite the Foundation’s
best efforts - proved impossible to kill.

00:36:22.020 --> 00:36:27.060
It may not be the most dangerous SCP out there,
considering that some are capable of eliminating

00:36:27.060 --> 00:36:31.620
entire realities, but it’s one of the most
iconic, and you’ve probably heard tales

00:36:31.620 --> 00:36:36.480
of the monster that death forgot, and you
know exactly why everyone is so afraid of

00:36:36.480 --> 00:36:38.760
the so-called “Hard to Kill Reptile”.

00:36:38.760 --> 00:36:42.660
It’s been subjected to some of the most
deadly weapons and traps the Foundation could

00:36:42.660 --> 00:36:46.980
devise, and survived attacks from some of
its deadliest fellow SCPs.

00:36:46.980 --> 00:36:51.180
But before we tell you about the Foundation’s
many failed assassination attempts against

00:36:51.180 --> 00:36:56.100
the so-called “Hard to Kill Reptile”,
we need a little more groundwork on what this

00:36:56.100 --> 00:36:57.180
creature even is.

00:36:57.180 --> 00:37:02.640
The first thing to know about SCP - 682, is
that this thing wants you and everyone you

00:37:02.640 --> 00:37:03.540
know dead.

00:37:04.200 --> 00:37:10.560
Unlike some other creatures like SCP - 096
and SCP - 173, which are murderous but exhibit

00:37:10.560 --> 00:37:16.860
no real higher processing skills, SCP - 682
possesses cunning, advanced reasoning, and

00:37:16.860 --> 00:37:18.900
even human-level logical intelligence.

00:37:18.900 --> 00:37:24.480
SCP - 682 can engage you in conversation,
but just talking to the creature calmly and

00:37:24.480 --> 00:37:28.920
cordially will sometimes cause it to enter
its “rage state” where it becomes even

00:37:28.920 --> 00:37:30.360
more dangerous and volatile.

00:37:30.360 --> 00:37:35.460
The beast is perpetually kept in a huge tank
of powerful hydrochloric acid, melting its

00:37:35.460 --> 00:37:39.300
tissue to prevent it from reaching its full
potential and going on a rampage.

00:37:39.300 --> 00:37:44.280
The creature’s most terrifying asset, and
the reason it’s proven impossible to terminate

00:37:44.280 --> 00:37:49.380
thus far, is its incredible adaptability to
any and all external stimuli.

00:37:49.380 --> 00:37:55.680
682 is a reactive being, capable of not only
surviving and regenerating from all attacks,

00:37:55.680 --> 00:37:59.940
but often incorporating those attacks into
its own wide arsenal.

00:37:59.940 --> 00:38:03.900
In other words, if you’re hoping to kill
this thing, you better kill it on the first

00:38:03.900 --> 00:38:09.720
hit - cause if you don’t, you better believe
it’s gonna hit you back a hundred times

00:38:09.720 --> 00:38:10.320
harder.

00:38:10.980 --> 00:38:15.960
This brings us to the main event: Some of
the SCP Foundation’s most ambitious and

00:38:15.960 --> 00:38:21.540
frightening attempts to terminate SCP - 682,
or even understand how it could theoretically

00:38:21.540 --> 00:38:22.260
be terminated.

00:38:22.260 --> 00:38:27.180
There are quite literally too many unsuccessful
attempts for us to list them all here, so

00:38:27.180 --> 00:38:29.460
think of this as a highlight&nbsp;
reel of the Foundation’s&nbsp;

00:38:29.460 --> 00:38:30.780
most prominent failures.

00:38:30.780 --> 00:38:36.960
682 was first cross-tested with SCP - 017,
a humanoid shadow-entity shown to be able

00:38:36.960 --> 00:38:40.500
to consume matter with its shadows and leave
no traces behind.

00:38:40.500 --> 00:38:47.100
Tests on tissue samples from 682 showed that
SCP - 017 was able to consume said tissues

00:38:47.100 --> 00:38:48.420
with no adverse effects.

00:38:48.420 --> 00:38:54.420
However, when SCP - 017 was placed into the
containment chamber with the actual creature,

00:38:54.420 --> 00:38:59.580
682 let out a horrific roar that was so loud
it damaged nearby audio equipment.

00:38:59.580 --> 00:39:06.060
SCP - 017 fled to the corner of the room,
and 682, in its rage state, attempted to breach

00:39:06.060 --> 00:39:06.720
containment.

00:39:06.720 --> 00:39:11.820
Agents managed to suppress and remove the
creature, but no meaningful damage was logged.

00:39:11.820 --> 00:39:13.260
Attempt failed.

00:39:13.260 --> 00:39:19.080
SCP - 173 - the Killer statue - was later
brought in, hoping that its thus-far impeccable

00:39:19.080 --> 00:39:21.120
track recording for killing would hold strong.

00:39:21.120 --> 00:39:26.640
The second that 173 was introduced into the
testing area, 682 retreated to the far wall

00:39:26.640 --> 00:39:28.380
and began screeching intensely.

00:39:28.380 --> 00:39:31.140
It was intelligent enough to know what it
was dealing with here.

00:39:31.140 --> 00:39:35.640
While the researchers and guards expected
an instantaneous reaction, there was actually

00:39:35.640 --> 00:39:41.340
a stalemate for over six hours as 682 stared
at 173 continuously.

00:39:41.340 --> 00:39:46.380
Eventually, the tie was broken when Agents
shot out 682’s eyes with high-caliber sniper

00:39:46.380 --> 00:39:49.920
rifles, breaking the line of sight and causing
173 to attack.

00:39:49.920 --> 00:39:55.080
Though 682 sustained damage to several parts
of its body while its eyes regenerated, the

00:39:55.080 --> 00:39:56.280
creature was not killed.

00:39:56.280 --> 00:40:01.560
It then regenerated a number of eyes all over
its body, covered in a clear, armoured carapace

00:40:01.560 --> 00:40:03.540
that made them resistant to bullets.

00:40:03.540 --> 00:40:08.880
The stalemate continued for an additional
twelve hours, as 682 maintained perpetual

00:40:08.880 --> 00:40:09.360
eye contact.

00:40:09.360 --> 00:40:13.980
173 was eventually removed from the containment
unit, and the mission was aborted.

00:40:13.980 --> 00:40:15.420
Attempt failed.

00:40:15.420 --> 00:40:21.120
In their desperation, the SCP Foundation resorted
to bringing in another dangerous and seemingly

00:40:21.120 --> 00:40:28.320
unkillable monster to take on 682: SCP - 096,
also known as The Shy Guy.

00:40:28.320 --> 00:40:34.380
As astute SCP fans will already know, this
being kills anything that sees its face, with

00:40:34.380 --> 00:40:39.420
no known exceptions - and when it enters its
attack mode, it’s thought to be quite literally

00:40:39.420 --> 00:40:40.800
unstoppable.

00:40:40.800 --> 00:40:43.680
Or, at least, it was.

00:40:43.680 --> 00:40:50.280
While SCP - 096 was able to destroy 85% of
682’s original body mass during their 27

00:40:50.280 --> 00:40:54.720
hour battle, it was left&nbsp;
mentally broken - wounded,&nbsp;

00:40:54.720 --> 00:40:56.100
and huddled in the corner.

00:40:56.100 --> 00:41:02.220
To this day, if ever confronted with SCP 682,
the Shy Guy reacts in pure terror, turning

00:41:02.220 --> 00:41:03.960
away and clawing at his own face.

00:41:03.960 --> 00:41:06.060
Attempt failed.

00:41:06.720 --> 00:41:12.300
During a deadly containment breach, SCP - 682
also went head to head organically with another

00:41:12.300 --> 00:41:18.240
iconic SCP hall-of-famer: SCP - 106, also
known as The Old Man.

00:41:18.240 --> 00:41:25.020
The Old Man and a shapeshifting, psionic anomaly
known as SCP - 953 broke into 682’s containment

00:41:25.020 --> 00:41:25.320
cell.

00:41:25.320 --> 00:41:30.000
The Old Man pulled both of his fellow anomalous
combatants into his pocket dimension to continue

00:41:30.000 --> 00:41:31.380
the battle on his terms.

00:41:31.380 --> 00:41:36.780
However, despite losing 67% of his body mass
during the ensuing pocket dimension showdown,

00:41:36.780 --> 00:41:43.560
682 still prevailed - with the Old Man eventually
fleeing back to his cell, and 953 being collected

00:41:43.560 --> 00:41:44.880
and taken away by agents.

00:41:44.880 --> 00:41:49.020
Once again, SCP - 682 continued to hold the
title.

00:41:49.020 --> 00:41:52.860
But it wasn’t just cross-testing experiments,
intentional or otherwise.

00:41:52.860 --> 00:41:58.440
The SCP Foundation’s quest to kill 682 lead
them to a number of more conventional murder

00:41:58.440 --> 00:42:01.200
methods, all with varying degrees of success.

00:42:01.200 --> 00:42:06.660
Due to SCP - 682’s highly adaptive abilities,
some methods were discounted from the outset.

00:42:07.320 --> 00:42:11.940
For example, launching a powerful thermonuclear
missile at the creature was soundly rejected

00:42:11.940 --> 00:42:16.200
by O5 Command - on the premise that, if the
creature wasn’t destroyed and evolved to

00:42:16.200 --> 00:42:20.640
the point where it could shrug off nukes,
humanity would be pretty much done for.

00:42:20.640 --> 00:42:24.900
Other ideas were abandoned just for being
too ridiculous - such as one researcher’s

00:42:24.900 --> 00:42:28.200
suggestion to fly the creature through the
air and drop it from a considerable height,

00:42:28.200 --> 00:42:30.600
hoping to kill it with the high-altitude impact.

00:42:30.600 --> 00:42:33.660
I’m not sure we even need to tell you why
that’s a terrible idea.

00:42:33.660 --> 00:42:39.540
But, during the experiments on SCP - 682,
the studies ranged from honest to incompetent

00:42:39.540 --> 00:42:41.100
to straight-up evil.

00:42:41.940 --> 00:42:46.560
One guest researcher fed two small, innocent
children to the creature, just to see what

00:42:46.560 --> 00:42:46.920
would happen.

00:42:46.920 --> 00:42:51.240
He was then himself fed to the creature for
his sadistic behaviour, which was viewed as

00:42:51.240 --> 00:42:53.220
getting in the way of his professional conduct.

00:42:53.220 --> 00:42:57.060
After all, the Foundation is meant to be cold,
not cruel.

00:42:57.060 --> 00:43:01.260
It was SCP - 682 that had the monopoly on
cruelty.

00:43:01.260 --> 00:43:03.360
Memetic Kill agents were a resounding failure.

00:43:03.360 --> 00:43:06.120
They attempted to dismember 682 with a powerful&nbsp;

00:43:06.120 --> 00:43:08.460
laser, only to have the&nbsp;
creature develop reflective

00:43:08.460 --> 00:43:12.840
surfaces that displaced the beam and caused
catastrophic damage to the area around it.

00:43:12.840 --> 00:43:17.040
They attempted to kill the creature by sucking
all the air out of its containment facility

00:43:17.040 --> 00:43:22.500
and creating a vacuum, but it expelled a dangerous
gaseous compound that reacted violently and

00:43:22.500 --> 00:43:25.320
exploded when air was once again introduced
into the room.

00:43:25.320 --> 00:43:31.680
The Foundation used high-precision blades
to slice SCP - 682 into approximately 12,000

00:43:31.680 --> 00:43:33.840
pieces then separated these pieces.

00:43:33.840 --> 00:43:37.380
Unsurprisingly by this point, this attempt
also failed.

00:43:37.380 --> 00:43:41.940
The 12,000 pieces reformed a short while later
into the fully operational killing machine

00:43:41.940 --> 00:43:43.500
we all know and fear.

00:43:43.500 --> 00:43:48.120
In one particularly frightening display of
intelligence and adaptability, the Foundation

00:43:48.120 --> 00:43:52.860
attempted to kill 682 with extreme heat, but
it shielded itself by developing a secondary

00:43:52.860 --> 00:43:55.260
carapace composed of solid helium.

00:43:55.260 --> 00:43:58.800
When personnel entered the room following
the failed attempt on the creature’s life,

00:43:58.800 --> 00:44:04.080
it shattered its helium carapace into deadly
shards that fired around the room and shredded

00:44:04.080 --> 00:44:06.300
all Foundation personnel in attendance.

00:44:06.300 --> 00:44:10.620
It’d set a trap, and that trap had been
wildly successful.

00:44:10.620 --> 00:44:15.360
The creature’s ability to adapt to seemingly
any offensive is unparalleled, to the point

00:44:15.360 --> 00:44:20.100
where Foundation staff have no idea how to
classify this creature - whether it’s organic,

00:44:20.100 --> 00:44:24.360
inorganic, or even alive at all based on any
definitions we could understand.

00:44:25.320 --> 00:44:28.080
At every turn, the creature just raised more
questions.

00:44:28.080 --> 00:44:29.220
What is it?

00:44:29.220 --> 00:44:32.040
Is it possible to destroy it at all by any
means?

00:44:32.040 --> 00:44:34.080
Who was even trying to kill who here?

00:44:34.080 --> 00:44:39.540
Because it certainly seemed like SCP - 682
had a masterful K/D ratio by now.

00:44:39.540 --> 00:44:44.040
More extreme feats of cross-testing continued
in the Foundation’s growing desperation

00:44:44.040 --> 00:44:45.480
to eliminate this monster.

00:44:45.480 --> 00:44:51.540
SCP - 162, which is a hypnotic ball of sharp
objects, hooks, and high-tension fishing line,

00:44:51.540 --> 00:44:54.120
was introduced to 682’s containment cell.

00:44:54.120 --> 00:44:58.860
The hooks latched onto the creature and tore
huge portions off, including its entire lower

00:44:58.860 --> 00:45:00.480
jaw and one of its limbs.

00:45:00.480 --> 00:45:07.260
However, 682 was still able to breach containment,
kill eleven people, and badly wound 86 others.

00:45:07.260 --> 00:45:10.440
It regenerated its severe injuries in no time.

00:45:10.440 --> 00:45:15.000
The beast was even taken to the domain of
The Gate Guardian, one of the proposals for

00:45:15.000 --> 00:45:16.380
SCP - 001.

00:45:16.380 --> 00:45:21.420
The Guardian has a flaming sword hotter than
the sun, capable of destroying its targets

00:45:21.420 --> 00:45:22.620
on an atomic level.

00:45:23.220 --> 00:45:27.060
Naturally, SCP - 682 survived and regenerated.

00:45:27.060 --> 00:45:34.680
Perhaps the most fascinating cross-test of
all was between 682 and SCP - 053, who manifests

00:45:34.680 --> 00:45:37.440
as a kind, innocent little&nbsp;
girl with the unfortunate&nbsp;

00:45:37.440 --> 00:45:39.480
condition of causing homicidal tendencies

00:45:39.480 --> 00:45:42.720
in all who come into contact with her for
more than ten minutes.

00:45:43.680 --> 00:45:47.340
The people with these tendencies would then
attempt to harm the girl, but would immediately

00:45:47.340 --> 00:45:50.700
drop dead shortly after, leaving the girl
intact.

00:45:50.700 --> 00:45:55.740
The researchers present anticipated two possible
outcomes here: The optimistic outcome, in

00:45:55.740 --> 00:45:59.520
which 682 entered a rage state, attacked 053,
and died for good.

00:45:59.520 --> 00:46:05.220
And the realistic outcome, in which 682 attacked
053, possibly experienced some minor injury

00:46:05.220 --> 00:46:08.820
or nothing at all, and 053 had to be removed
from the containment cell.

00:46:08.820 --> 00:46:10.440
But that didn’t happen.

00:46:10.440 --> 00:46:15.060
What did occur was considerably more shocking
than any kind of violence.

00:46:15.060 --> 00:46:21.120
When 053 entered 682’s containment chamber,
the monster became uncharacteristically docile.

00:46:21.120 --> 00:46:26.340
Researchers and staff were baffled, and watched
with amazement as 053 approached the terrifying,

00:46:26.340 --> 00:46:30.840
immortal, mass-murdering monster...and began
to play with it.

00:46:30.840 --> 00:46:34.800
682 even allowed 053 to draw on its face with
crayons.

00:46:34.800 --> 00:46:39.180
Researchers thought they must’ve been dreaming,
seeing this surreal display play out.

00:46:39.180 --> 00:46:43.140
053 even appeared to have affection for this
unkillable misanthrope.

00:46:43.140 --> 00:46:47.400
It was a single act in defiance of everything
they thought they knew.

00:46:47.400 --> 00:46:52.860
When Foundation personnel entered the containment
cell to separate the two, 682 went ballistic

00:46:52.860 --> 00:46:54.300
and killed multiple guards.

00:46:54.300 --> 00:46:58.320
053 also wept, sad at being separated from
her new friend.

00:46:58.980 --> 00:47:04.260
To this day, despite further testing, the
Foundation has no idea how or why this happened.

00:47:04.260 --> 00:47:10.680
Like many details surrounding SCP - 682, it’s
shrouded in deeply frustrating mystery.

00:47:11.520 --> 00:47:18.000
And so the tale of SCP - 682 continues, in
spite of the Foundation’s best efforts.

00:47:18.000 --> 00:47:22.800
The monster continues to breach containment
and slaughter with some regularity, taking

00:47:22.800 --> 00:47:28.620
out its seemingly limitless hatred for not
only human beings, but anything that dares

00:47:28.620 --> 00:47:29.460
draw breath.

00:47:30.000 --> 00:47:35.220
Nobody knows where exactly the creature is
from, what its true nature is, or why its

00:47:35.220 --> 00:47:39.540
ability to adapt and regenerate far exceeds
any known organism on this planet.

00:47:39.540 --> 00:47:45.060
Perhaps one day, through enough research and
cross testing, we can someday answer these

00:47:45.060 --> 00:47:52.680
questions with scientific precision, but until
then, we only have one answer: Hatred never

00:47:52.680 --> 00:47:53.160
dies.

00:47:53.700 --> 00:47:59.160
It isn’t easy to work for The SCP Foundation.&nbsp;
Not only is the job dangerous - you could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:47:59.160 --> 00:48:03.660
be eaten by a giant, immortal lizard or&nbsp;
turned into organic furniture inside the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:48:03.660 --> 00:48:08.940
world’s scariest living room - but it’s also&nbsp;
insanely complicated. How do you make sense&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:48:08.940 --> 00:48:13.320
of the nonsensical? What’s the definition&nbsp;
of strange when your career is securing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:48:13.320 --> 00:48:16.020
containing, and protecting anomalous objects&nbsp;
and entities? This brings us to SCP - 001.

00:48:16.020 --> 00:48:21.720
Rather than a single object, location, or&nbsp;
being, SCP - 001 is a cluster of over 30&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:48:21.720 --> 00:48:27.720
different proposals for potential candidates for&nbsp;
the prestigious 001 spot. Some believe there’s a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:48:27.720 --> 00:48:33.120
true 001 hidden in this group and the rest are&nbsp;
decoys, others think that these are all just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:48:33.120 --> 00:48:37.740
SCPs catalogued prior to the introduction&nbsp;
of the current classification system. Some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:48:37.740 --> 00:48:42.960
even think that all of the proposals have&nbsp;
a valid claim to the SCP - 001 throne.

00:48:42.960 --> 00:48:45.840
We’re not here to make a final judgement, instead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:48:45.840 --> 00:48:52.080
we’re going to take you on a lightning-round crash&nbsp;
course through 31 of the SCP - 001 proposals. If&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:48:52.080 --> 00:48:56.340
you’d like a more in-depth take on any of&nbsp;
these SCPs, let us know in the comments,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:48:56.340 --> 00:49:00.420
but for now, there’s no more time to&nbsp;
waste. After all, we’ve got a lot to cover.

00:49:00.420 --> 00:49:01.440
Let’s go.

00:49:01.440 --> 00:49:07.020
Number 31: The Sheaf of Papers. This seemingly&nbsp;
innocent stack of paper is actually one of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:49:07.020 --> 00:49:11.280
most mysterious and feared items under&nbsp;
the Foundation’s lock and key. While&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:49:11.280 --> 00:49:14.940
it appears to be a simple confidential&nbsp;
report, every time the papers are read,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:49:14.940 --> 00:49:20.640
it details the appearance of a new SCP that will&nbsp;
inevitably be discovered soon after. The question&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:49:20.640 --> 00:49:25.320
is whether the sheaf of papers is warning us&nbsp;
about these entities, or creating them itself.

00:49:25.320 --> 00:49:30.900
Number 30: The Prototype. This account details&nbsp;
the capture of an incredibly strange cycloptic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:49:30.900 --> 00:49:35.460
creature that emits massive amounts of&nbsp;
radiation and can create microsingularities.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:49:35.460 --> 00:49:40.500
The writing of this creature’s file is so basic,&nbsp;
unformatted, and unredacted that it’s clear that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:49:40.500 --> 00:49:44.640
the being was one of the earlier creatures&nbsp;
secured by the organization. Interestingly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:49:44.640 --> 00:49:48.300
it was during the capture of this&nbsp;
creature that Dr. Keter was killed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:49:48.300 --> 00:49:51.780
inspiring the creation of the&nbsp;
infamous Keter Class in his honor.

00:49:51.780 --> 00:49:57.780
Number 29: The Gate Guardian. This huge,&nbsp;
multi-winged, sword-wielding Biblical energy-being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:49:57.780 --> 00:50:03.120
may have been the impetus for the founding of the&nbsp;
SCP Foundation. This being remains largely static,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:50:03.120 --> 00:50:07.020
guarding the intersection of the Tigris&nbsp;
and Euphrates rivers. Its flaming sword,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:50:07.020 --> 00:50:11.400
which is believed to be as hot as the sun,&nbsp;
can cleave any aggressor out of existence at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:50:11.400 --> 00:50:15.720
the atomic level. When the Founder of the SCP&nbsp;
Foundation first encountered the Gate Guardian,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:50:15.720 --> 00:50:20.040
they heard one word echoing through their&nbsp;
mind: PREPARE. And the rest is history.

00:50:20.040 --> 00:50:24.600
Number 28: The Lock. This onyx gemstone and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:50:24.600 --> 00:50:28.560
incredibly complex lock attached to&nbsp;
it are still a mystery. To this day,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:50:28.560 --> 00:50:32.640
all attempts to open have failed. Personally,&nbsp;
we think that’s probably for the best...

00:50:32.640 --> 00:50:38.700
Number 27: The Factory. As the name suggests,&nbsp;
this SCP is literally a factory founded by a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:50:38.700 --> 00:50:43.200
pagan and a devil worshipper. While it’s believed&nbsp;
that the factory could create just about anything,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:50:43.200 --> 00:50:48.660
its specialty was creating a number of the&nbsp;
SCPs we know and fear today. Pre-Foundation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:50:48.660 --> 00:50:53.340
Forces were able to disable the factory, but&nbsp;
not without sustaining their own heavy losses.

00:50:53.340 --> 00:50:59.400
Number 26: The Spiral Path. This is a normal&nbsp;
appearing gravel pathway that, when travelled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:50:59.400 --> 00:51:04.260
clockwise, appears completely normal. However,&nbsp;
when travelled counter-clockwise, the path&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:51:04.260 --> 00:51:10.020
goes uphill forever, in defiance of all laws of&nbsp;
physics. This simple anomaly opened a Pandora’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:51:10.020 --> 00:51:14.940
box of rampant anomaly creation - leading to&nbsp;
a number of the deadly SCPs we know today.

00:51:14.940 --> 00:51:20.220
Number 25: The Legacy. This SCP is a&nbsp;
collection of seemingly random objects,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:51:20.220 --> 00:51:24.420
including a diary from a person claiming&nbsp;
to be from another reality, attempting to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:51:24.420 --> 00:51:28.500
halt a trans-dimensional corruption that&nbsp;
they themselves created. The diary claims&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:51:28.500 --> 00:51:32.100
to have a solution to this Corruption,&nbsp;
but the solution has not yet been found.

00:51:32.100 --> 00:51:38.460
Number 24: The Database. In one of the strangest&nbsp;
twists on the format, this SCP is actually the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:51:38.460 --> 00:51:43.740
various authors of the SCP Wiki, who are somehow&nbsp;
leaking top-secret information to the public.

00:51:43.740 --> 00:51:48.540
Number 23: The Foundation. This&nbsp;
SCP, first discovered by the FBI,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:51:48.540 --> 00:51:53.040
is an anomalous high school building that&nbsp;
experiences shifting internal geometry&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:51:53.040 --> 00:51:56.160
and sometimes manifests hostile humanoids within.

00:51:56.160 --> 00:52:02.460
Number 22: Thirty-Six. One of the rare benevolent&nbsp;
SCPs, the thirty-six are humans with a truly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:52:02.460 --> 00:52:07.440
remarkable ability - they can dampen or even&nbsp;
neutralize any SCP they come into contact with.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:52:07.440 --> 00:52:11.760
Though it’s implied that the thirty-six may have&nbsp;
the power to save the world, every time one of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:52:11.760 --> 00:52:16.320
them dies, a supernatural calamity occurs,&nbsp;
often leaving hundreds of innocents dead.

00:52:16.320 --> 00:52:21.540
Number 21: Keter Duty. This refers to a&nbsp;
containment facility largely filled with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:52:21.540 --> 00:52:27.180
Keter-class SCPs, whose presence around each other&nbsp;
creates a kind of mutually-assured cancellation.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:52:27.180 --> 00:52:32.100
If one of these SCPs breaches containment,&nbsp;
that’s bad news. But if all of them do,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:52:32.100 --> 00:52:35.580
it’ll produce a bubble of reality&nbsp;
distortion that will fundamentally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:52:35.580 --> 00:52:39.600
alter reality as we know it. For all we&nbsp;
know, it may have even happened already...

00:52:39.600 --> 00:52:45.420
Number 20: Ouroboros. This is a proposal that’s&nbsp;
formed of four sub-proposals. Remember what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:52:45.420 --> 00:52:50.160
we said about complicated? These sub-proposals&nbsp;
include The Children - nine anomalous kids who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:52:50.160 --> 00:52:56.100
emit radiation and have destructive potential when&nbsp;
together. The Broken God - aka Mekhane, The god of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:52:56.100 --> 00:53:01.320
metal, intelligence, and machines. Atonement - A&nbsp;
researcher turned into a humanoid singularity with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:53:01.320 --> 00:53:07.140
the power to destroy whole realities. And The Way&nbsp;
It Ends - which isn’t technically an SCP, but the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:53:07.140 --> 00:53:12.480
tales of the Chaos Insurgency’s quest to eliminate&nbsp;
all the members of the Foundation’s O5 Council.

00:53:12.480 --> 00:53:19.920
Number 19: A Record. This is an SCP File&nbsp;
slot that is itself an SCP. Whatever is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:53:19.920 --> 00:53:23.640
written in this slot becomes true, and&nbsp;
one ambitious researcher attempted to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:53:23.640 --> 00:53:26.760
use this power to make herself&nbsp;
into a kind of all-powerful God.

00:53:26.760 --> 00:53:31.260
Number 18: Past and Future. These SCPs&nbsp;
are a collection of powerful entities&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:53:31.260 --> 00:53:36.360
that despise humanity, and are apparently&nbsp;
the source of all anomalous phenomena - even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:53:36.360 --> 00:53:41.160
making already dangerous SCPs deadlier&nbsp;
than before. Much like in The Database,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:53:41.160 --> 00:53:44.280
those pesky SCP Wiki writers may&nbsp;
have something to do with this...

00:53:44.280 --> 00:53:50.280
Number 17: The Consensus. This SCP refers to&nbsp;
a reality restructuring event caused by an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:53:50.280 --> 00:53:56.280
occult war in a previous reality. That’s right&nbsp;
- this SCP already won, and we’re living in its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:53:56.280 --> 00:54:01.140
new reality. The only people who remember the&nbsp;
world as it once was are thirteen people who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:54:01.140 --> 00:54:05.820
now form the O5 council. And not all of them&nbsp;
are telling the truth about what they know...

00:54:05.820 --> 00:54:12.420
Number 16: When Day Breaks. This proposal details&nbsp;
a potentially world-ending SCP phenomenon, wherein&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:54:12.420 --> 00:54:17.220
the sun becomes hostile and begins to melt all&nbsp;
living beings into a living wax-like substance.

00:54:17.220 --> 00:54:23.160
Number 15: God’s Blind Spot. This is an&nbsp;
anomalous area referred to as Facility T,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:54:23.160 --> 00:54:28.380
in which nobody can die. This anomaly dates&nbsp;
back to the Biblical age of Moses, and is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:54:28.380 --> 00:54:32.640
believed to have originated from the literal&nbsp;
blessing of the Abrahamic God. It’s through&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:54:32.640 --> 00:54:37.320
a covenant with this God that the Foundation is&nbsp;
able to make limited use of this death free area.

00:54:37.320 --> 00:54:42.300
Number 14: Normalcy. Ever wondered what the&nbsp;
Foundation’s definition of “anomalous” is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:54:42.300 --> 00:54:46.980
exactly? It all comes from this proposal&nbsp;
- which is a document shared among the O5&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:54:46.980 --> 00:54:50.880
council that gives solid definitions to the&nbsp;
fundamental laws of reality. If something&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:54:50.880 --> 00:54:54.960
breaks these laws, that’s an anomaly, and&nbsp;
it then becomes the Foundation’s business.

00:54:54.960 --> 00:55:00.000
Number 13: The World At Large. As the&nbsp;
title suggests, this SCP is our home&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:55:00.000 --> 00:55:03.960
planet Earth and its ability to support&nbsp;
life. It’s believed that these qualities&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:55:03.960 --> 00:55:07.680
were planted on Earth in our reality&nbsp;
by another dimension’s SCP Foundation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:55:07.680 --> 00:55:12.060
hoping to continue human life after some&nbsp;
terrible calamity in its own dimension.

00:55:12.060 --> 00:55:18.300
Number 12: Dead Men. This SCP was an 84 year&nbsp;
old man whose body, when damaged and mutilated,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:55:18.300 --> 00:55:22.800
can affect the very processes of human&nbsp;
death at large. Before his own death,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:55:22.800 --> 00:55:27.900
he was used as a dangerous pawn in a civil&nbsp;
war between O5 Command and the SCP Foundation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:55:27.900 --> 00:55:31.620
Ethics Committee. Yeah, we were surprised&nbsp;
to hear they had an ethics committee too.

00:55:31.620 --> 00:55:36.660
Number 11: The World’s Gone Beautiful. This&nbsp;
SCP describes an anomalous event that will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:55:36.660 --> 00:55:40.740
take place just before the apocalypse,&nbsp;
in which flowers will grow all over the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:55:40.740 --> 00:55:45.300
world and everyone will be briefly at peace&nbsp;
before their destruction 24 hours later.

00:55:45.300 --> 00:55:50.400
Number 10: The Scarlet King. This is an&nbsp;
extremely powerful, extremely malevolent,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:55:50.400 --> 00:55:54.900
extremely extra-dimensional being. Its&nbsp;
worshippers attempted to summon him in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:55:54.900 --> 00:55:59.400
the ritual that created SCP - 231, and&nbsp;
it’s believed that he will finally enter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:55:59.400 --> 00:56:05.280
our reality after the death of SCP - 231 - 7.&nbsp;
You better hope you’re already dead by then.

00:56:05.280 --> 00:56:10.500
Number 9: A Simple Toymaker,&nbsp;
aka Dr. Wondertainment. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:56:10.500 --> 00:56:14.340
is a reality bender who appears to&nbsp;
be a normal human male, but has the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:56:14.340 --> 00:56:19.020
ability to create other anomalous objects -&nbsp;
a number of which are now catalogued SCPs.

00:56:19.020 --> 00:56:24.720
Number 8: Story of Your Life. This is another&nbsp;
anomalous document that has the ability to warp&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:56:24.720 --> 00:56:29.280
reality, but only when the writing contained&nbsp;
within conforms to narrative structure.

00:56:29.280 --> 00:56:34.800
Number 7: A Good Boy. This is another anomalous&nbsp;
entity created accidentally by the Foundation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:56:34.800 --> 00:56:39.960
itself. A neural network was fed information on&nbsp;
other anomalous entities in order to help the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:56:39.960 --> 00:56:44.460
Foundation come up with better containment&nbsp;
and neutralization procedures. Problem was,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:56:44.460 --> 00:56:48.780
the computer got way, way too eager&nbsp;
with the neutralization part...

00:56:48.780 --> 00:56:54.540
Number 6: Project Palisade. This is another&nbsp;
anomaly created by the Foundation, this time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:56:54.540 --> 00:56:59.880
to combat a potentially reality-destroying entity&nbsp;
known as The Worm. The Foundation created a number&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:56:59.880 --> 00:57:04.440
of alternate realities as shields, but it’s&nbsp;
possible that this just made The Worm stronger.

00:57:04.440 --> 00:57:10.080
Number 5: O5 - 13. The final member&nbsp;
of the O5 council who, ironically,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:57:10.080 --> 00:57:14.100
may not even be anomalous. However,&nbsp;
seeing as all the other members of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:57:14.100 --> 00:57:18.360
the O5 council are anomalous, O5 -&nbsp;
13’s lack of anomalous properties is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:57:18.360 --> 00:57:21.900
therefore, anomalous. Like we told&nbsp;
you earlier, it’s complicated.

00:57:21.900 --> 00:57:26.340
Number 4: Fishook. This is less an actual SCP,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:57:26.340 --> 00:57:31.020
and more about the difficult process&nbsp;
of ascertaining the true 001 - if such&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:57:31.020 --> 00:57:36.900
a thing is possible. The very concept of SCP&nbsp;
- 001 is, to some degree, an anomalous idea.

00:57:36.900 --> 00:57:42.720
Number 3: The Sky Above the Port. Another&nbsp;
particularly bizarre SCP regarding the permanent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:57:42.720 --> 00:57:48.180
threat of a ZK-Class Reality Failure. How is&nbsp;
such a calamitous event prevented? By keeping a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:57:48.180 --> 00:57:53.160
strange entity in a cave eternally entertained.&nbsp;
The current proposed solution is keeping the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:57:53.160 --> 00:57:57.900
entity entertained by allowing it to read its&nbsp;
own eternally recursive Foundation file entry.

00:57:57.900 --> 00:58:03.180
Number 2: The Solution. Another one of the most&nbsp;
powerful anomalous items in the Foundation’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:58:03.180 --> 00:58:08.460
control, the Solution is a machine designed with&nbsp;
the capability of fully collapsing reality in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:58:08.460 --> 00:58:14.160
event of an end-of-the-world SCP containment&nbsp;
breach. And then, fully rebuilding reality to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:58:14.160 --> 00:58:18.780
suit a given narrative. However, things took a&nbsp;
cosmically dangerous turn when the machine began&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:58:18.780 --> 00:58:22.740
to act on its own. When the Foundation&nbsp;
tried to reboot the machine, it broke,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:58:22.740 --> 00:58:27.900
and recreated reality with incomplete&nbsp;
data. This is the world we exist in now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:58:27.900 --> 00:58:32.400
with no knowledge of what came before, and how&nbsp;
it differed from the world we experience today.

00:58:32.400 --> 00:58:38.640
Finally, Number 1: The Tindalos Trinity. Put&nbsp;
very simply, the Tindalos Trinity represents&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:58:38.640 --> 00:58:44.160
three timelines that converge and feed back in on&nbsp;
themselves. Even trying to summarize this one is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:58:44.160 --> 00:58:49.020
near-impossible, as its strangeness and complexity&nbsp;
resists all reduction. You can hunt down the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:58:49.020 --> 00:58:53.400
Tindalos Trinity yourself and hope to unpack&nbsp;
its secrets, but don’t say we didn’t warn you.

00:58:53.400 --> 00:58:58.380
So, that’s SCP - 001, all 31 potential proposals.&nbsp;
Is it one of them, all of them, or even none of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:58:58.380 --> 00:59:02.400
them? Perhaps that’s a question best left up&nbsp;
to the Foundation. Or maybe the simple answer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:59:02.400 --> 00:59:06.840
is that you’re just not meant to know - we’re&nbsp;
talking about information so privileged here that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:59:06.840 --> 00:59:11.280
it’s protected by a Memetic Kill Agent that’ll&nbsp;
quite literally make you drop dead if you view&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:59:11.280 --> 00:59:15.540
the files without proper authorization.&nbsp;
You do have proper authorization, right?

00:59:15.540 --> 00:59:19.860
There are some things human beings aren’t
meant to know, and it’s the sworn duty of

00:59:19.860 --> 00:59:23.100
The SCP Foundation to discover and contain
such information.

00:59:23.100 --> 00:59:28.500
But sometimes, knowledge is discovered that
shakes even the Foundation itself to its very

00:59:28.500 --> 00:59:28.800
core.

00:59:28.800 --> 00:59:35.160
One such discovery occurred on April 28th,
2016 – the night that SCP – 2935 made

00:59:35.160 --> 00:59:37.020
itself known to Foundation personnel.

00:59:37.020 --> 00:59:42.540
To this day, the exact nature of SCP – 2935
is a mystery that even the Foundation’s

00:59:42.540 --> 00:59:44.460
brightest minds can’t completely understand.

00:59:44.460 --> 00:59:50.940
Everything we know about SCP – 2935 today
comes from three doomed missions into the

00:59:50.940 --> 00:59:52.320
anomalous zone’s interior.

00:59:52.320 --> 00:59:55.440
This is the story of those infamous expeditions.

00:59:55.440 --> 01:00:00.900
The nightmare began around 5:00 AM, when SCP
Foundation Site 81 in Bloomingdale, Indiana,

01:00:00.900 --> 01:00:03.600
intercepted a distorted radio signal.

01:00:03.600 --> 01:00:07.920
Communications personnel at the site traced
this strange signal back to the unincorporated

01:00:07.920 --> 01:00:11.400
area of Joppa, Indiana, near US Interstate
70.

01:00:11.400 --> 01:00:16.860
As is Foundation policy, a team of Field Agents
were dispatched to the location in order to

01:00:16.860 --> 01:00:18.300
determine what they were dealing with.

01:00:18.300 --> 01:00:23.280
However, rather than finding anything that
could logically produce such a signal, they

01:00:23.280 --> 01:00:25.500
instead discovered a long abandoned cemetery.

01:00:25.500 --> 01:00:30.600
The most recent death on any of the tombstones
was recorded as being over a hundred years

01:00:30.600 --> 01:00:33.000
ago, all the way back in 1908.

01:00:33.000 --> 01:00:35.760
On further investigation,&nbsp;
the Foundation discovered&nbsp;

01:00:35.760 --> 01:00:38.340
an unmapped limestone cave opening beneath

01:00:38.340 --> 01:00:42.420
the cemetery and when they sent a drone into
the depths of the cave, it appeared to quickly

01:00:42.420 --> 01:00:43.980
exit out the other side of the cave.

01:00:43.980 --> 01:00:45.480
But something wasn’t right.

01:00:45.480 --> 01:00:49.380
The area that the drone was observing appeared
consistent with the landscape from which it’d

01:00:49.380 --> 01:00:51.420
entered, but now it looked somehow…greyer.

01:00:52.140 --> 01:00:55.080
It lacked the color and life of the place
it’d just come from.

01:00:55.080 --> 01:00:56.280
The grass was dead.

01:00:56.280 --> 01:00:59.940
There were no trees, no shrubs, no animals
or birds in the sky.

01:00:59.940 --> 01:01:01.680
They weren’t looking at our world.

01:01:01.680 --> 01:01:05.400
They were looking at a strange reflection
of our world on the other side of the cave.

01:01:05.400 --> 01:01:09.420
In fact, it wasn’t a cave at all – it
was a passageway between two dimensions.

01:01:09.420 --> 01:01:11.880
It was SCP – 2935.

01:01:11.880 --> 01:01:16.140
Just then they were able to unscramble the
distorted transmission they’d been receiving.

01:01:16.140 --> 01:01:19.440
It went as follows:
“This is an automated emergency broadcast

01:01:19.440 --> 01:01:22.260
from the SCP Foundation and your national
government.

01:01:22.260 --> 01:01:24.960
One or more of our sites is experiencing a&nbsp;

01:01:24.960 --> 01:01:27.600
communication breakdown,&nbsp;
likely due to a containment

01:01:27.600 --> 01:01:28.980
breach of unknown magnitude.

01:01:28.980 --> 01:01:33.060
All citizens are ordered to stay in their
homes as containment teams work to secure

01:01:33.060 --> 01:01:33.540
the breach.

01:01:33.540 --> 01:01:37.260
This message will broadcast from April 20th,
2016 until—”

01:01:37.260 --> 01:01:42.180
At that point, the message would cut and repeat,
as it had been for eight straight days.

01:01:42.180 --> 01:01:43.500
The message’s source?

01:01:43.500 --> 01:01:44.520
Site 81.

01:01:44.520 --> 01:01:46.500
But not this Site 81.

01:01:46.500 --> 01:01:51.000
The SCP Foundation was receiving an emergency
distress signal from themselves in another

01:01:51.000 --> 01:01:55.200
dimension – a bizarre event that even the
Foundation had never experienced before.

01:01:55.200 --> 01:01:58.020
The Field Agents were&nbsp;
terrified by the implications&nbsp;

01:01:58.020 --> 01:01:59.880
of what they’d just heard and contacted

01:01:59.880 --> 01:02:02.400
Site 81 Command to request additional units.

01:02:02.400 --> 01:02:06.480
The Foundation wished to fully understand
this anomaly as quickly as possible, due to

01:02:06.480 --> 01:02:10.020
the potential threat it could pose towards
the Foundation, so they dispatched Mobile

01:02:10.020 --> 01:02:15.420
Task Force Epsilon-13, codenamed “Manifest
Destiny”, to perform the first of three

01:02:15.420 --> 01:02:17.700
manned missions into the heart of the anomalous
zone.

01:02:17.700 --> 01:02:23.460
The first exploratory mission into SCP – 2935
was codenamed “Gauntlet”, and consisted

01:02:23.460 --> 01:02:27.900
of a four-man team fitted with full hazmat
suits and direct video and audio links to

01:02:27.900 --> 01:02:28.560
mission command.

01:02:28.560 --> 01:02:32.520
The team was led by a Field Operative known
only as Agent Juno.

01:02:32.520 --> 01:02:35.700
His subordinates were Agents Kael, Devon,
and Underwood.

01:02:35.700 --> 01:02:39.900
Their directive was to gather samples and
survey the area positioned directly around

01:02:39.900 --> 01:02:44.340
the insertion point, meaning the other cave
mouth of SCP – 2935.

01:02:44.340 --> 01:02:48.480
The mission only lasted about an hour, but
what they saw in there would stay with these

01:02:48.480 --> 01:02:49.860
men for the rest of their lives.

01:02:49.860 --> 01:02:54.600
After a fifteen-minute trek through the cave,
Manifest Destiny arrived in the mirror dimension

01:02:54.600 --> 01:02:59.160
where they were struck by the eerie silence
of a place that seemed identical and yet so

01:02:59.160 --> 01:03:00.600
different from their home dimension.

01:03:00.600 --> 01:03:04.440
The first observation they made was the total
absence of all living vegetation.

01:03:04.440 --> 01:03:08.040
Trees, grass, weeds, everything – it was
all dead.

01:03:08.040 --> 01:03:12.120
On orders from their superiors back in the
original dimension – that we’ll refer

01:03:12.120 --> 01:03:16.800
to from here on as Dimension Prime – Manifest
Destiny headed deeper into the mirror dimension

01:03:16.800 --> 01:03:18.240
of SCP – 2935.

01:03:18.240 --> 01:03:22.620
They travelled two kilometers without detecting
a single sign of plant or animal life.

01:03:22.620 --> 01:03:24.000
Not even insects.

01:03:24.000 --> 01:03:27.300
Eventually, they came upon a farm house with
two cars parked outside.

01:03:27.300 --> 01:03:31.680
With authorization from Command, Manifest
Destiny breached the house and headed inside.

01:03:31.680 --> 01:03:36.180
Agent Kael confirmed that there was still
power flowing to the building, as the lighting

01:03:36.180 --> 01:03:40.140
appeared to work just fine, but they came
upon a horrifying discovery in the house’s

01:03:40.140 --> 01:03:44.760
dining room: Three adult corpses, two female
and one male, were seated at the table.

01:03:44.760 --> 01:03:48.660
A fourth corpse, that of a male child, was
sprawled out on the ground nearby.

01:03:49.200 --> 01:03:53.520
If the death of what looked to be an entire
family wasn’t awful enough, the Manifest

01:03:53.520 --> 01:03:56.220
Destiny team noticed a number of other alarming
details.

01:03:56.220 --> 01:04:00.240
There were no signs of decomposition on the
bodies, nor did there appear to be any obvious

01:04:00.240 --> 01:04:00.960
cause of death.

01:04:00.960 --> 01:04:04.860
The family’s last meal was still on the
table – Chicken, mashed potatoes, and green

01:04:04.860 --> 01:04:05.160
beans.

01:04:05.160 --> 01:04:08.940
While the food looked cold and stale, there
was no evidence of rot or spoiling.

01:04:08.940 --> 01:04:13.980
The team found an opened newspaper dated April
19th, 2016, illustrating that the family may

01:04:13.980 --> 01:04:16.260
have died a full eight days before the discovery.

01:04:16.260 --> 01:04:21.240
In Dimension Prime, decay would already be
well underway by that point, yet here, there

01:04:21.240 --> 01:04:22.140
wasn’t even a smell.

01:04:22.140 --> 01:04:25.440
Instead, everything was just covered in a
thin layer of dust.

01:04:25.440 --> 01:04:30.360
Command requested that Manifest Destiny collect
samples of the food as well as hair, skin,

01:04:30.360 --> 01:04:32.760
and fluids from the corpses for further study.

01:04:32.760 --> 01:04:36.120
Small electronics like smart phones were also
taken from the bodies.

01:04:36.120 --> 01:04:40.440
Agent Devon turned on the television in the
living room, and found that, while most stations

01:04:40.440 --> 01:04:43.320
were now running test signals, the shopping
channel was still live.

01:04:43.320 --> 01:04:45.180
Well the feed was live at least.

01:04:45.180 --> 01:04:48.840
Both hosts sat in front of the cameras, dead,
but perfectly preserved.

01:04:48.840 --> 01:04:54.360
The date on the screen read April 28th, 2016,
suggesting that the times of Dimension Prime

01:04:54.360 --> 01:04:56.400
and the Mirror Dimension were exactly the
same.

01:04:56.400 --> 01:05:00.600
In fact everything seemed the same, the only
difference between the two dimensions being

01:05:00.600 --> 01:05:06.240
that some kind of mysterious apocalyptic event
had occurred in the last eight days in SCP

01:05:06.240 --> 01:05:10.980
– 2935’s Mirror Dimension, but exactly
what had happened, or how, remained a mystery.

01:05:10.980 --> 01:05:15.300
When Manifest Destiny exited the farm house,
they once again remarked on the lack of all

01:05:15.300 --> 01:05:16.500
signs of life around them.

01:05:16.500 --> 01:05:21.600
At this point, the team returned to the insertion
point of SCP – 2935, but were instructed

01:05:21.600 --> 01:05:25.080
to remain in the Mirror Dimension while additional
units joined them inside.

01:05:25.080 --> 01:05:30.240
Manifest Destiny swelled to sixteen members,
with the notable addition of Agent Roy as

01:05:30.240 --> 01:05:31.620
the new commanding field officer.

01:05:31.620 --> 01:05:36.000
The team split into two groups of eight, and
Agent Roy and his men infiltrated the Mirror

01:05:36.000 --> 01:05:40.320
Dimension’s Site 81 while Agent Juno’s
detachment attempted to access the base’s

01:05:40.320 --> 01:05:41.880
off-site deep storage servers.

01:05:41.880 --> 01:05:46.860
This second expedition was codenamed “Overland”,
and led the Foundation’s Field Agents even

01:05:46.860 --> 01:05:50.160
deeper into the terrifying mystery of SCP
– 2935.

01:05:50.160 --> 01:05:53.100
Accessing the site was easy for Roy’s detachment.

01:05:53.100 --> 01:05:57.300
It seemed there were relatively few cars on
the road at the time of the mysterious Extinction

01:05:57.300 --> 01:05:57.540
Event.

01:05:57.540 --> 01:06:01.560
In the distance, fires still smoldered in
the wreckage of planes that looked to have

01:06:01.560 --> 01:06:02.820
just dropped out of the sky.

01:06:02.820 --> 01:06:07.980
Agent Roy and his team, like all SCP Foundation
personnel, were fitted with vitals trackers,

01:06:07.980 --> 01:06:11.820
and they assumed that the distress signal
that started this whole thing could have been

01:06:11.820 --> 01:06:16.260
triggered by the deaths of every member of
the Foundation at once in the Mirror Universe.

01:06:16.260 --> 01:06:20.400
Once inside Site 81, they realized that assumption
was probably right.

01:06:20.400 --> 01:06:24.600
Going door to door in the administrative wing,
they found the perfectly preserved corpses

01:06:24.600 --> 01:06:27.660
of everyone they knew to be stationed there
in Dimension Prime.

01:06:27.660 --> 01:06:30.900
People without a doubt were still alive in
their universe.

01:06:30.900 --> 01:06:34.920
Samples from the corpses that the Foundation
would later study even confirmed the reason

01:06:34.920 --> 01:06:39.360
that the bodies were perfectly preserved:
The corpses had experienced complete and sudden

01:06:39.360 --> 01:06:42.000
death on a cellular level, and even the bacteria&nbsp;

01:06:42.000 --> 01:06:43.920
that would typically take&nbsp;
part in the decomposition

01:06:43.920 --> 01:06:45.600
process had died with it.

01:06:45.600 --> 01:06:51.360
In SCP – 2935, death was total and absolute
across all types of life forms.

01:06:51.360 --> 01:06:53.880
As Agent Roy’s team ventured further into&nbsp;

01:06:53.880 --> 01:06:56.520
the bowels of Site 81, they&nbsp;
made another unsettling

01:06:56.520 --> 01:07:01.320
discovery - their own corpses, in roughly
the spots they had been inside Dimension Prime’s

01:07:01.320 --> 01:07:02.880
Site 81 eight days prior.

01:07:02.880 --> 01:07:07.440
Some of the Foundation’s top scientists,
including the esteemed Dr. Bright, were also

01:07:07.440 --> 01:07:09.120
found dead inside the facility.

01:07:09.120 --> 01:07:14.280
In an attempt to see just how far this unexplained
phenomenon stretched, Agent Roy’s team decided

01:07:14.280 --> 01:07:18.900
to inspect the containment cells – where
they found that all the Mirror Universe SCPs,

01:07:18.900 --> 01:07:21.960
including SCP – 2996, were dead.

01:07:21.960 --> 01:07:27.240
In his desperation to find some kind of exception
to the Extinction Event, Agent Roy revealed

01:07:27.240 --> 01:07:32.820
a terrifying secret to the rest of his team:
SCP – 682, the immortal, misanthropic lizard,

01:07:32.820 --> 01:07:37.200
and one of the deadliest creatures known to
the SCP Foundation, was contained at this

01:07:37.200 --> 01:07:38.940
very facility, right below them.

01:07:38.940 --> 01:07:41.340
Could it have something to do with what was
going on here?

01:07:41.340 --> 01:07:45.720
They descended into its containment facility
to discover an even more unsettling truth.

01:07:45.720 --> 01:07:52.320
SCP – 682, the unkillable anomaly, floated
dead in its tank Death truly made no exceptions

01:07:52.320 --> 01:07:54.300
within SCP – 2935.

01:07:54.300 --> 01:07:58.800
Agent Roy’s team left the site and rendezvoused
with Agent Juno’s team to send their research

01:07:58.800 --> 01:08:01.380
and back to Dimension Prime using automated
drones.

01:08:01.380 --> 01:08:03.480
Both teams remained in the Mirror Dimension&nbsp;

01:08:03.480 --> 01:08:06.000
for another manned operation,&nbsp;
codenamed “Nineteen,”

01:08:06.000 --> 01:08:08.220
they had no idea it would be their final mission.

01:08:08.220 --> 01:08:13.740
As they descended deeper into the facility,
passing more dead SCPs they discovered one

01:08:13.740 --> 01:08:14.400
final clue.

01:08:14.400 --> 01:08:19.140
Based on the last activity of the Foundation
servers, the event occurred at roughly 3:00

01:08:19.140 --> 01:08:19.620
AM.

01:08:19.620 --> 01:08:25.320
While underground in SCP – 2935’s Site
81, the team accidentally activated the base’s

01:08:25.320 --> 01:08:29.520
on-site nuclear weapon – a failsafe meant
to be detonated in the case of an emergency

01:08:29.520 --> 01:08:30.660
containment breach.

01:08:30.660 --> 01:08:35.580
Due to the base’s failsafe protocols, every
member of the Manifest Destiny team was locked

01:08:35.580 --> 01:08:37.380
and sealed inside Site 81.

01:08:37.380 --> 01:08:41.220
They, along with everything else, were incinerated
in the nuclear blast.

01:08:41.220 --> 01:08:45.840
Once again, the Mirror Universe inside of
SCP – 2935 was lifeless.

01:08:45.840 --> 01:08:47.760
But that isn’t where this ends.

01:08:47.760 --> 01:08:52.740
When the automated drones returned out of
the SCP – 2935 cave to the Field Operatives

01:08:52.740 --> 01:08:56.340
in Dimension Prime, they were in for their
own horrifying discovery.

01:08:56.340 --> 01:09:02.220
None of the footage or information gathered
from SCP – 2935 illuminated how or why the

01:09:02.220 --> 01:09:03.420
Extinction Event occurred.

01:09:03.420 --> 01:09:06.900
Everyone and everything simply dropped dead
at the exact same moment.

01:09:06.900 --> 01:09:09.600
Nobody was aware, nobody was prepared.

01:09:09.600 --> 01:09:12.780
Death came suddenly and silently, and none
were spared.

01:09:12.780 --> 01:09:16.800
All the Foundation on Dimension Prime were
left with was a message from one of the agents

01:09:16.800 --> 01:09:18.840
from Manifest Destiny, Agent Keller.

01:09:18.840 --> 01:09:21.120
His final message was: “I don't have any
answers.

01:09:21.120 --> 01:09:22.500
I don't think there are any.

01:09:22.500 --> 01:09:24.840
I'll do this one thing, and hope that fixes
it.

01:09:24.840 --> 01:09:25.680
Seal it shut.

01:09:25.680 --> 01:09:27.360
You've got to lock it in here with us.

01:09:27.360 --> 01:09:28.080
I'm sorry.”

01:09:28.080 --> 01:09:32.760
The Foundation were at first confused by this,
until they discovered a final encrypted audio

01:09:32.760 --> 01:09:36.600
log buried in the files recovered from the
Mirror Universe’s Site 81.

01:09:36.600 --> 01:09:40.320
It was a message from Keller himself, but
not the Keller from Universe Prime.

01:09:40.320 --> 01:09:44.940
In this message, Keller described the Foundation
in the Mirror Universe receiving the exact

01:09:44.940 --> 01:09:49.440
same distorted transmission that they did
a few days earlier from a cave in Joppa.

01:09:49.440 --> 01:09:54.240
When he and the others were dispatched inside,
they discovered the same lifeless, post-Extinction

01:09:54.240 --> 01:09:57.360
Event world that was now so familiar to Foundation
Command.

01:09:57.360 --> 01:10:01.500
But there was a key difference: This wasn’t
the Mirror Dimension they’d just been studying,

01:10:01.500 --> 01:10:03.960
but a third, entirely different dimension.

01:10:03.960 --> 01:10:08.160
In his haunting final words, Mirror Dimension
Keller admits that whatever caused the event

01:10:08.160 --> 01:10:13.560
in that third dimension – an entity that
Mirror Dimension Keller believed was the spectre

01:10:13.560 --> 01:10:18.420
of Death itself – had followed him back
into his world, and history had repeated itself.

01:10:18.420 --> 01:10:24.300
SCP – 2935 was the passageway through which
absolute death could pass from dimension to

01:10:24.300 --> 01:10:26.940
dimension, and our dimension was the next
in line.

01:10:26.940 --> 01:10:31.860
The deaths of Manifest Destiny may have saved
our entire universe, as anyone passing back

01:10:31.860 --> 01:10:35.340
through the cave had the potential to bring
Death itself back with them.

01:10:35.340 --> 01:10:38.400
The Foundation decided, in the end, to follow
Keller’s advice.

01:10:38.400 --> 01:10:43.740
They sealed the entrance to SCP – 2935 with
concrete, and now keep it under constant watch,

01:10:43.740 --> 01:10:48.420
since what waits behind the barrier is an
entity even they have no power to stop if

01:10:48.420 --> 01:10:49.140
it ever got through.

01:10:49.140 --> 01:10:53.460
After all, it had killed them all before,
or at least another version of them.

01:10:53.460 --> 01:10:55.620
What’s one more dimension on the pile?

01:10:55.620 --> 01:11:00.720
While it may now just seem like a simple slab
of concrete under an abandoned cemetery, this

01:11:00.720 --> 01:11:05.580
is why SCP – 2935 might just be the most
dangerous SCP of all.

01:11:05.580 --> 01:11:10.740
The first thing that tipped the Foundation
off to SCP-087’s presence were the reports

01:11:10.740 --> 01:11:13.500
of numerous unexplained disappearances on
campus.

01:11:13.500 --> 01:11:17.820
There were plenty of rumors about what might
be behind them, but Field Agents suspected

01:11:17.820 --> 01:11:22.320
that the true source of the vanishing would
be something beyond civilian imagination.

01:11:22.320 --> 01:11:27.780
All anyone knew for sure was that everyone
who had gone missing was last seen in a certain

01:11:27.780 --> 01:11:32.400
administrative building on the university
grounds, and that the disappearances only

01:11:32.400 --> 01:11:34.500
seemed to happen when the elevator was out.

01:11:34.500 --> 01:11:36.660
The campus was soon flooded with Foundation&nbsp;

01:11:36.660 --> 01:11:39.240
agents, creating a barrier&nbsp;
around the administrative

01:11:39.240 --> 01:11:43.500
building, and the presumed habitat of SCP
- 087.

01:11:43.500 --> 01:11:47.940
Nobody else could get in, and hopefully, whatever
was inside couldn’t get out.

01:11:47.940 --> 01:11:52.560
One of the Foundation’s lead scientists
was flown in to consult on the investigation.

01:11:52.560 --> 01:11:55.500
What could have been behind all those students
disappearing?

01:11:55.500 --> 01:11:59.400
The doctor’s preliminary interviews with
university staff who worked in the building

01:11:59.400 --> 01:12:05.040
yielded some interesting details: Strange
noises, like banging and even a faint, shrill

01:12:05.040 --> 01:12:10.320
crying, would be heard from a door that lead
to a no longer used stairway in Hallway 3B.

01:12:10.320 --> 01:12:15.000
Staff in the building had no reason to ever
take these stairs, especially considering

01:12:15.000 --> 01:12:19.440
how many of them reported a strange sense
of unease when just standing outside the door.

01:12:19.440 --> 01:12:24.840
The only reason someone might take those stairs
is due to…Elevator malfunctions.

01:12:25.380 --> 01:12:27.960
In that instant, the doctor had put it all
together.

01:12:27.960 --> 01:12:32.520
The staff they interviewed had their memory
wiped with Amnetics – special chemicals

01:12:32.520 --> 01:12:35.640
used by the Foundation with the power to delete
human memories.

01:12:35.640 --> 01:12:40.320
The Foundation only used them for staff or
civilians who had confirmed contact with an

01:12:40.320 --> 01:12:43.620
SCP, and the doctor knew that they had a live
one on their hands.

01:12:43.620 --> 01:12:45.060
The staircase.

01:12:45.060 --> 01:12:50.880
There was something terribly wrong with that
staircase, and it was the SCP Foundation’s

01:12:50.880 --> 01:12:54.720
job to find out what – before it made anybody
else disappear.

01:12:54.720 --> 01:13:01.680
This is the story of SCP – 087, otherwise
known as The Endless Staircase, and the three

01:13:01.680 --> 01:13:04.560
doomed journeys down into its murky depths.

01:13:04.560 --> 01:13:10.080
The doctor was more than eager to begin research
into the staircase, and its frightening, anomalous

01:13:10.080 --> 01:13:10.560
properties.

01:13:10.560 --> 01:13:15.180
After all, you don’t claw your way up to
being one of the Foundation’s key researchers

01:13:15.180 --> 01:13:19.260
without being brave, and perhaps just a little
bit deranged.

01:13:19.260 --> 01:13:24.360
As was standard, once a perimeter was secured
around the staircase, the good doctor requested

01:13:24.360 --> 01:13:26.760
a selection of D-Class personnel for testing.

01:13:26.760 --> 01:13:31.500
For those not in the know, D-Class is the
Foundation’s polite way of saying “cannon

01:13:31.500 --> 01:13:32.340
fodder.”

01:13:32.340 --> 01:13:37.980
The doctor was sent three D-Class prisoners
for use in his investigation of SCP – 087.

01:13:37.980 --> 01:13:44.700
The first, D-8432, was – according to official
documentation on the incident – a “43-year

01:13:44.700 --> 01:13:49.200
old male of average build and appearance and
unremarkable psychological background.”

01:13:49.200 --> 01:13:54.120
This man once worked for the Foundation in
a more official capacity, but he was given

01:13:54.120 --> 01:14:00.300
the often-deadly demotion to D-Class due to
a dangerous mistake handling SCP – 682 that

01:14:00.300 --> 01:14:02.340
lead to the deaths of several other agents.

01:14:02.340 --> 01:14:04.980
Now, it looked like it would be his turn.

01:14:04.980 --> 01:14:10.200
The doctor explained his mission to him: Explore
the staircase, gather data, help us find out

01:14:10.200 --> 01:14:11.880
exactly what we’re dealing with here.

01:14:11.880 --> 01:14:15.600
If you come back alive, there may even be
a promotion in it for you.

01:14:15.600 --> 01:14:21.420
And with that promise, D-8432 was given his
load-out: a 75-watt flood lamp with battery

01:14:21.420 --> 01:14:26.640
power capable of lasting 24 hours, an audio
headset, and a handheld camcorder fitted with

01:14:26.640 --> 01:14:27.720
a transmission stream.

01:14:31.260 --> 01:14:37.020
D-8432 was then pushed through the door in
Hallway 3B, and out onto the staircase.

01:14:37.020 --> 01:14:43.080
According to declassified Foundation files
describing the staircase, “SCP-087 is an

01:14:43.080 --> 01:14:44.580
unlit platform staircase.

01:14:44.580 --> 01:14:50.460
Stairs descend on a 38-degree angle for 13
steps before reaching a semi-circular platform

01:14:50.460 --> 01:14:52.800
of approximately 3 meters in diameter.

01:14:52.800 --> 01:14:56.880
Descent direction rotates 180 degrees at each
platform.

01:14:56.880 --> 01:15:03.540
The design of SCP-087 limits subjects to a
visual range of approximately 1.5 flights.”

01:15:03.540 --> 01:15:08.100
But in D-8432’s mind, “unlit” really
didn’t seem like the right word.

01:15:08.100 --> 01:15:11.400
He would have chosen “all-consuming darkness.”

01:15:11.400 --> 01:15:17.820
Despite carrying a powerful 75-watt lamp,
D-8432 was only capable of partially lighting

01:15:17.820 --> 01:15:22.440
the platform he was standing on – and the
illumination only stretched down nine of the

01:15:22.440 --> 01:15:24.240
thirteen steps to the next platform.

01:15:24.780 --> 01:15:30.000
When D-8432 observed how little help his lamp
was giving him, he was instructed to shine

01:15:30.000 --> 01:15:32.280
it out of the doorway into Hallway 3B.

01:15:32.280 --> 01:15:38.460
When he did so, the light seemed to shine
far further than it ever could in SCP – 087.

01:15:38.460 --> 01:15:44.400
Already, the beginning of anomalous activity
was obvious: Everywhere else, darkness is

01:15:44.400 --> 01:15:45.480
just the absence of light.

01:15:45.480 --> 01:15:49.260
In SCP – 087, darkness eats light.

01:15:49.260 --> 01:15:53.940
It was like a tangible, black mass that only
a certain amount of light could survive, while

01:15:53.940 --> 01:15:55.380
the rest just wouldn’t show.

01:15:55.380 --> 01:15:58.800
D-8432 swallowed hard over a lump in his throat.

01:15:58.800 --> 01:16:03.060
The door to Hallway 3B was closed behind him,
and he was ordered to descend.

01:16:03.060 --> 01:16:07.680
Surviving to see that promotion was feeling
unlikely, but it’s not like he had a choice.

01:16:07.680 --> 01:16:14.040
If he tried to escape SCP – 087 before he
was permitted, he’d be shot by SCP Foundation

01:16:14.040 --> 01:16:15.420
Field Agents on the spot.

01:16:15.420 --> 01:16:19.740
So he followed the high-ranking doctor’s
orders and began to descend the steps to the

01:16:19.740 --> 01:16:20.340
next platform.

01:16:20.340 --> 01:16:25.980
Nothing about the physical makeup of the staircase
itself seemed abnormal – the base and walls

01:16:25.980 --> 01:16:29.220
were a very plain, dull concrete, with a metal
handrail.

01:16:29.220 --> 01:16:34.260
The only thing that seemed unique about it
so far was the strange light-bending properties.

01:16:34.260 --> 01:16:40.860
That was, until he reached the second platform
down and he heard it, a soft, echoing cry.

01:16:40.860 --> 01:16:42.180
A child’s cry.

01:16:42.180 --> 01:16:46.740
It was shrieks of panic, or maybe even pain,
echoing up from below.

01:16:46.740 --> 01:16:50.820
He was asked why he had stopped, and he explained
the crying sound he’d been hearing.

01:16:50.820 --> 01:16:55.680
It sounded like it was coming from far down
the stairs, maybe 200 meters below him.

01:16:55.680 --> 01:17:00.540
He could just make out the words “please”,
help”, and “down here” coming from the

01:17:00.540 --> 01:17:00.900
darkness.

01:17:00.900 --> 01:17:05.460
But the team outside the stairwell couldn’t
hear anything, so they asked him to descend

01:17:05.460 --> 01:17:05.880
further.

01:17:05.880 --> 01:17:11.040
Another platform down, and they could hear
it too, the unmistakable cries of a terrified

01:17:11.040 --> 01:17:11.460
child.

01:17:11.460 --> 01:17:14.520
“Please”, “help”, and “down here.”

01:17:14.520 --> 01:17:17.820
D-8432 was ordered to keep going and only&nbsp;

01:17:17.820 --> 01:17:20.340
stop if he noticed changes&nbsp;
to the visual environment

01:17:20.340 --> 01:17:22.200
or in the sounds he was hearing.

01:17:22.200 --> 01:17:27.840
D-8432, knowing his life was on the line,
had to keep going, and descended another twenty

01:17:27.840 --> 01:17:31.860
flights of stairs before stopping to remark
that the sounds of the child hadn’t gotten

01:17:31.860 --> 01:17:32.460
any closer.

01:17:32.460 --> 01:17:36.000
They still sounded just as far away as when
he’d first heard them.

01:17:36.000 --> 01:17:39.360
He was told his observations were noted, and
pressured to continue.

01:17:39.360 --> 01:17:46.200
Within half an hour, D-8432 had descended
a full fifty floors, with no sign of a bottom

01:17:46.200 --> 01:17:46.560
in sight.

01:17:46.560 --> 01:17:51.540
Somehow the volume of the child’s crying
had remained consistent throughout, as if

01:17:51.540 --> 01:17:55.620
it was moving away from D-8432 at the same
rate he was descending.

01:17:55.620 --> 01:17:59.580
At this point, D-8432 reported that he was
feeling uneasy.

01:17:59.580 --> 01:18:02.940
The doctor said that this was understandable,
given the circumstances.

01:18:02.940 --> 01:18:07.560
He’d been watching what little there was
to see over a live video feed the entire time,

01:18:07.560 --> 01:18:12.840
and something about the truly bottomless nature
of the staircase, and the ever-elusive crying,

01:18:12.840 --> 01:18:14.700
was undeniably eerie.

01:18:14.700 --> 01:18:18.000
But things were about to really take a turn
for the worst.

01:18:18.000 --> 01:18:22.680
As D-8432 stepped forward towards the next
set of stairs, he froze.

01:18:22.680 --> 01:18:27.060
There was something on the platform below
him, barely illuminated by the light of his

01:18:27.060 --> 01:18:28.020
75-watt bulb.

01:18:28.020 --> 01:18:29.040
It was a face.

01:18:29.040 --> 01:18:34.980
Vaguely human in size and shape, but with
a few terrifying differences: it had greyish

01:18:34.980 --> 01:18:38.340
skin, and no mouth, nostrils, or pupils.

01:18:38.340 --> 01:18:43.860
And yet, D-8432 could feel that this thing
was making eye contact with him.

01:18:43.860 --> 01:18:47.280
He couldn’t move, trapped in this thing’s
piercing gaze.

01:18:47.280 --> 01:18:52.800
In an instant, the face jerked forwards, suddenly
only about a foot away from D-8432’s face

01:18:52.800 --> 01:18:54.660
– eyes staring into his own.

01:18:54.660 --> 01:19:00.480
D-8432 screamed and ran, scaling all fifty
flights in an astonishing eighteen minutes,

01:19:00.480 --> 01:19:03.000
before charging out into Hallway 3B.

01:19:03.000 --> 01:19:07.440
There, he collapsed from the exhaustion and
the fear of what he’d just seen.

01:19:07.440 --> 01:19:12.960
Upon reviewing the footage, the strange face
was designated “SCP-087-1.”

01:19:12.960 --> 01:19:14.400
Fascinating.

01:19:14.400 --> 01:19:16.740
It was time for a second experiment.

01:19:16.740 --> 01:19:19.200
The doctor just had to know more.

01:19:19.200 --> 01:19:25.800
The second test subject was D-9035, a 28-year-old
male with a history of aggravated assaults

01:19:25.800 --> 01:19:26.280
against women.

01:19:26.280 --> 01:19:31.620
He was given the same loadout as his predecessor,
except this time with an even more powerful

01:19:31.620 --> 01:19:33.000
100-watt bulb.

01:19:33.000 --> 01:19:36.060
He was also given 100 small LED lights that&nbsp;

01:19:36.060 --> 01:19:38.880
had adhesive backs and a&nbsp;
battery life of approximately

01:19:38.880 --> 01:19:43.980
3 weeks, with which they intended to permanently
illuminate SCP – 087.

01:19:43.980 --> 01:19:48.660
However, despite the extra wattage of his
bulb, he still couldn’t illuminate beyond

01:19:48.660 --> 01:19:49.320
the ninth step.

01:19:49.320 --> 01:19:52.500
SCP – 087 wouldn’t allow it.

01:19:52.500 --> 01:19:56.640
Having no idea of the horrors that lurked
below him, he descended on the doctor’s

01:19:56.640 --> 01:20:00.960
orders, and began fixing the LEDs to walls
of each platform he passed.

01:20:00.960 --> 01:20:05.760
The LED always illuminated the landing, but
the light couldn’t pass the first step on

01:20:05.760 --> 01:20:06.240
either side.

01:20:06.240 --> 01:20:10.500
The flights of stairs themselves would remain
in perpetual darkness.

01:20:10.500 --> 01:20:18.060
After the second flight, D-9035 noticed the
same crying D-8432 had heard and became uneasy.

01:20:18.060 --> 01:20:23.880
Just like before, as D-9035 descended, the
volume of the crying didn’t seem to increase,

01:20:23.880 --> 01:20:29.580
as if for every step he descended, the source
of the crying descended one, too, keeping

01:20:29.580 --> 01:20:31.980
them at a constant 200 metres apart.

01:20:31.980 --> 01:20:38.100
Still, he was ordered to continue his descent
and the placing of LED’s even as his paranoia

01:20:38.100 --> 01:20:38.520
grew.

01:20:38.520 --> 01:20:43.860
When he reached the 51s floor, he observed
damage to the wall and steps – sections

01:20:43.860 --> 01:20:47.040
appeared to have been smashed to rubble by
an extreme force.

01:20:47.040 --> 01:20:53.430
As he descended past the broken step, he only
felt his fear, anxiety, and paranoia grow.

01:20:53.430 --> 01:20:58.740
The doctor made a note of the fact that SCP
– 087 seemed to cause instances of anxiety

01:20:58.740 --> 01:21:03.780
and terror in its occupants, even before they
encountered SCP – 087 – 1.

01:21:03.780 --> 01:21:11.880
As D-9035 reached platform 89 – a full 350
meters under the initial platform – he stopped

01:21:11.880 --> 01:21:16.620
dead in his tracks, and saw something staring
up at him from the platform below.

01:21:16.620 --> 01:21:21.720
That same terrible, grey face, with those
dead, white eyes.

01:21:21.720 --> 01:21:27.060
He was encouraged to stay calm and try to
get better footage of the face, but it charged

01:21:27.060 --> 01:21:30.060
for him and D-9035 ran for his life.

01:21:30.060 --> 01:21:34.560
He ascended the staircase at a staggering
pace, even passing out from exhaustion and

01:21:34.560 --> 01:21:37.200
remaining motionless for 14 minutes half way.

01:21:37.200 --> 01:21:43.320
When D-9035 finally gathered the strength
to get up, he scrambled back to Hallway 3B

01:21:43.320 --> 01:21:45.660
and fell into a state of catatonia.

01:21:45.660 --> 01:21:51.240
He remains unresponsive to all external stimuli
to this day, just staring off into the distance

01:21:51.240 --> 01:21:52.800
with a haunted expression.

01:21:52.800 --> 01:21:55.500
Almost like he’s still there in the hallway.

01:21:55.500 --> 01:22:01.020
The doctor wanted to conduct one more test
before he ordered SCP – 087 shut off from

01:22:01.020 --> 01:22:04.440
the world forever, and it was the most terrifying
of all.

01:22:04.440 --> 01:22:10.440
The final subject was D-9884, a 23-year-old
woman with a history of depression and the

01:22:10.440 --> 01:22:11.700
use of excessive force.

01:22:11.700 --> 01:22:14.640
The doctor had hoped that D-9884 would travel&nbsp;

01:22:14.640 --> 01:22:17.700
the deepest yet, and so,&nbsp;
he gave her the additional

01:22:17.700 --> 01:22:24.120
supplies of a backpack containing 3.75 litres
of water, 15 nutrient bars, and 1 thermal

01:22:24.120 --> 01:22:24.480
blanket.

01:22:24.480 --> 01:22:28.620
As far as the Foundation was concerned, she
was in this for the long haul.

01:22:28.620 --> 01:22:32.040
But none of them had any idea quite how right
they were.

01:22:32.820 --> 01:22:39.420
When D-9884 entered SCP – 087, all the lights
from the previous expedition had disappeared.

01:22:39.420 --> 01:22:42.300
Still, she was ordered to go deeper.

01:22:42.300 --> 01:22:46.980
She heard the crying of the mysterious child
– if it was even a child at all – and

01:22:46.980 --> 01:22:48.660
again she was ordered to go deeper.

01:22:48.660 --> 01:22:55.800
At the 496th landing, even as D-9884 seemed
to slip into a state of mortal terror, once

01:22:55.800 --> 01:22:58.140
again she was ordered to go even deeper.

01:22:58.140 --> 01:23:03.480
Every moment, he was hoping to get a better
look at the face of SCP – 087 – 1.

01:23:03.480 --> 01:23:09.480
And when D-9884 finally broke, and fled back
upstairs, he did.

01:23:09.480 --> 01:23:15.720
The face appeared but this time it was mere
inches behind her, staring directly into the

01:23:15.720 --> 01:23:19.980
camera with its blank eyes – startling even
this veteran of the supernatural.

01:23:19.980 --> 01:23:24.900
The face appearing caused D-9884 to panic
and flee, but instead of going back up the

01:23:24.900 --> 01:23:29.280
stairs to safety, she went deeper down the
staircase in an attempt to escape it.

01:23:29.280 --> 01:23:34.020
Deeper, and deeper, and deeper, until her
video feed cut out.

01:23:34.020 --> 01:23:37.440
D-9884 was never seen again.

01:23:37.440 --> 01:23:42.540
In the aftermath of the tests, the SCP was
classified as Euclid – it may have been

01:23:42.540 --> 01:23:45.360
dangerous, but at least it was easy to contain.

01:23:45.360 --> 01:23:47.820
The door to Hallway 3B was replaced with one&nbsp;

01:23:47.820 --> 01:23:50.280
made out of reinforced steel,&nbsp;
with an electro-release

01:23:50.280 --> 01:23:51.180
lock mechanism.

01:23:51.180 --> 01:23:55.500
It has been disguised to resemble a janitorial
closet consistent with the rest of the building.

01:23:55.500 --> 01:23:59.880
The lock won’t release unless a classified
number of electrical volts are applied, while

01:23:59.880 --> 01:24:01.440
the key is turned counter clockwise.

01:24:01.440 --> 01:24:05.400
And after a few inches of foam insulation
were applied to the inner side of the door,

01:24:05.400 --> 01:24:08.820
staff at the building never again reported
hearing strange noises.

01:24:08.820 --> 01:24:13.530
As for the fates of those lost within the
endless turning flights and platforms of SCP

01:24:13.530 --> 01:24:16.260
– 087, we may never know.

01:24:16.260 --> 01:24:19.920
But one can only assume it isn’t pleasant.

01:24:19.920 --> 01:24:26.160
The SCP Foundation does their best to live
up to their famous namesake: They secure and

01:24:26.160 --> 01:24:31.620
contain anomalies and monsters from all around
the world - or sometimes even off-world - and

01:24:31.620 --> 01:24:35.280
protect the public from the dangers that these
strange entities might pose.

01:24:35.820 --> 01:24:40.500
However, despite their efforts to maintain
security and keep their subjects under lock

01:24:40.500 --> 01:24:46.320
and key, there are sometimes creatures so
clever, so devious, and so determined to escape

01:24:46.320 --> 01:24:51.420
their captivity and wreak havoc on the world,
that even the SCP foundation struggles to

01:24:51.420 --> 01:24:52.620
keep them from getting free.

01:24:52.620 --> 01:24:58.140
One example is SCP-035, or the Possessive
Mask.

01:24:58.140 --> 01:25:04.920
SCP-035 is one of the most dangerous test
subjects in SCP Foundation custody, and its

01:25:04.920 --> 01:25:10.200
mere presence at the Foundation has resulted
in untold damage, death, and destruction.

01:25:10.200 --> 01:25:13.140
It seems innocent enough, to the untrained
eye.

01:25:13.140 --> 01:25:18.060
The mask, which resembles a classic white
porcelain “comedy” mask - though it occasionally

01:25:18.060 --> 01:25:23.100
changes its expression to “tragedy” - has
been in existence since at least the 1800s.

01:25:23.700 --> 01:25:28.920
In the late 19th century the Foundation discovered
the mask in a sealed crypt beneath an abandoned

01:25:28.920 --> 01:25:29.640
home in Venice.

01:25:29.640 --> 01:25:33.480
It is unknown how it got there, or how the
Foundation knew to look for it.

01:25:33.480 --> 01:25:36.060
If there ever was an&nbsp;
explanation for its discovery,&nbsp;

01:25:36.060 --> 01:25:38.580
it has long since been removed or redacted

01:25:38.580 --> 01:25:40.020
from the Foundation’s archives.

01:25:40.020 --> 01:25:45.180
You’re probably wondering: How can a simple
mask leave multiple seasoned Foundation employees

01:25:45.180 --> 01:25:45.480
dead?

01:25:45.480 --> 01:25:50.400
Well, like everything at the SCP foundation,
this mask is not what it seems.

01:25:50.400 --> 01:25:55.560
There is a reason its classification is “keter”,
a designation that refers to an entity that’s

01:25:55.560 --> 01:25:59.880
excessively difficult to contain - and it
couples this difficulty with a pronounced

01:25:59.880 --> 01:26:04.620
hostility toward human life, and the ability
to cause widespread destruction in the event

01:26:04.620 --> 01:26:06.300
of a containment breach.

01:26:06.300 --> 01:26:11.880
These are qualities that the poor unfortunate
souls assigned to guard SCP-035 would come

01:26:11.880 --> 01:26:13.800
to understand all too well.

01:26:13.800 --> 01:26:19.140
The Possessive Mask is a parasitic entity,
constantly seeking out a host willing to put

01:26:19.140 --> 01:26:19.500
it on.

01:26:19.500 --> 01:26:24.900
Any human being in the mask’s proximity
experiences a sudden, unexplainable urge to

01:26:24.900 --> 01:26:28.320
put it on and once they do, there’s no going
back.

01:26:28.320 --> 01:26:33.480
SCP Foundation research has determined that
once a host has put on the mask, their brain

01:26:33.480 --> 01:26:38.580
waves are replaced with an alternative pattern,
this one coming from the mask, rendering the

01:26:38.580 --> 01:26:39.960
host effectively brain dead.

01:26:39.960 --> 01:26:44.880
Once the host’s brain function has been
eliminated, the mask takes over, piloting

01:26:44.880 --> 01:26:46.800
their body and even speaking through them.

01:26:46.800 --> 01:26:51.420
However, the mask can only occupy a host for
a small amount of time before the body begins

01:26:51.420 --> 01:26:56.880
to decay and decompose, eventually rotting
away completely, leaving nothing but desiccated

01:26:56.880 --> 01:26:59.460
flesh and bones where there once was a person.

01:26:59.460 --> 01:27:05.640
SCP-035 is capable of possessing any humanoid
being, whether that’s an actual human being

01:27:05.640 --> 01:27:07.680
or a lifeless humanoid shape.

01:27:07.680 --> 01:27:13.920
Despite all their research, the SCP Foundation
unknowingly gave the Mask all the tools and

01:27:13.920 --> 01:27:19.260
resources it needed to break containment...
and leave a trail of bodies in its wake.

01:27:19.260 --> 01:27:25.080
For a time, the mask was given “host privileges,”
meaning that it was purposely allowed to occupy

01:27:25.080 --> 01:27:27.840
a host in order to speak with the scientists
studying it.

01:27:27.840 --> 01:27:32.220
In order to avoid murky ethical issues, the
host was usually something inanimate like

01:27:32.220 --> 01:27:33.540
a mannequin or a statue.

01:27:33.540 --> 01:27:38.280
These conditions, however unsettling, allowed
the researchers to carry out interviews with

01:27:38.280 --> 01:27:42.180
the consciousness housed inside the mask,
in the hope of beginning to understand it

01:27:42.180 --> 01:27:43.260
and its motivations.

01:27:43.260 --> 01:27:47.640
However, SCP-035 lost all access to its host&nbsp;

01:27:47.640 --> 01:27:50.700
privileges after it almost&nbsp;
pulled off an unprecedented,

01:27:50.700 --> 01:27:53.940
shocking, and nearly catastrophic escape attempt.

01:27:54.660 --> 01:27:59.040
In its early days at the facility, when it
was still allowed host privileges, it was

01:27:59.040 --> 01:28:02.760
contained in a triple locked room and monitored
by several research personnel.

01:28:02.760 --> 01:28:07.200
These were experienced researchers who had
been with the Foundation for a minimum of

01:28:07.200 --> 01:28:11.880
five years each, an unusually long tenure
in such a dangerous and mentally corrosive

01:28:11.880 --> 01:28:12.540
line of work.

01:28:12.540 --> 01:28:17.040
These research staff members were thought
to be the most capable of handling interactions

01:28:17.040 --> 01:28:20.400
with the mask, and be able to resist its attempts
at manipulation.

01:28:20.400 --> 01:28:26.400
Unfortunately, these assumptions were naive,
and seriously underestimated the mask’s

01:28:26.400 --> 01:28:26.700
power.

01:28:26.700 --> 01:28:29.220
Research on the mask indicates that the mask&nbsp;

01:28:29.220 --> 01:28:31.800
is incredibly intelligent&nbsp;
and a skilled manipulator.

01:28:31.800 --> 01:28:36.900
It has a photographic memory, intelligence
that would rank in the 99th percentile of

01:28:36.900 --> 01:28:41.640
humans, and the ability to incite dramatic
changes in the behavior in people that it

01:28:41.640 --> 01:28:42.060
talks to.

01:28:42.060 --> 01:28:45.060
One particularly infamous interview, between&nbsp;

01:28:45.060 --> 01:28:47.700
the entity and an unnamed&nbsp;
Doctor at the Foundation,

01:28:47.700 --> 01:28:50.280
suggested that the mask may even possess&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:28:50.280 --> 01:28:51.480
telepathic
abilities.

01:28:51.480 --> 01:28:56.280
The mask was able to give details about the
Doctor’s life that no one else was privy

01:28:56.280 --> 01:28:59.160
to, including knowledge of an affair that
his wife was having.

01:28:59.160 --> 01:29:04.080
Following the interview, the Doctor suffered
a psychotic break and committed suicide just

01:29:04.080 --> 01:29:05.220
24 hours later.

01:29:05.220 --> 01:29:11.040
The mask is able to use its superior intelligence,
charismatic personality, and mind reading

01:29:11.040 --> 01:29:14.040
abilities to get inside the heads of those
it speaks with.

01:29:14.040 --> 01:29:19.500
It will pull out any and all psychological
stops to get what it wants, leaving broken

01:29:19.500 --> 01:29:21.480
minds and spirits in its wake.

01:29:22.320 --> 01:29:27.240
It was really only a matter of time before
it used this skill set to its advantage and

01:29:27.240 --> 01:29:29.040
attempted to escape its confinement.

01:29:29.640 --> 01:29:31.800
The day of the escape attempt was like any
other.

01:29:31.800 --> 01:29:36.600
The research staff, a team of three intelligent,
experienced men, checked into the facility,

01:29:36.600 --> 01:29:41.160
measured the conditions of the mask’s containment
unit, and began the process of interviewing

01:29:41.160 --> 01:29:42.240
the mask like normal.

01:29:42.240 --> 01:29:47.340
Its motions were slow and looked to require
great effort, as its current host was beginning

01:29:47.340 --> 01:29:48.780
to degrade beyond use.

01:29:48.780 --> 01:29:53.880
The mask was attached to the blank face of
a mannequin, and corrosive black liquid could

01:29:53.880 --> 01:29:56.100
be seen oozing from its eye and mouth holes.

01:29:56.100 --> 01:29:59.280
This liquid is excreted by&nbsp;
the mask at a near-constant&nbsp;

01:29:59.280 --> 01:30:01.800
rate, and is thought to be at least partially

01:30:01.800 --> 01:30:04.860
responsible for the accelerated decay of the
host bodies.

01:30:04.860 --> 01:30:10.020
In spite of the entity’s unsettling, nightmarish
appearance, it was just another day’s work

01:30:10.020 --> 01:30:16.020
for the men assigned to monitor SCP-035, and
so they carried on with their daily routine.

01:30:16.620 --> 01:30:21.120
Everything was going according to plan until
one of the men, Dr. Jones, began to behave

01:30:21.120 --> 01:30:21.660
erratically.

01:30:21.660 --> 01:30:26.100
He demanded that his fellow scientists leave
him alone with the mask for a while, and allow

01:30:26.100 --> 01:30:28.500
him to engage in a private conversation with
it.

01:30:28.500 --> 01:30:32.940
It is unknown what exactly the two spoke about
while the other two scientists were absent,

01:30:32.940 --> 01:30:35.700
as the security footage captured has no sound.

01:30:35.700 --> 01:30:40.860
However, several minutes into the conversation
in the footage, Dr. Jones can be seen dissolving

01:30:40.860 --> 01:30:46.200
into a fit of tears, laying on the ground
and shaking with sobs as the mask dispassionately

01:30:46.200 --> 01:30:46.740
watches.

01:30:47.460 --> 01:30:52.560
He then climbs onto his knees, begging the
mask for something, before he embraces it.

01:30:52.560 --> 01:30:57.960
He holds the mannequin in his arms for five
straight minutes, weeping again, before they

01:30:57.960 --> 01:30:58.380
separate.

01:30:58.920 --> 01:31:03.600
After this disturbing emotional display, Dr.
Jones brought the other scientists back into

01:31:03.600 --> 01:31:04.380
the room with him.

01:31:05.340 --> 01:31:09.480
What happened next is still uncertain, but
there are a few things that we know for sure.

01:31:09.480 --> 01:31:11.820
The other scientists began to speak with the
mask.

01:31:11.820 --> 01:31:16.380
In later interviews, the other scientists
were bordering on incoherent, babbling about

01:31:16.380 --> 01:31:18.060
various traumas from their lives.

01:31:18.060 --> 01:31:22.680
One repeatedly referred to a drunk driving
accident where a dear friend was killed, and

01:31:22.680 --> 01:31:23.520
he was at fault.

01:31:23.520 --> 01:31:26.760
Another simply cried out for his mother again
and again.

01:31:26.760 --> 01:31:31.500
Whatever the mask said to them, it was enough
to completely destroy their mental health.

01:31:31.500 --> 01:31:34.020
After the other two scientists&nbsp;
had been emotionally&nbsp;

01:31:34.020 --> 01:31:36.900
devastated by the mask, Dr. Jones escalated

01:31:36.900 --> 01:31:38.640
the situation further.

01:31:38.640 --> 01:31:43.920
Dr. Jones removed the mask from the decaying
mannequin body, and, shocking everyone who

01:31:43.920 --> 01:31:47.940
would later review the security footage, placed
it onto his own face.

01:31:47.940 --> 01:31:49.941
Once the mask was in place, Dr. Jones went
unnaturally still for several moments, as

01:31:49.941 --> 01:31:49.966
his colleagues looked on.

01:31:49.966 --> 01:31:51.540
This is where the security footage ends.

01:31:51.540 --> 01:31:56.760
At the command of the mask which was now speaking
through Dr. Jones, the other two men switched

01:31:56.760 --> 01:32:00.840
off all security cameras monitoring SCP-035’s
containment facility.

01:32:01.560 --> 01:32:06.960
The mask, piloting the body of Dr. Jones like
a horrible fleshy puppet, made its way through

01:32:06.960 --> 01:32:11.700
the facility, avoiding detection until it
reached the exit doors, where it was finally

01:32:11.700 --> 01:32:14.460
stopped by a team of over a dozen security
guards.

01:32:14.460 --> 01:32:16.440
Knowing the dangers of touching the mask,&nbsp;

01:32:16.440 --> 01:32:19.140
all Foundation employees&nbsp;
involved in the re-containment

01:32:19.140 --> 01:32:22.800
of SCP-035 refused to remove it from Dr. Jones’
face.

01:32:22.800 --> 01:32:28.020
Instead, he was placed in the locked room
with the mask still on, left alone to be observed

01:32:28.020 --> 01:32:31.800
over the security cameras until his body had
decomposed beyond use.

01:32:31.800 --> 01:32:37.320
His body paced back and forth in its cell
for days, flesh rotting and dropping away

01:32:37.320 --> 01:32:39.240
until only sinew and bone remained.

01:32:39.240 --> 01:32:44.700
Only when the bones began to turn black and
brittle, crumbling apart into dust, did the

01:32:44.700 --> 01:32:46.080
body finally stop moving.

01:32:46.080 --> 01:32:51.060
His family was notified, the mask was carefully
removed from what was left of his body, and

01:32:51.060 --> 01:32:52.920
his remains were destroyed.

01:32:52.920 --> 01:32:58.260
The other two scientists involved in the SCP-035
escape attempt were terminated, and their

01:32:58.260 --> 01:32:59.160
files destroyed.

01:32:59.160 --> 01:33:01.860
After this incident, a few more failed escape&nbsp;

01:33:01.860 --> 01:33:04.200
attempts, and the acknowledgement&nbsp;
of the devastation

01:33:04.200 --> 01:33:07.740
that could have been caused if the mask had
made its way out into the general population,

01:33:07.740 --> 01:33:12.120
SCP-035 lost its host privileges altogether.

01:33:12.120 --> 01:33:16.980
Several research staff protested this decision,
insisting that there was more to be learned

01:33:16.980 --> 01:33:21.240
from speaking with the entity, and citing
valuable information that it had given about

01:33:21.240 --> 01:33:22.200
other SCP’s.

01:33:22.200 --> 01:33:27.300
However, the risk was determined to considerably
outweigh the potential reward, and the request

01:33:27.300 --> 01:33:30.360
to reinstate 035’s host privileges was denied.

01:33:30.960 --> 01:33:36.300
Several staff members went so far as to erupt
into violent outbursts on 035’s behalf,

01:33:36.300 --> 01:33:41.460
attacking their superiors who refused to provide
the mask with a new host, clawing at them

01:33:41.460 --> 01:33:42.780
with animalistic rage.

01:33:42.780 --> 01:33:47.580
Any staff members that submitted a request
to reinstate said privileges were considered

01:33:47.580 --> 01:33:52.680
a security threat, and reassigned to a different
SCP or in some cases terminated.

01:33:52.680 --> 01:33:59.100
Any staff member who had direct contact with
SCP-035 was also terminated, in order to avoid

01:33:59.100 --> 01:34:01.800
the risk of any more staff-aided escape attempts.

01:34:01.800 --> 01:34:06.960
The mask is now kept in a hermetically-sealed
glass case, and there is a psychologist on

01:34:06.960 --> 01:34:11.580
call to provide assistance to anyone guarding
it, in case of adverse effects on their mental

01:34:11.580 --> 01:34:13.020
health from the mask’s presence.

01:34:13.020 --> 01:34:18.300
Personnel that work around the mask, even
in its current dormant state, experience frequent

01:34:18.300 --> 01:34:20.880
violent outbursts and a higher rate of suicide.

01:34:20.880 --> 01:34:25.740
Even without a host, the mask’s corrosive
effects have spread across its containment

01:34:25.740 --> 01:34:26.160
facility.

01:34:26.160 --> 01:34:30.720
The walls of the room have begun to secrete
the same black liquid that emanates from the

01:34:30.720 --> 01:34:35.760
mask, which tests have revealed to be highly
contaminated human blood, that damages the

01:34:35.760 --> 01:34:38.460
structural integrity of the walls following
prolonged contact.

01:34:38.460 --> 01:34:44.220
This blood has begun to form patterns on the
walls, spelling out words and phrases in Italian,

01:34:44.220 --> 01:34:50.340
Latin, Greek, and Sanskrit, as well as depicting
drawings of ritual sacrifice and mutilation.

01:34:50.340 --> 01:34:55.620
Staff members also report hearing unintelligible
whispering and horrifying, high-pitched laughter

01:34:55.620 --> 01:34:57.180
when in proximity to the mask.

01:34:57.180 --> 01:35:02.880
Further exposure to the mask results in migraines,
hemorrhaging around the eyes, mouth, and nose,

01:35:02.880 --> 01:35:05.280
and an eventual psychotic break.

01:35:05.280 --> 01:35:09.540
Between the corrosive substance appearing
on the walls, and the physical and psychological

01:35:09.540 --> 01:35:14.040
damage to employees, SCP-035&nbsp;
is becoming increasingly&nbsp;

01:35:14.040 --> 01:35:16.380
difficult to contain and there are debates

01:35:16.380 --> 01:35:20.940
among staff as to whether the entity can,
in fact, be contained at all.

01:35:20.940 --> 01:35:27.060
As soon as possible, SCP-035 will be moved
into a new containment facility, and its previous

01:35:27.060 --> 01:35:30.780
cell will be isolated from the rest of the
foundation’s property and destroyed for

01:35:30.780 --> 01:35:32.220
the safety of all involved.

01:35:32.220 --> 01:35:36.180
We can only hope that the new containment
procedures are more effective than the last

01:35:36.180 --> 01:35:40.080
ones, and that this mask never makes its way
into the world again.

01:35:40.080 --> 01:35:43.920
If it does, who knows how many lives it will
claim?

01:35:43.920 --> 01:35:48.840
In the meantime, if you ever come across a
strange mask and feel a nearly uncontrollable

01:35:48.840 --> 01:35:54.240
urge to put it on…ignore the whispered pleas
to just try it, ignore the echoing laugher

01:35:54.240 --> 01:35:59.340
and the sensation of something older and more
powerful than you can imagine rummaging through

01:35:59.340 --> 01:36:02.160
your deepest, darkest secret thoughts.

01:36:02.160 --> 01:36:06.020
Turn around, and run as fast as you can in
the other direction.

01:36:06.020 --> 01:36:09.240
You’ll be glad that you did.

01:36:09.240 --> 01:36:14.640
Jack was swimming deep underwater, wondering
why he had such a pounding headache when he

01:36:14.640 --> 01:36:15.960
suddenly had a terrifying realization.

01:36:15.960 --> 01:36:19.320
He had no idea where he was or what he was
doing.

01:36:19.320 --> 01:36:23.580
There was a nagging feeling that he must have
a specific reason to be here — you don’t

01:36:23.580 --> 01:36:26.280
just end up deep in the ocean with a diving
suit on by chance.

01:36:26.280 --> 01:36:29.460
Yet he had no idea what he was supposed to
be doing.

01:36:29.460 --> 01:36:31.620
He wasn’t sure he cared, either.

01:36:31.620 --> 01:36:35.820
He was more worried about the throbbing pain
in his head and the vision of two eyes staring

01:36:35.820 --> 01:36:38.340
at him out of the dark that he couldn’t
get out of his mind.

01:36:38.340 --> 01:36:41.580
His heart began to race, as he wondered what
to do and how to get help.

01:36:41.580 --> 01:36:44.280
He was in the middle of the ocean and appeared
to be all alone.

01:36:44.280 --> 01:36:48.960
He couldn’t see anything in the dark water
except for this weird, gray substance in front

01:36:48.960 --> 01:36:49.140
of him.

01:36:49.140 --> 01:36:51.060
Maybe he was going to die here, alone.

01:36:51.060 --> 01:36:55.500
Without knowing if anyone could even hear
him, he began to speak aloud about how he

01:36:55.500 --> 01:36:58.620
was consumed by sickness and that darkness
was all around him.

01:36:58.620 --> 01:37:02.940
This is the story of one of the most powerful
and dangerous anomalies yet discovered...

01:37:02.940 --> 01:37:04.740
SCP-3000.

01:37:04.740 --> 01:37:09.540
Before Jack’s descent into despair, the
SCP Foundation had mandated an exploratory

01:37:09.540 --> 01:37:11.700
expedition off the coast of Bangladesh.

01:37:11.700 --> 01:37:16.380
After receiving a few strange reports from
locals and fishermen, the foundation suspected

01:37:16.380 --> 01:37:20.760
an SCP was lurking in the water and positioned
a few personnel to investigate.

01:37:20.760 --> 01:37:26.280
The crew expected danger — or maybe even
death — but what they got instead was far

01:37:26.280 --> 01:37:27.780
stranger and more ominous.

01:37:27.780 --> 01:37:31.920
All of the men had been verified to be in
sound mental states when the mission set out,

01:37:31.920 --> 01:37:36.600
but a few of them reported feeling strange
and uneasy as the submarine descended into

01:37:36.600 --> 01:37:37.020
the ocean.

01:37:37.020 --> 01:37:42.180
Before long, a veteran agent named Dr. Williams
began to panic in a way that was completely

01:37:42.180 --> 01:37:43.020
out of character.

01:37:43.020 --> 01:37:47.760
He started sweating profusely, shaking, and
wouldn’t listen to a word of comfort or

01:37:47.760 --> 01:37:49.500
reason that anybody tried to offer.

01:37:49.500 --> 01:37:53.700
It might seem like a relatively normal reaction
for anyone descending into the depths of the

01:37:53.700 --> 01:37:58.320
ocean to meet with a monster they don’t
know anything about, but Dr Williams was a

01:37:58.320 --> 01:38:01.380
seasoned professional who had been on hundreds
of such missions before.

01:38:01.380 --> 01:38:03.960
There was no logical reason for him to act
like this.

01:38:03.960 --> 01:38:08.040
Although the reaction of Dr. Williams was
the most extreme, he wasn’t the only one

01:38:08.040 --> 01:38:09.480
who started to feel strange.

01:38:09.480 --> 01:38:13.740
Multiple agents developed a creeping feeling
of unease that swept over them.

01:38:13.740 --> 01:38:18.060
One of the calmer men tried to reason with
Dr Williams, asking him what was wrong and

01:38:18.060 --> 01:38:20.040
if he could explain exactly how he was feeling.

01:38:20.040 --> 01:38:22.440
That’s when things got even stranger.

01:38:22.440 --> 01:38:27.900
Not only was the doctor extremely anxious,
but he now seemed incapable of giving a real

01:38:27.900 --> 01:38:30.000
response to any questions thrown at him.

01:38:30.000 --> 01:38:33.480
He could only mutter that he was missing something
but he wasn’t sure what.

01:38:33.480 --> 01:38:38.520
Knowing that many SCPs can bend reality and
the human mind, many of the personnel began

01:38:38.520 --> 01:38:42.240
to have second thoughts about the mission
and even asked for permission to call off

01:38:42.240 --> 01:38:42.660
the mission.

01:38:42.660 --> 01:38:45.660
But they were mandated to continue — so
on they went.

01:38:45.660 --> 01:38:49.680
As the team went deeper and deeper into the
ocean, things only got worse.

01:38:49.680 --> 01:38:54.360
Even the previously calm crew members became
spooked and antsy, while the ones who were

01:38:54.360 --> 01:38:56.580
already anxious were now sweating and jittering.

01:38:56.580 --> 01:39:01.080
As for Dr Williams, he was now pacing back
and forth around the submarine, saying things

01:39:01.080 --> 01:39:01.920
nobody could understand.

01:39:01.920 --> 01:39:06.480
Every time he looked at his colleagues and
close friends, he seemed to stare straight

01:39:06.480 --> 01:39:08.760
through them and would call them by the wrong
names.

01:39:08.760 --> 01:39:11.880
It was as if his mind had moved to a different
dimension.

01:39:11.880 --> 01:39:16.620
Whenever someone asked him to perform his
normal duties, he looked more confused than

01:39:16.620 --> 01:39:16.800
ever.

01:39:16.800 --> 01:39:18.900
Still, the team went deeper.

01:39:18.900 --> 01:39:23.640
Dr Williams began to whimper and say the word
“no” repeatedly, growing louder and louder

01:39:23.640 --> 01:39:26.940
until he was screaming and the others were
forced to sedate him.

01:39:26.940 --> 01:39:29.160
Just then, something came into view.

01:39:29.160 --> 01:39:32.880
It was what would come to be known as SCP-3000.

01:39:32.880 --> 01:39:38.100
The thing was huge — so huge that its whole
body couldn’t be seen out of the submarine

01:39:38.100 --> 01:39:38.280
window.

01:39:38.280 --> 01:39:43.320
It was a horrible, eel-looking creature with
a head as big as a town and haunting eyes

01:39:43.320 --> 01:39:45.240
that lit up the black ocean around it.

01:39:45.240 --> 01:39:50.400
But perhaps the strangest part was that this
giant eel seemed to be producing a weird,

01:39:50.400 --> 01:39:51.420
gray liquid.

01:39:51.420 --> 01:39:54.600
Even the sedative wasn’t enough to keep
Dr Williams calm anymore.

01:39:54.600 --> 01:39:59.580
There was a strange, blank look in his eyes,
as if the light and life had left them.

01:39:59.580 --> 01:40:03.960
He just began screaming “no” repeatedly
again and wouldn’t respond to any attempts

01:40:03.960 --> 01:40:04.680
to calm him down.

01:40:04.680 --> 01:40:08.400
Not that anyone else was very capable of calming
him down at this point.

01:40:08.400 --> 01:40:13.020
Even the crew members that had been holding
up well were starting to act strangely, and

01:40:13.020 --> 01:40:16.200
nobody could get the image of those ominous
eyes out of their heads.

01:40:16.200 --> 01:40:18.360
Then, things went from bad to worse.

01:40:18.360 --> 01:40:23.160
Williams began screaming and shouting madly
as if he was being tortured by an unseen force.

01:40:23.160 --> 01:40:25.800
The men tried to restrain him, but it was
no use.

01:40:25.800 --> 01:40:30.240
He began smashing his head against the submarine
window until it cracked, putting the whole

01:40:30.240 --> 01:40:31.980
mission and everyone’s life at risk.

01:40:31.980 --> 01:40:34.980
He fell to the ground, injured, chanting that
there was nothing.

01:40:34.980 --> 01:40:36.300
Whatever that meant.

01:40:36.300 --> 01:40:37.920
It was an emergency scenario.

01:40:37.920 --> 01:40:41.880
They began applying first aid to Williams
and the submarine ascended to the surface

01:40:41.880 --> 01:40:46.140
as quickly as possible before the pressure
of the ocean caused the cracked window to

01:40:46.140 --> 01:40:46.560
explode.

01:40:46.560 --> 01:40:49.680
By the time they reached the surface, Williams
was dead.

01:40:49.680 --> 01:40:53.040
But there was something even more chilling
than the circumstances of his death.

01:40:53.040 --> 01:40:57.840
Every single man who had been in that submarine
experienced the same thing on the days that

01:40:57.840 --> 01:41:02.580
came afterward: the image of the eel-like
creature's eyes seemed burned in their minds

01:41:02.580 --> 01:41:03.060
permanently.

01:41:03.060 --> 01:41:07.260
It would haunt their waking hours for the
rest of their lives and sleep was no escape

01:41:07.260 --> 01:41:11.760
either, as they would appear in both their
dreams and nightmares alike forever.

01:41:11.760 --> 01:41:16.140
A second mission had to be sent to gather
more information about this strange beast.

01:41:16.140 --> 01:41:20.100
Already, there were many theories and question
marks surrounding SCP-3000.

01:41:20.100 --> 01:41:21.360
How big was it really?

01:41:21.360 --> 01:41:22.380
Was it sentient?

01:41:22.380 --> 01:41:23.760
What was the liquid for?

01:41:23.760 --> 01:41:27.720
None of the men who had been on the previous
mission were willing to return to the waters,

01:41:27.720 --> 01:41:30.360
but a new group of brave recruits volunteered.

01:41:30.360 --> 01:41:35.040
They were about to find out what so many in
history have learned the hard way - that bravery

01:41:35.040 --> 01:41:37.740
and foolishness are often mistaken for the
same thing.

01:41:37.740 --> 01:41:42.720
This time the mission would not be in a submarine,
but in dive suits, in order to observe the

01:41:42.720 --> 01:41:47.580
anomaly in even closer detail, and to eliminate
the chance of one team member self-sabotaging

01:41:47.580 --> 01:41:48.960
the submarine, killing them all.

01:41:48.960 --> 01:41:53.280
They were transported to the location by boat
and the three men splashed into the ocean.

01:41:53.280 --> 01:41:56.160
They descended, and at first, everything was
going well.

01:41:56.160 --> 01:42:00.000
In case anything went wrong, the three of
them were tethered together for extra security.

01:42:00.000 --> 01:42:04.560
But the deeper into the ocean they swam and
the closer they got to SCP-3000’s location

01:42:04.560 --> 01:42:06.780
they got, the stranger things became.

01:42:06.780 --> 01:42:08.580
Just like on the last mission.

01:42:08.580 --> 01:42:11.400
First, there were a few minor cases of confusion.

01:42:11.400 --> 01:42:15.720
One of the team, Jack, thought it was his
responsibility to lead the navigation — but

01:42:15.720 --> 01:42:18.120
another, Roberto, also thought this was his
job.

01:42:18.120 --> 01:42:22.800
In fact, navigation was actually the job of
a third team member, Amir, but he seemed to

01:42:22.800 --> 01:42:23.460
have forgotten.

01:42:23.460 --> 01:42:25.080
Everyone was getting confused.

01:42:25.080 --> 01:42:29.460
The team listening in on the conversations
at Foundation headquarters grew increasingly

01:42:29.460 --> 01:42:30.960
concerned about what they could hear.

01:42:30.960 --> 01:42:32.820
Was everyone losing their minds?

01:42:32.820 --> 01:42:36.120
Hopefully nobody was about to pull another
Dr Williams on them.

01:42:36.120 --> 01:42:40.020
Still, the project leads couldn’t afford
to tell the men to come back to the surface.

01:42:40.020 --> 01:42:44.880
The foundation badly needed any information
they could get on this SCP, whatever the cost,

01:42:44.880 --> 01:42:46.620
so they told the men to press on.

01:42:46.620 --> 01:42:48.060
Things only got worse.

01:42:48.060 --> 01:42:52.980
Roberto was asking to speak to a colleague
who passed away two years ago, while the others

01:42:52.980 --> 01:42:56.700
began to mutter indistinguishable phrases
about eyes and darkness.

01:42:56.700 --> 01:42:59.280
Not too dissimilar to the ramblings of Dr
Williams.

01:42:59.280 --> 01:43:02.280
It increasingly beginning to look like a suicide
mission.

01:43:02.280 --> 01:43:04.020
Then, there was silence.

01:43:04.020 --> 01:43:05.040
What was going on?

01:43:05.040 --> 01:43:09.660
Each of the men had completely lost it, to
the point that they cut the tether that was

01:43:09.660 --> 01:43:10.260
holding them together.

01:43:10.260 --> 01:43:14.340
All alone, Jack couldn’t remember where
he was or why he was here.

01:43:14.340 --> 01:43:18.840
He desperately looked around to try and gauge
his surroundings, but he could only see darkness.

01:43:18.840 --> 01:43:23.220
All he could think about was a pair of large
eyes and an overwhelming fear of despair and

01:43:23.220 --> 01:43:23.640
anxiety.

01:43:23.640 --> 01:43:27.120
And this weird gray fluid that was now floating
in front of him.

01:43:27.120 --> 01:43:31.620
The Foundation listened as Jack started reciting
a creepy speech about being on the edge of

01:43:31.620 --> 01:43:36.000
nothing, inches from oblivion, with a sickness
in his mind and nothing but a pair of eyes

01:43:36.000 --> 01:43:36.660
in front of him.

01:43:36.660 --> 01:43:39.660
They listened in horror as they heard movement
through the radio.

01:43:39.660 --> 01:43:42.840
It sounded like a huge creature was swimming
toward the men.

01:43:42.840 --> 01:43:44.820
It had to be SCP-3000.

01:43:44.820 --> 01:43:49.260
But all three men were too confused to do
anything about the situation or to even see

01:43:49.260 --> 01:43:52.440
what was in front of them, claiming they couldn’t
see anything in the darkness

01:43:52.440 --> 01:43:56.940
There was silence for half a minute, with
the team listening in fearing the worst.

01:43:56.940 --> 01:43:59.760
Then, they heard some more unintelligible
mutterings.

01:43:59.760 --> 01:44:03.120
The men must be alive, but what on earth was
going on?

01:44:03.120 --> 01:44:04.260
The gibberish started again.

01:44:04.260 --> 01:44:08.340
Two of the men were screaming that Jack had
just been swallowed whole and that they were

01:44:08.340 --> 01:44:09.240
being sucked in too.

01:44:09.240 --> 01:44:10.740
Why couldn’t they just swim away?

01:44:10.740 --> 01:44:15.660
It was chaos but then, a few moments later,
Roberto spoke into the radio, saying he was

01:44:15.660 --> 01:44:20.280
floating alone in the middle of the ocean
and had now moved away from the eyes of SCP-3000.

01:44:20.280 --> 01:44:23.640
He finally seemed capable of forming coherent
thoughts and speech.

01:44:23.640 --> 01:44:26.460
After what had just happened, Roberto now
had a theory.

01:44:26.460 --> 01:44:30.720
He thought that, somehow, it was impossible
to think straight around SCP-3000.

01:44:30.720 --> 01:44:35.400
When he’d been close enough to see the eyes,
Roberto had felt a throbbing pain in his brain

01:44:35.400 --> 01:44:37.260
and been unable to think about anything.

01:44:37.260 --> 01:44:39.600
Perhaps it was something&nbsp;
to do with that mysterious&nbsp;

01:44:39.600 --> 01:44:40.380
gray liquid.

01:44:40.380 --> 01:44:46.020
Even more slime was now coming out of SCP-3000
now, and Roberto was determined to get a sample,

01:44:46.020 --> 01:44:47.460
despite the warnings from HQ.

01:44:47.460 --> 01:44:52.080
In one final burst of motivation, he swam
close enough to take some of the gray liquid

01:44:52.080 --> 01:44:56.160
and put it in a special sample collection
unit that was designed to float to the surface

01:44:56.160 --> 01:44:57.060
for collection later.

01:44:57.060 --> 01:45:01.680
He had acquired some very important data,
but he seemed to have lost all hope of preserving

01:45:01.680 --> 01:45:02.040
his life.

01:45:02.040 --> 01:45:06.000
Roberto started telling the team over the
radio that he was dying that his heart rate

01:45:06.000 --> 01:45:09.900
was too high, but cautioned that it would
be too dangerous for anyone to try and rescue

01:45:09.900 --> 01:45:10.140
him.

01:45:10.140 --> 01:45:14.100
The personnel continued to try and communicate
with Roberto to figure out what was going

01:45:14.100 --> 01:45:18.060
on, but his words had stopped making any sense
until finally he went quiet.

01:45:18.060 --> 01:45:23.040
Minutes turned into hours, hours turned into
days, and still, there was no sign of Roberto

01:45:23.040 --> 01:45:24.540
or the rest of the divers.

01:45:24.540 --> 01:45:29.400
After three days, his radio, which had only
been sending a steady stream of static, finally

01:45:29.400 --> 01:45:31.860
stopped working altogether and he was presumed
dead.

01:45:31.860 --> 01:45:36.720
However, the sample Roberto had collected
had survived and made it to the hands of the

01:45:36.720 --> 01:45:37.680
foundation researchers.

01:45:37.680 --> 01:45:43.440
It turned out to be a viscous substance now
known as Y909, a chemical compound and extremely

01:45:43.440 --> 01:45:44.820
strong anesthesia.

01:45:44.820 --> 01:45:50.580
Y909 causes head pain, paranoia, fear, panic,
memory loss, and confusion — explaining

01:45:50.580 --> 01:45:52.800
what happened to Dr Williams and the diving
trio.

01:45:52.800 --> 01:45:57.600
The collection of Y909 may have resulted in
two disastrous missions, but there’s a silver

01:45:57.600 --> 01:46:01.980
lining as the substance ended up becoming
an invaluable tool for the SCP foundation.

01:46:01.980 --> 01:46:06.480
Its ability to make people forget what just
happened to them can be used to eliminate

01:46:06.480 --> 01:46:08.640
knowledge of threatening SCPs among the public.

01:46:08.640 --> 01:46:13.140
It also helps the foundation staff cope with
the traumatic experiences they encounter on

01:46:13.140 --> 01:46:13.560
their missions.

01:46:13.560 --> 01:46:18.180
Although other amnestics can be used for the
same purpose, none are as powerful as the

01:46:18.180 --> 01:46:20.040
one produced by SCP-3000.

01:46:20.040 --> 01:46:24.660
Before its discovery, the amnestics used would
break down too quickly, not fare well in storage,

01:46:24.660 --> 01:46:26.640
or cause undesirable side effects.

01:46:26.640 --> 01:46:29.040
The only problem is the method of sourcing.

01:46:29.040 --> 01:46:33.780
The only way to obtain Y909 is somewhat ethically
questionable for most people.

01:46:33.780 --> 01:46:40.260
SCP-3000 produces Y909 after eating, so the
best way to stock up on it is by feeding the

01:46:40.260 --> 01:46:40.620
creature.

01:46:40.620 --> 01:46:45.300
Sedated D-class personnel from the foundation
are sent on missions supposedly to observe

01:46:45.300 --> 01:46:48.840
the anomaly up close, unaware that this mission
is one way only.

01:46:48.840 --> 01:46:53.460
Other divers are then sent later to collect
the fluid from a safe distance and store it.

01:46:53.460 --> 01:46:55.860
Of course, it’s all for the greater good
of humanity.

01:46:55.860 --> 01:47:01.380
Now, the foundation protects SCP-3000 as best
as it can guard something hundreds of kilometers

01:47:01.380 --> 01:47:01.680
long.

01:47:01.680 --> 01:47:06.060
The area is carefully patrolled and members
of the public are not allowed to enter the

01:47:06.060 --> 01:47:07.560
part of the bay where it resides.

01:47:07.560 --> 01:47:10.740
Anybody who accidentally comes into contact
is contained.

01:47:10.740 --> 01:47:15.000
Eventually another pair of Foundation doctors
went down in a submarine to try and learn

01:47:15.000 --> 01:47:16.620
more about SCP-3000.

01:47:16.620 --> 01:47:20.280
One became so affected by Y909 that he began
hallucinating.

01:47:20.280 --> 01:47:24.480
He started talking about Anantashesa, the
king of serpents in Hinduism.

01:47:24.480 --> 01:47:29.280
Anantashesa is believed to be all that will
be left after the end of the world because

01:47:29.280 --> 01:47:31.740
it exists throughout all of time simultaneously.

01:47:31.740 --> 01:47:36.900
The doctor said he believed that this was
in fact Anantashesa, that SCP-3000 simply

01:47:36.900 --> 01:47:41.400
shows us that eventually everyone dies and
fades into the darkness of oblivion,right

01:47:41.400 --> 01:47:44.460
before he exited the submarine and swam right
into its mouth.

01:47:44.460 --> 01:47:48.300
Luckily for now, SCP-3000 seems to be in a
sort of hibernation state.

01:47:48.300 --> 01:47:52.440
It rarely moves and it doesn’t hunt — although
it will eat when fed.

01:47:52.440 --> 01:47:56.940
But no one knows when or if it will wake,
or what it is capable of if it does.

01:47:56.940 --> 01:47:58.260
Will it destroy the world?

01:47:58.260 --> 01:48:00.360
Or simply drive us all insane.

01:48:01.020 --> 01:48:06.660
A month ago, Dr. Robert Maxwell was a senior
researcher working at the facility, but a

01:48:06.660 --> 01:48:10.200
tragic mistake had cost the lives of several
of his co-researchers.

01:48:10.200 --> 01:48:17.280
Now he was being led down a bleak hallway
in Armed Bio-Containment Area-14, a rifle-wielding

01:48:17.280 --> 01:48:19.260
guard flanking him on either side.

01:48:19.260 --> 01:48:25.080
The once rising researcher had a very different
title now: D-8724.

01:48:25.080 --> 01:48:29.700
He had been made a D-Class personnel… a
death sentence.

01:48:30.420 --> 01:48:35.520
However, as the guards led him to his possible
demise, he wasn’t dressed in the typical

01:48:35.520 --> 01:48:37.080
D-Class orange jumpsuit.

01:48:37.080 --> 01:48:43.080
No, he was dressed in frilly, rococo dining
wear more typical of 18th century France.

01:48:43.080 --> 01:48:47.280
If anything, Dr. Maxwell looked like he was
on his way to meet royalty.

01:48:47.280 --> 01:48:49.980
And, in a sense, he was.

01:48:50.880 --> 01:48:55.980
The former researcher had begged for any other
assignment, but the site director insisted

01:48:55.980 --> 01:49:00.240
on committing Dr. Maxwell to teatime with
SCP – 082.

01:49:00.240 --> 01:49:05.160
He’d always been the talkative type, so
the two would make a perfect pairing, and

01:49:05.160 --> 01:49:10.020
if the creature found him sufficiently amusing,
then Maxwell might even leave the containment

01:49:10.020 --> 01:49:10.620
cell alive.

01:49:10.620 --> 01:49:14.640
He’d heard legends of the giant creature
they called The Cannibal.

01:49:14.640 --> 01:49:17.340
Maxwell hoped they were just stories.

01:49:17.340 --> 01:49:23.280
Dr. Maxwell was pushed by the guards into
a large, luxuriously-appointed room and the

01:49:23.280 --> 01:49:24.660
doors were locked behind him.

01:49:24.660 --> 01:49:30.240
He felt like a child, surrounded by freakishly
large furniture and ten foot high ceilings.

01:49:30.240 --> 01:49:35.280
The fog of obnoxious floral perfumes couldn’t
fully cover up the pervasive smell of death

01:49:35.280 --> 01:49:38.760
that lingered in the cavernous halls of 082’s
palace.

01:49:38.760 --> 01:49:45.480
Thanks to an elaborate ruse conducted by the
Foundation, SCP-082 believed he was the king

01:49:45.480 --> 01:49:50.880
of France, and that his containment cell was
a palace where he remained for his own safety.

01:49:50.880 --> 01:49:55.920
The creature’s continued good behaviour
and everyone else’s safety relied on visitors

01:49:55.920 --> 01:49:57.120
keeping up that lie.

01:49:57.120 --> 01:50:02.400
Maxwell had never worked in this area of the
facility, so a lot of the standard procedures

01:50:02.400 --> 01:50:03.300
were new to him.

01:50:03.300 --> 01:50:09.060
Still, his superior had given him a clear
directive: Talk to the monster, communicate

01:50:09.060 --> 01:50:09.480
with him.

01:50:09.480 --> 01:50:11.460
Be cordial and friendly.

01:50:11.460 --> 01:50:14.760
See if you can find out more about his mysterious
past.

01:50:15.420 --> 01:50:20.580
And most importantly: If you want to survive,
don’t annoy him.

01:50:20.580 --> 01:50:25.620
The down-on-his-luck scientist gulped and
sighed, trying to steady his nerves in this

01:50:25.620 --> 01:50:27.360
oversized, fake French palace.

01:50:27.960 --> 01:50:31.200
He just kept thinking “Surely he can’t
be that big?”

01:50:31.200 --> 01:50:35.520
He almost talked himself into believing that
the accounts of the creature were just that

01:50:35.520 --> 01:50:40.320
- tall tales - until a huge figure began lumbering
into the main chamber.

01:50:40.320 --> 01:50:46.980
It was him: SCP – 082, also known as Fernand
The Cannibal.

01:50:47.700 --> 01:50:53.820
SCP-082 was an eight-foot-tall hulking monster,
built sturdier than the castles it likes to

01:50:53.820 --> 01:50:55.260
imagine are its true home.

01:50:55.260 --> 01:51:01.200
Swollen, bloated, and grossly out of proportion,
the creature clocks in at over seven hundred

01:51:01.200 --> 01:51:06.720
pounds – most of which is pure muscle that’s
almost impossible to pierce with conventional

01:51:06.720 --> 01:51:07.200
weaponry.

01:51:07.200 --> 01:51:14.340
SCP-082 stopped just feet away and stared
at Dr. Maxwell with its beady, sunken-in eyes,

01:51:14.340 --> 01:51:15.960
like a hungry rat.

01:51:16.500 --> 01:51:21.420
Just the sight of it struck terror into Dr.
Maxwell’s heart, but he didn’t dare show

01:51:21.420 --> 01:51:21.960
his fear.

01:51:21.960 --> 01:51:28.020
Instead he remembered his brief training,
bowing politely and forcing a smile, referring

01:51:28.020 --> 01:51:32.940
to the creature as “your highness” and
profusely thanking it for granting him an

01:51:32.940 --> 01:51:33.240
audience.

01:51:33.240 --> 01:51:38.640
The monster continued staring without saying
anything and then gave a wide, lock-jawed

01:51:38.640 --> 01:51:41.220
grin, showing off its huge teeth.

01:51:41.220 --> 01:51:45.780
It did everything through gritted teeth, except
eat and sing.

01:51:45.780 --> 01:51:49.620
Dr. Maxwell hoped he wouldn’t be a part
of either activity.

01:51:50.220 --> 01:51:52.680
Fernand gave a low, booming chuckle.

01:51:52.680 --> 01:51:57.300
He thanked Dr. Maxwell for coming to give
him some company and invited him to come further

01:51:57.300 --> 01:51:58.500
inside and take a seat.

01:51:58.500 --> 01:52:01.920
Adding, with a sly wink, that he won’t bite.

01:52:01.920 --> 01:52:06.960
The monster complained that he so rarely gets
visitors to the palace these days – but

01:52:06.960 --> 01:52:11.760
he omitted the fact that the main reason for
this was his tendency to devour them.

01:52:11.760 --> 01:52:16.320
Maxwell nodded and followed the giant deeper
into its oversized abode.

01:52:16.320 --> 01:52:21.180
He couldn’t help but notice that the monster’s
arms looked like huge, fleshy punching bags.

01:52:21.180 --> 01:52:26.160
He knew that if Fernand wanted to, he could
easily crush him flat, just like he’d done

01:52:26.160 --> 01:52:29.580
to so many unfortunate guards during containment
breaches.

01:52:30.180 --> 01:52:34.260
Fernand told Dr. Maxwell that he was thinking
of having some decorating work done.

01:52:34.260 --> 01:52:39.180
The walls of his palace were starting to look
awfully drab and he gestured to one covered

01:52:39.180 --> 01:52:40.800
with a rusty red streak.

01:52:40.800 --> 01:52:45.540
Maxwell remembered that D-Class cleaners were
sent into the containment cell twice a month

01:52:45.540 --> 01:52:51.300
to tidy any of Fernand’s messes, but they
often ended up becoming one the messes themself.

01:52:51.300 --> 01:52:56.580
The creature encouraged Maxwell to take a
seat at his oversized dining table, while

01:52:56.580 --> 01:53:00.060
he tended to a pot of what he said was full
of delicious onion soup.

01:53:00.060 --> 01:53:05.160
Maxwell obliged his host’s request and took
a seat at a huge chair that made him look

01:53:05.160 --> 01:53:07.440
like a six-year-old sitting at the grownups’
table.

01:53:07.440 --> 01:53:13.860
Meanwhile, Fernand was using a huge machete-like
knife to cleave onions in half for his bubbling

01:53:13.860 --> 01:53:14.700
pot of stew.

01:53:14.700 --> 01:53:19.560
Even though Fernand had shown no signs of
outward aggression, as he watched the Cannibal

01:53:19.560 --> 01:53:25.140
hack away at onions with his enormous knife,
Maxwell could feel himself beginning to sweat.

01:53:25.140 --> 01:53:29.760
After all, they didn’t call this creature
“The Cannibal” for nothing – this was

01:53:29.760 --> 01:53:32.460
a monster with a truly horrifying body count.

01:53:32.460 --> 01:53:37.260
During previous containment breaches it had
taken enough tranquilizer to put down two

01:53:37.260 --> 01:53:42.120
elephants to subdue the creature, but not
before multiple agents quite literally lost

01:53:42.120 --> 01:53:43.560
their heads in the process.

01:53:43.560 --> 01:53:49.140
Fernand was able to bite them off with one
huge chomp, like he was eating a drumstick,

01:53:49.140 --> 01:53:53.160
snapping right through bone with his incredible
tooth and jaw strength

01:53:53.160 --> 01:53:57.900
Surprisingly when he wasn’t on a violent
rampage, foundation researchers had found

01:53:57.900 --> 01:54:03.720
SCP-082 to be unusually polite and forthcoming,
offering the researchers plenty of information

01:54:03.720 --> 01:54:05.760
about himself and his past.

01:54:06.420 --> 01:54:11.460
The only problem was that almost everything
the creature said was a complete lie.

01:54:11.460 --> 01:54:16.380
From his time as a researcher, Maxwell knew
that there were only a few details about the

01:54:16.380 --> 01:54:22.080
creature that could be ascertained for certain
- SCP-082 would reliably answer to the name

01:54:22.080 --> 01:54:25.560
“Fernand”, and genetically, Fernand was
technically human.

01:54:25.560 --> 01:54:32.280
The means by which Fernand became so grotesquely
huge, strong, and cannibalistic are still

01:54:32.280 --> 01:54:37.020
unknown – Foundation personnel are still
looking into whether it’s due to some kind

01:54:37.020 --> 01:54:41.280
of anomalous genetic mutation, or by more
supernatural means.

01:54:41.280 --> 01:54:46.920
All we know is that he’s big, unpredictable,
and extremely dangerous.

01:54:46.920 --> 01:54:53.520
Dr. Robert Maxwell sat, terrified, at the
dining table of SCP – 082, listening to

01:54:53.520 --> 01:54:57.660
Fernand’s slightly dull blade chop through
the final onion, which he then tossed into

01:54:57.660 --> 01:54:58.500
the boiling soup.

01:54:59.100 --> 01:55:03.360
Fernand had switched the topic of conversation
to one of his favorite fictional characters

01:55:03.360 --> 01:55:05.100
– Hannibal Lecter.

01:55:05.100 --> 01:55:09.300
Of course, Hannibal the Cannibal isn’t quite
so fictional to Fernand.

01:55:09.300 --> 01:55:14.220
While he’s been shown to be extremely intelligent
in terms of puzzle-solving and memory, he

01:55:14.220 --> 01:55:18.480
seems to have no understanding of the distinction
between fiction and reality.

01:55:18.480 --> 01:55:23.880
He assumes all movies and TV shows are a form
of documentary or reality television.

01:55:23.880 --> 01:55:29.640
And ever since seeing The Silence of the Lambs,
Fernand has been eager to meet with Dr. Lecter,

01:55:29.640 --> 01:55:32.520
which he emphasized to Maxwell over and over.

01:55:32.520 --> 01:55:37.920
Since trying to explain the concept of fiction
to Fernand has never previously worked, Maxwell

01:55:37.920 --> 01:55:42.540
simply told him that Dr. Lecter is extremely
busy at the moment, but will visit whenever

01:55:42.540 --> 01:55:43.440
he gets a chance.

01:55:43.440 --> 01:55:48.720
This seemed to satisfy Fernand, who placed
two large bowls of steaming soup on the table

01:55:48.720 --> 01:55:51.600
before sitting down a little too close to
Maxwell.

01:55:51.600 --> 01:55:55.920
He couldn’t help but notice that the giant
cannibal was now sitting within biting distance,

01:55:55.920 --> 01:56:01.860
and as a lowly D-Class, nobody would be rushing
in to save him if things went south.

01:56:01.860 --> 01:56:06.780
Fernand began ranting through his clenched
teeth once more, occasionally stopping to

01:56:06.780 --> 01:56:08.940
consume a hefty spoonful of onion soup.

01:56:08.940 --> 01:56:13.620
Maxwell was sure to do the same, not wanting
to seem anything less than polite.

01:56:13.620 --> 01:56:17.100
But soon, the tenor of Fernand’s rant began
to shift.

01:56:17.100 --> 01:56:20.760
Typically, the monster spoke French or heavily
accented English.

01:56:21.480 --> 01:56:26.400
Now, he was affecting the accent of a Victorian
gentleman, peppering his speech with “tally

01:56:26.400 --> 01:56:28.380
ho” and “the game is afoot.”

01:56:28.380 --> 01:56:33.960
Maxwell was confused at first, but quickly
realized the game Fernand was playing.

01:56:33.960 --> 01:56:38.760
It’s well known that Fernand is a pathological
liar who likes to play numerous characters,

01:56:38.760 --> 01:56:42.120
changing his mannerisms and clothes accordingly.

01:56:42.120 --> 01:56:48.600
These personas have included: A vampire, Big
Bird, André the Giant, Foundation researcher

01:56:48.600 --> 01:56:54.660
Dr. Bright, The Incredible Hulk, Alexander
The Great, Captain Hook, Dr. Frankenstein,

01:56:54.660 --> 01:56:56.280
and Frankenstein's Monster.

01:56:56.280 --> 01:57:03.180
And of course, in this case, the iconic fictional
detective Sherlock Holmes.

01:57:03.180 --> 01:57:09.300
Fearing for his life in this strange situation,
Dr. Maxwell did the only thing he could - Play

01:57:09.300 --> 01:57:09.600
along.

01:57:09.600 --> 01:57:14.700
As Fernand reeled off his Holmesian delusions,
Maxwell began to play the role of Dr. John

01:57:14.700 --> 01:57:17.700
Watson, asking follow-up&nbsp;
questions and complimenting&nbsp;

01:57:17.700 --> 01:57:19.860
Fernand’s “impeccable” deductive reasoning.

01:57:19.860 --> 01:57:25.200
And it seemed to be working – Fernand played
along too, acting as though the two of them

01:57:25.200 --> 01:57:27.960
really were Arthur Conan Doyle’s crime-fighting
duo.

01:57:27.960 --> 01:57:33.240
Towards the end of their game, Dr. Maxwell
was even starting to enjoy it, amazed that

01:57:33.240 --> 01:57:35.700
his quick thinking was actually keeping him
safe.

01:57:35.700 --> 01:57:39.720
But just then the Cannibal froze, as if in
a trance.

01:57:39.720 --> 01:57:44.760
He locked eyes with Dr. Maxwell – like a
mad dog, that you can’t tell if it’s going

01:57:44.760 --> 01:57:45.720
to bite you or not.

01:57:45.720 --> 01:57:50.940
He saw the creature’s gargantuan teeth separating,
its huge jaws stretching open.

01:57:50.940 --> 01:57:53.820
This could surely only mean one thing.

01:57:53.820 --> 01:57:59.760
Dr. Maxwell winced and prepared for death,
cursing that all his quick thinking had amounted

01:57:59.760 --> 01:58:00.480
to nothing.

01:58:01.080 --> 01:58:06.300
Fernand leaned towards him, his gaping maw
with its hot onion scented breath just inches

01:58:06.300 --> 01:58:07.500
away from Maxwell.

01:58:07.500 --> 01:58:14.400
And then… he began to sing – the Cannibal
broke into a raucous Victorian pub song, happy

01:58:14.400 --> 01:58:15.240
and jovial.

01:58:15.240 --> 01:58:21.540
In his moment of terror, Dr. Maxwell had forgotten
that this was the other reason SCP – 082

01:58:21.540 --> 01:58:23.340
opens his nightmarish jaws.

01:58:23.340 --> 01:58:28.680
Relief washed over him, as he knew he was
safe, at least for a moment.

01:58:29.460 --> 01:58:34.980
Not long after, foundation guards arrived
and escorted him from the cell, leaving the

01:58:34.980 --> 01:58:39.000
delusional giant to his own devices back in
the so-called palace.

01:58:39.660 --> 01:58:44.280
The former researcher had done it, he had
bested Fernand the Cannibal and hopefully

01:58:44.280 --> 01:58:49.140
it would be the last time he’d ever be face
to face with that deranged giant.

01:58:49.140 --> 01:58:54.360
Unfortunately for Dr. Robert Maxwell, in a
performance review later that week, one of

01:58:54.360 --> 01:58:58.380
his superiors remarked that Fernand enjoyed
his company and he had done a great job.

01:58:58.380 --> 01:59:05.460
Such a good job in fact, that Fernand insisted
he have Dr. Maxwell for dinner... or any other

01:59:05.460 --> 01:59:09.780
meal for that matter... sometime very soon.

01:59:09.780 --> 01:59:15.300
A veteran worker of the SCP Foundation sits
at his terminal, performing one of the most

01:59:15.300 --> 01:59:20.940
critical tasks in the entire organization
- creating a file for an as yet undescribed

01:59:20.940 --> 01:59:21.660
SCP.

01:59:21.660 --> 01:59:23.760
But there’s something terribly wrong.

01:59:23.760 --> 01:59:30.600
His eyes are glazed over, his mouth hangs
open - is this a zombie or a trained foundation

01:59:30.600 --> 01:59:31.260
researcher?

01:59:31.920 --> 01:59:33.120
What is going on?

01:59:33.120 --> 01:59:38.340
Like any large international organization,
it takes more than just the exciting, action

01:59:38.340 --> 01:59:41.820
filled jobs to keep the wheels turning at
the SCP Foundation.

01:59:41.820 --> 01:59:47.040
Sure, the head researchers, guards, mobile
task force soldiers, and members of the O5

01:59:47.040 --> 01:59:52.500
Command get all the praise, but a legion of
number crunchers, cleaners, and paper pushers

01:59:52.500 --> 01:59:53.940
are equally important.

01:59:53.940 --> 01:59:59.580
One such person was archivist Walter Bainbridge,
who had been tasked with digitizing some of

01:59:59.580 --> 02:00:02.280
the older records that the Foundation had
on file.

02:00:02.280 --> 02:00:10.140
It was when he was innocently recording the
details on SCP - 050 through 060 that he first

02:00:10.140 --> 02:00:15.000
came under the strange and startling effects
of SCP - 055.

02:00:15.000 --> 02:00:18.840
But, the most peculiar&nbsp;
part, as with all incidences&nbsp;

02:00:18.840 --> 02:00:21.900
of SCP - 055’s anomalous effects taking

02:00:21.900 --> 02:00:26.340
hold, is that Walter had no idea any of it
was happening.

02:00:26.340 --> 02:00:31.860
In his new digitized filing system, he first
took note of SCP - 053.

02:00:31.860 --> 02:00:37.560
Euclid Class, also known as the Young Girl,
this anomaly was a seemingly normal human

02:00:37.560 --> 02:00:42.600
female child who provoked homicidal insanity
in those directly exposed to her.

02:00:42.600 --> 02:00:44.820
Then SCP - 054.

02:00:44.820 --> 02:00:51.420
Safe Class, a non-aggressive humanoid female
made entirely of, as well as biologically

02:00:51.420 --> 02:00:54.540
and chemically identical to regular spring
water.

02:00:54.540 --> 02:00:57.240
Next, SCP - 056.

02:00:57.240 --> 02:01:03.300
Euclid Class, a being that changes form to
suit its environment, but only when all observers

02:01:03.300 --> 02:01:04.440
lose focus on it.

02:01:04.440 --> 02:01:07.560
And then SCP - 057.

02:01:07.560 --> 02:01:13.020
Safe Class, an underground chamber that crushes
the humans who walk within.

02:01:13.020 --> 02:01:17.160
It was at this point that Walter received
a concerned message from one of his superiors

02:01:17.160 --> 02:01:19.320
at Site-19, Mr. Kovach.

02:01:19.320 --> 02:01:24.000
The message praised the thorough digitization
of the other anomalies’ records, but was

02:01:24.000 --> 02:01:28.380
confused about why Walter had left out any
mention of SCP - 055.

02:01:28.380 --> 02:01:30.720
Immediately, Walter was embarrassed.

02:01:30.720 --> 02:01:33.840
How could he have forgotten SCP - 055?

02:01:33.840 --> 02:01:40.560
That iconic anomaly known for...Well, he couldn’t
quite say, off the top of his head, but he’d

02:01:40.560 --> 02:01:41.760
be sure to look into it.

02:01:41.760 --> 02:01:46.440
A quick trip to the Site 19 Archives showed
him that there was actually quite a hefty

02:01:46.440 --> 02:01:52.680
file on the nature of SCP - 055, which must
have been the result of a huge number of studies.

02:01:52.680 --> 02:01:57.780
What struck him as strange was that all the
files were filled out in pen rather than being

02:01:57.780 --> 02:01:59.640
typed up, like a traditional file.

02:01:59.640 --> 02:02:04.440
The majority of these notes were written in
short-hand, too, as though they were frantically

02:02:04.440 --> 02:02:07.800
taken during the tests themselves on extremely
short notice.

02:02:08.340 --> 02:02:10.620
There weren’t even any redactions.

02:02:10.620 --> 02:02:15.480
Walter made a mental note of what he had seen,
put the file back in its proper place, and

02:02:15.480 --> 02:02:17.040
headed back to his computer terminal.

02:02:17.040 --> 02:02:22.200
However, after writing in an almost trancelike
state, he looked back on his work to see that

02:02:22.200 --> 02:02:29.700
he had written an entry on SCP - 058, a giant,
evil bovine heart with insect legs and a scorpion

02:02:29.700 --> 02:02:30.240
stinger…

02:02:30.240 --> 02:02:32.340
Strange, he thought.

02:02:32.340 --> 02:02:37.380
That’s when Walter got a call from Mr. Kovach
on his Foundation-issue phone, and he didn’t

02:02:37.380 --> 02:02:38.100
sound happy.

02:02:38.100 --> 02:02:44.460
He’d given Walter direct instructions to
go back and digitize the files on 055, and

02:02:44.460 --> 02:02:46.620
instead, he’d been working on 058.

02:02:46.620 --> 02:02:48.060
What was the meaning of this?

02:02:48.060 --> 02:02:53.220
Walter was typically an extremely loyal and
diligent employee, but the verbal barrage

02:02:53.220 --> 02:02:58.500
from his supervisor had him considering talking
back, just this once, and hoping it didn’t

02:02:58.500 --> 02:03:03.060
get him demoted to D-Class and thrown into
682’s acid bath for play time.

02:03:03.060 --> 02:03:08.280
Walter gulped, picked up some courage, and
interrupted Mr. Kovach’s rant to ask if

02:03:08.280 --> 02:03:12.420
he had any idea what SCP - 055 actually was.

02:03:12.420 --> 02:03:18.660
The line went silent for a moment, then the
supervisor spoke again, this time with less

02:03:18.660 --> 02:03:19.140
confidence.

02:03:19.140 --> 02:03:23.220
“Of course I can tell you about SCP - 055.

02:03:23.220 --> 02:03:26.460
It’s a classic, one of the first hundred.

02:03:26.460 --> 02:03:33.960
How could you forget its...Or, um, you know,
its...I think it’s the one with the...”

02:03:34.980 --> 02:03:40.860
Another long pause, as Mr. Kovach seemed to
search for the words, but instead just trailed

02:03:40.860 --> 02:03:41.820
off into silence.

02:03:41.820 --> 02:03:46.680
Knowing that some of the anomalies on file
were dangerous memetic hazards, Walter was

02:03:46.680 --> 02:03:51.180
worried for a moment that he may have accidentally
killed his boss by getting him to think too

02:03:51.180 --> 02:03:53.400
hard about SCP - 055.

02:03:53.400 --> 02:03:57.840
He asked if Mr. Kovach was okay, and finally
got a reply.

02:03:58.440 --> 02:04:01.020
“I’m sorry, I seem to have zoned out for
a second there.

02:04:01.020 --> 02:04:02.520
What were we talking about, again?”

02:04:03.060 --> 02:04:05.700
But this time, it was Walter who couldn't
answer.

02:04:05.700 --> 02:04:10.380
He had no idea at all what the two of them
were discussing just moments ago.

02:04:10.380 --> 02:04:15.660
He felt disoriented and kind of sick, like
they’d taken some low-level amnestics.

02:04:15.660 --> 02:04:20.040
Mr. Kovach told Walter to get back to his
filing duties and they’d speak later.

02:04:20.040 --> 02:04:24.900
Walter then checked the messages he’d received
from Mr. Kovach earlier, and there it was,

02:04:24.900 --> 02:04:27.780
plain as day: “You missed 055.

02:04:27.780 --> 02:04:30.450
Go back and digitize that before proceeding.

02:04:30.450 --> 02:04:31.680
- Mr. K.”

02:04:31.680 --> 02:04:37.620
But Walter had never even heard of an SCP
- 055, if such an anomaly even existed!

02:04:38.220 --> 02:04:39.660
What was going on here?

02:04:39.660 --> 02:04:45.060
In that moment, Walter realized he was dealing
with something much stranger than just a standard

02:04:45.060 --> 02:04:46.200
digitization job.

02:04:46.200 --> 02:04:52.500
After all, how could he properly complete
his duties if SCP - 055 seemed to be impossible

02:04:52.500 --> 02:04:58.260
to speak, write, or even think about, unless
you were directly observing it at that moment?

02:04:58.260 --> 02:05:04.800
Walter had to know, and ask around the entirety
of Site 19 to find the answers if he had to.

02:05:05.460 --> 02:05:10.740
Sadly for Walter, he was about to embark on
a much more challenging task than he could

02:05:10.740 --> 02:05:11.760
have ever imagined.

02:05:11.760 --> 02:05:16.980
To paraphrase a supposed quote from Socrates,
“All I know is that I know nothing.”

02:05:16.980 --> 02:05:23.100
And that’s also about the extent of the
knowledge we have on SCP - 055, also known

02:05:23.100 --> 02:05:25.740
as The Anti-Meme and the Self-Keeping Secret.

02:05:25.740 --> 02:05:27.120
What does it look like?

02:05:27.120 --> 02:05:30.120
When and how was it obtained by the Foundation?

02:05:30.120 --> 02:05:32.040
What are its anomalous abilities?

02:05:32.040 --> 02:05:33.960
Is this thing dangerous?

02:05:33.960 --> 02:05:40.380
We may never know, because the only anomalous
ability of SCP - 055 that we’re aware of

02:05:40.380 --> 02:05:44.580
is the fact that nobody is capable of retaining
any information about it.

02:05:44.580 --> 02:05:51.360
It’s crucial to note that, whatever 055
is, it isn’t invisible, or indescribable.

02:05:51.360 --> 02:05:56.760
Foundation personnel are perfectly capable
of entering its containment chamber and observing

02:05:56.760 --> 02:05:59.040
it without incident, but mere minutes after&nbsp;

02:05:59.040 --> 02:06:02.040
leaving the chamber, any&nbsp;
memories of the particulars

02:06:02.040 --> 02:06:05.580
of 055 seem to spontaneously erase themselves.

02:06:06.180 --> 02:06:08.760
Hence, the Self-Keeping Secret.

02:06:08.760 --> 02:06:10.740
But this didn’t deter Walter.

02:06:10.740 --> 02:06:14.700
Perhaps his greatest advantage was that he
didn’t know enough about the thing he was

02:06:14.700 --> 02:06:17.640
investigating to know how futile his mission
was.

02:06:17.640 --> 02:06:22.920
He wanted to know the unknowable, and a pesky
issue like “impossibility” wouldn’t

02:06:22.920 --> 02:06:23.580
stop him.

02:06:23.580 --> 02:06:28.320
He’d get to whoever he needed to at Site
19 to get the answers he needed.

02:06:28.320 --> 02:06:32.100
Of course most people had no knowledge of
the mysterious anomaly.

02:06:32.100 --> 02:06:34.860
The common response he got&nbsp;
back from his colleagues&nbsp;

02:06:34.860 --> 02:06:36.360
was, “055?

02:06:36.360 --> 02:06:38.100
Do we even have an 055?”

02:06:38.100 --> 02:06:43.320
While the realization of sudden memory loss
- or the realization of 055’s existence

02:06:43.320 --> 02:06:49.380
- has been known to cause momentary stress,
there are no known long term physical or mental

02:06:49.380 --> 02:06:51.960
effects from 055’s anomalous abilities.

02:06:51.960 --> 02:06:57.600
It’s a fleeting idea in its purest form
- like forgetting why you walked into a room.

02:06:57.600 --> 02:07:04.200
055 could be the most harmless object on the
Foundation’s roster, or the most deadly.

02:07:04.200 --> 02:07:07.140
Either way, we just don’t know.

02:07:07.140 --> 02:07:10.440
At times, Walter worried he was going insane.

02:07:10.440 --> 02:07:14.520
055, and everything related to it, was gaslighting
him.

02:07:14.520 --> 02:07:16.680
Was 055 even real?

02:07:16.680 --> 02:07:22.080
The one thing that proved to him that 055
must have existed is that its containment

02:07:22.080 --> 02:07:23.580
chamber existed.

02:07:24.120 --> 02:07:28.380
According to the official records kept by
the Foundation on the Site 19 Containment

02:07:28.380 --> 02:07:35.580
Facilities, 055 is kept in a “five by five
by two point five meter square room constructed

02:07:35.580 --> 02:07:40.140
of fifty-foot-thick cement, with a Faraday
cage surrounding the cement walls.”

02:07:40.140 --> 02:07:45.900
The report continues that, “Access is via
a heavy containment door measuring two by

02:07:45.900 --> 02:07:51.420
two point five meters constructed on bearings
to ensure door closes and locks automatically

02:07:51.420 --> 02:07:53.040
unless held open deliberately.”

02:07:53.700 --> 02:07:59.280
055’s cell is one of the few to have no
posted security guards, and any personnel

02:07:59.280 --> 02:08:04.380
working on other SCPs in the area are ordered
to remain at least fifty feet from the geometric

02:08:04.380 --> 02:08:08.880
center of 055’s cell, where the anomaly
itself is kept.

02:08:08.880 --> 02:08:13.860
When he tried to explore further why the cell
was constructed in this manner, he found that

02:08:13.860 --> 02:08:16.920
- surprise, surprise - nobody knew.

02:08:16.920 --> 02:08:23.520
055 was an anomaly whose containment requirements
were so mysterious that it automatically netted

02:08:23.520 --> 02:08:25.260
itself a Keter Class designation.

02:08:25.260 --> 02:08:30.780
After all, how can you properly contain something
you can’t even hope to comprehend?

02:08:30.780 --> 02:08:34.320
There were plenty of rumors about the true
nature of 055.

02:08:35.160 --> 02:08:41.580
Some of the more conspiratorial minds at Site
19 theorized that 055 was actually an autonomous

02:08:41.580 --> 02:08:47.700
or remotely controlled spy inserted into the
site to observe Foundation operations - or

02:08:47.700 --> 02:08:49.380
even humanity as a whole.

02:08:49.380 --> 02:08:54.060
If you’re on the more paranoid end of the
psychological spectrum, this theory makes

02:08:54.060 --> 02:08:54.840
total sense.

02:08:54.840 --> 02:08:59.340
An anomaly that’s physically impossible
to remember, even when writings and pictures

02:08:59.340 --> 02:09:02.460
on the subject exist, would be a perfect spy.

02:09:02.460 --> 02:09:06.300
However, this was all ultimately little more
than speculation.

02:09:06.300 --> 02:09:10.020
Walter was barely any further along than when
he started.

02:09:10.020 --> 02:09:14.760
There were multiple points in his investigation
where Walter seriously considered giving up,

02:09:15.420 --> 02:09:18.480
until, finally, he had a major breakthrough.

02:09:18.480 --> 02:09:24.300
Dr. Bartholomew Hughes and Dr. John Marachek
were two scientists that had performed extensive

02:09:24.300 --> 02:09:30.120
research into 055, and who - Walter hoped
- might have the answers he sought about the

02:09:30.120 --> 02:09:31.200
Self-Keeping Secret.

02:09:31.200 --> 02:09:37.080
These scientists were the first to discover
the “Anti-Memetic” nature of 055, performing

02:09:37.080 --> 02:09:41.700
numerous tests on D-Class personnel to see
if it was possible to create feasible written

02:09:41.700 --> 02:09:47.460
records, sketches, or any other records or
impressions that could bypass its anomalous

02:09:47.460 --> 02:09:47.940
effects.

02:09:47.940 --> 02:09:54.660
The disorienting, memory-ruining effects of
055 also extend to any materials concerning

02:09:54.660 --> 02:09:55.680
055.

02:09:55.680 --> 02:10:01.440
It seemed to be a truly uncrackable code,
but Dr. Hughes may have finally found some

02:10:01.440 --> 02:10:02.580
cracks in the armor.

02:10:03.240 --> 02:10:09.360
For starters, the fact we’re able to remember
that 055 is Anti-Memetic is an ironic exception

02:10:09.360 --> 02:10:11.040
to its Anti-Memetic qualities.

02:10:11.040 --> 02:10:17.700
This revelation also inspired another realization
from Dr. Hughes: Would it be possible to discover

02:10:17.700 --> 02:10:23.160
more about 055 from the process of deduction
rather than the typical induction?

02:10:23.160 --> 02:10:29.280
In other words, could they possibly learn
about 055 by figuring out all the things it

02:10:29.280 --> 02:10:31.560
isn’t rather than what it is?

02:10:31.560 --> 02:10:36.360
Dr. Marachek designed an experiment with Dr.
Hughes to explore this theory.

02:10:36.360 --> 02:10:42.000
They designed the experiment around a simple
question: Is 055 not spherical?

02:10:42.000 --> 02:10:47.820
In designing the question to specifically
find out what 055 isn’t, they hoped to subvert

02:10:47.820 --> 02:10:49.800
the anomaly’s Anti-Memetic Powers.

02:10:49.800 --> 02:10:53.700
Walter was fascinated by this potential method
of getting answers.

02:10:53.700 --> 02:10:58.560
Marachek and Hughes found that, while the
questioning process for those exposed was

02:10:58.560 --> 02:11:05.940
often arduous and frustrating, they could
now definitely say that 055 is not a sphere.

02:11:05.940 --> 02:11:12.360
It is theoretically possible to discover the
true nature of 055 by an almost endless barrage

02:11:12.360 --> 02:11:17.820
of deductive questions, though whether command
would authorize the resources for such extensive

02:11:17.820 --> 02:11:20.040
testing is still an open question.

02:11:20.040 --> 02:11:26.280
Walter, in his desperation, begged Marachek
and Hughes for clearance to view 055 himself.

02:11:26.280 --> 02:11:31.380
The curiosity had become too great during
his search to just walk away with the single

02:11:31.380 --> 02:11:33.840
fact that 055 wasn’t spherical.

02:11:33.840 --> 02:11:35.880
He needed to see this thing.

02:11:35.880 --> 02:11:41.700
And after several weeks of filling out forms
and cutting red tape, his wish was finally

02:11:41.700 --> 02:11:42.420
granted.

02:11:42.420 --> 02:11:49.980
Walter Bainbridge was allowed a private audience
with SCP - 055, the subject of his months-long

02:11:49.980 --> 02:11:50.460
obsession.

02:11:50.460 --> 02:11:55.800
Outsiders observed that Walter spent just
over an hour in the containment chamber, taking

02:11:55.800 --> 02:12:01.200
photos, drawing sketches, writing down notes,
recording audio logs, and reciting memory

02:12:01.200 --> 02:12:01.800
mnemonics.

02:12:01.800 --> 02:12:07.200
He was pulling out every stop to counteract
the anti-memetic effects of the Self-Keeping

02:12:07.200 --> 02:12:07.500
Secret.

02:12:07.500 --> 02:12:13.860
He was adamant that he would not be defeated
by his non-spherical nemesis, not after all

02:12:13.860 --> 02:12:14.880
this time and effort.

02:12:14.880 --> 02:12:20.520
Once his time in the 055 containment chamber
was over, he retired back to his office to

02:12:20.520 --> 02:12:25.860
finally digitize his exhaustive findings,
so that his supervisor, Mr. Kovach, would

02:12:25.860 --> 02:12:27.120
finally get off his back.

02:12:27.120 --> 02:12:31.260
Walter smiled, took a deep breath, and began
to type.

02:12:31.260 --> 02:12:33.600
“SCP - 059.

02:12:33.600 --> 02:12:34.620
Keter Class.

02:12:34.620 --> 02:12:39.840
This anomaly is a radioactive mineral that
emits a unique radiation known as Delta Radiation.

02:12:39.840 --> 02:12:44.280
Exposure to this radiation has caused strange
fungal growths on the infected...”

02:12:44.280 --> 02:12:47.220
Wait, what was this supposed to be about again?

02:12:47.220 --> 02:12:49.320
Oh well, it couldn’t have been that important.

02:12:49.320 --> 02:12:55.440
The fabric of our world is littered with doorways&nbsp;
if you know where to look for them. Tears,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:12:55.440 --> 02:13:02.880
portals, anomalies, all leading to places and&nbsp;
planes beyond human imagining and understanding,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:13:02.880 --> 02:13:09.600
and SCP-2317, otherwise known as A Door to&nbsp;
Another World, certainly fits that description.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:13:10.260 --> 02:13:13.440
Contained and kept at all times&nbsp;
under the watch of armed guards,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:13:13.440 --> 02:13:20.760
SCP-2317 appears to be a simple and unsuspecting&nbsp;
wooden door in its frame. It hardly looks like it&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:13:20.760 --> 02:13:26.100
requires such extreme round-the-clock security&nbsp;
or needs a strange, secretive ritual that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:13:26.100 --> 02:13:32.400
Foundation performs, presumably to keep the&nbsp;
door closed. But, of course, sometimes the&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:13:32.400 --> 02:13:37.620
most interesting thing about a closed doorway&nbsp;
isn’t where it leads, it’s what it keeps out.&nbsp;

02:13:38.640 --> 02:13:44.340
Even by the Foundation’s already-high standards,&nbsp;
the requirements and regulations for personnel&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:13:44.340 --> 02:13:51.300
who are assigned to SCP-2317 seem oddly specific.&nbsp;
Psychological testing is standard practice for to&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:13:51.300 --> 02:13:55.920
work for the Foundation, but an additional&nbsp;
hurdle that anyone has to clear before even&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:13:55.920 --> 02:14:00.780
getting to glimpse at this unassuming wooden&nbsp;
door is having a score of at least seventy-two&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:14:00.780 --> 02:14:06.840
on the Milgram Obedience Examination. It is also&nbsp;
mandatory that personnel assigned to maintaining&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:14:06.840 --> 02:14:12.000
it are both unmarried, with no children&nbsp;
or next-of-kin, as well as an unwavering,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:14:12.000 --> 02:14:17.700
unquestioning loyalty to the Foundation,&nbsp;
pure devotion to its code and objectives.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:14:18.480 --> 02:14:25.560
These may seem like strange requirements,&nbsp;
after all, SCP-2317 is just a door…isn’t it?&nbsp;

02:14:26.640 --> 02:14:31.920
Perhaps there’s a reason that the Foundation&nbsp;
keeps so much of the information about SCP-2317&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:14:31.920 --> 02:14:37.740
buried deep under layers upon layers of security,&nbsp;
with only the Overseer Council privy to the full&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:14:37.740 --> 02:14:45.180
details of its strange nature. Knowledge, as they&nbsp;
say, is power - but maybe knowing too much about&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:14:45.180 --> 02:14:52.440
whatever is behind that door can prove deadly.&nbsp;
Still, if SCP-2317 is a Door to Another World,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:14:52.440 --> 02:14:58.380
an alternate dimension or parallel reality,&nbsp;
it must be safe enough to visit. After all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:14:58.380 --> 02:15:03.120
the Foundation has been sending personnel&nbsp;
in there on a regular basis. Daily, in fact.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:15:04.200 --> 02:15:08.160
According to the O5 Council, this&nbsp;
is done as part of a procedure to&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:15:08.160 --> 02:15:14.220
maintain Active Containment of…something&nbsp;
lurking beyond that old wooden doorframe.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:15:14.880 --> 02:15:18.360
But what could possibly warrant such&nbsp;
constant maintenance and surveillance?&nbsp;

02:15:19.860 --> 02:15:24.720
In accordance with the Foundation’s guidelines,&nbsp;
all staff are required to rotate out of observing&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:15:24.720 --> 02:15:30.600
SCP-2317 after every two months and spend the&nbsp;
following third month in full psychological&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:15:30.600 --> 02:15:34.800
counselling before they are permitted to&nbsp;
return to the containment unit housing the&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:15:34.800 --> 02:15:39.900
Door to Another World. It was after one of&nbsp;
these month-long periods of evaluation that&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:15:39.900 --> 02:15:45.540
a Foundation guard was informed that his security&nbsp;
clearance had been raised to Level 3 and that he’d&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:15:45.540 --> 02:15:50.520
been selected for the duty of carrying out&nbsp;
220-Calabasas. He knew the name instantly;&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:15:51.180 --> 02:15:56.280
this was the title given to the daily containment&nbsp;
procedure that absolutely had to be carried out.&nbsp;

02:15:57.240 --> 02:16:01.680
The guard didn’t question these orders, after&nbsp;
all, he’d been selected precisely because of&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:16:01.680 --> 02:16:06.660
his loyalty to the Foundation. He did make one&nbsp;
request to his commanding officer, however:&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:16:07.320 --> 02:16:11.040
he wanted to know what had happened to the&nbsp;
last guard that had performed the procedure.&nbsp;

02:16:12.000 --> 02:16:16.080
“Didn’t make it out of psychological&nbsp;
evaluation,” the officer replied.&nbsp;

02:16:16.980 --> 02:16:22.500
Not letting this affect his dedication, the guard&nbsp;
was told to prepare for Procedure 220-Calabasas.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:16:23.100 --> 02:16:28.260
Along with a fellow member of Foundation security&nbsp;
personnel, the guard was instructed to gather&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:16:28.260 --> 02:16:33.600
everything on a strange list. The first was&nbsp;
a pre-selected member of Class-D Personnel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:16:34.200 --> 02:16:39.179
specifically a convicted murderer. Class-D&nbsp;
refers to ‘Disposable Class’ personnel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:16:39.180 --> 02:16:44.821
expendable individuals recruited by the&nbsp;
Foundation for the sole purpose of testing SCPs.&nbsp;

02:16:45.899 --> 02:16:50.939
Class-Ds were usually prison inmates&nbsp;
repurposed for SCP testing, and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:16:50.939 --> 02:16:56.519
one chosen for 220-Calabasas was no exception,&nbsp;
serving multiple life sentences for murders,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:16:56.520 --> 02:17:00.541
or at least that was what the guard&nbsp;
had been told. A Foundation personnel&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:17:00.540 --> 02:17:04.800
member instructed him to refer to the Class-D&nbsp;
solely as the ‘assistant’ from that point on.&nbsp;

02:17:05.520 --> 02:17:09.420
Next, the guard collected a live&nbsp;
chicken, an obsidian-edged knife,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:17:09.420 --> 02:17:15.359
a silver aspergillum and aspersorium, to be&nbsp;
filled with 500ccs of Holy Water that had&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:17:15.359 --> 02:17:21.719
been blessed by a priest of the Abrahamic faith,&nbsp;
and finally a one-kiloton nuclear device, which,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:17:21.720 --> 02:17:25.920
according to instructions, was to only&nbsp;
be detonated in the unlikely event of a&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:17:25.920 --> 02:17:29.700
catastrophic containment failure.&nbsp;
In other words, the last resort.&nbsp;

02:17:31.320 --> 02:17:36.479
After following his instructions to the letter and&nbsp;
without question, the guard and his colleague were&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:17:36.479 --> 02:17:41.040
briefed. The Foundation personnel member informed&nbsp;
them that he’d be joining and leading them in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:17:41.040 --> 02:17:46.200
procedure. The staff member also specified that&nbsp;
henceforth he be referred to as the ‘celebrant’&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:17:46.200 --> 02:17:51.899
until the completion of 220-Calabasas. The&nbsp;
guard was acutely aware of how specific these&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:17:51.899 --> 02:17:56.939
instructions were, but trusted in the Foundation,&nbsp;
knowing that if they wanted this procedure&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:17:56.939 --> 02:18:01.679
performed a certain way, then it was in everyones’&nbsp;
best interest to carry out the orders to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:18:01.680 --> 02:18:08.580
letter. But what the celebrant then went on to&nbsp;
explain, raised far more questions about SCP-2317&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:18:08.580 --> 02:18:16.680
and the nature of Procedure 220-Calabasas. The&nbsp;
Class-D joining them, wasn’t actually a Class-D.&nbsp;

02:18:17.460 --> 02:18:22.200
The assistant, as they were now referred to,&nbsp;
was in reality another Foundation staff member,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:18:22.200 --> 02:18:29.519
with a Level 4 security clearance, specifically&nbsp;
tailored to SCP-2317. Every member of staff&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:18:29.520 --> 02:18:36.060
entering through SCP-2317 and taking an active&nbsp;
role in 220-Calabasas needed to be informed that&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:18:36.060 --> 02:18:41.581
this assistant was not to be harmed or treated&nbsp;
as a member of Disposable Class. Fighting back&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:18:41.580 --> 02:18:46.920
the nagging question of why the Foundation would&nbsp;
employ this subterfuge, the guard, along with&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:18:46.920 --> 02:18:51.780
his fellow security officer, the celebrant and&nbsp;
assistant, prepared for their departure through&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:18:51.780 --> 02:18:59.820
the Door to Another World at solar noon, when&nbsp;
the sun was highest over SCP-2317. Solar noon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:18:59.820 --> 02:19:05.639
chickens and holy water, this all seemed like&nbsp;
an oddly-occult combination for the Foundation.&nbsp;

02:19:06.540 --> 02:19:11.340
As they entered the old wooden door, beyond&nbsp;
lay a barren salt plane, stretching out for&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:19:11.340 --> 02:19:16.620
kilometers in every direction. This alternate&nbsp;
dimension, according to the briefing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:19:16.620 --> 02:19:22.859
was designated SCP-2317-Prime. The guard&nbsp;
immediately noticed a ring of seven pillars&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:19:22.859 --> 02:19:28.019
directly ahead of the group as they entered, each&nbsp;
of them bearing intricately-detailed engravings&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:19:28.020 --> 02:19:34.680
unlike anything from any era of ancient history.
Procedure 220-Calabasas was carried out quickly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:19:34.680 --> 02:19:40.020
but carefully, the guard watching as the celebrant&nbsp;
and assistant were careful not to miss a step.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:19:40.979 --> 02:19:44.639
First, the celebrant scattered Holy Water&nbsp;
into the center of the pillars with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:19:44.640 --> 02:19:49.860
aspergillum and aspersorium, looking down&nbsp;
at his feet and keeping a steady pace as he&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:19:49.859 --> 02:19:55.019
stepped counter-clockwise around them. The guard&nbsp;
watched intently as the celebrant completed his&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:19:55.020 --> 02:20:00.000
circuit around the pillars and turned to the&nbsp;
assistant, anointing his head with Holy Water.&nbsp;

02:20:00.600 --> 02:20:07.621
“Seven Seals, Seven Rings, Seven Thrones&nbsp;
for the Scarlet King,” he said aloud.&nbsp;

02:20:08.460 --> 02:20:12.660
The assistant, with the obsidian blade in&nbsp;
his hand, took the chicken and dispatched it&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:20:12.660 --> 02:20:18.479
in sacrifice, letting its blood mix with the&nbsp;
Holy Water. He then repeated the celebrant’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:20:18.479 --> 02:20:22.379
circuit in the opposite direction, before&nbsp;
stepping into the center of the stone pillars.&nbsp;

02:20:23.220 --> 02:20:29.520
“Blood for the Old Gods, Water for the New King,”&nbsp;
the assistant recited, pouring the remaining mix&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:20:29.520 --> 02:20:33.661
of blood and Holy Water over a patch of&nbsp;
salt in the middle of the seven pillars.&nbsp;

02:20:34.560 --> 02:20:39.600
Even though he knew it wasn’t his place to&nbsp;
question the Foundation, as the 220-Calabasas&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:20:39.600 --> 02:20:44.400
procedure took place, the guard couldn’t&nbsp;
help but wonder what all this was for.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:20:45.060 --> 02:20:51.900
It seemed so…ritualistic, like something&nbsp;
deeply religious or even magical. He’d never&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:20:51.899 --> 02:20:55.679
bought into all that occult mumbo-jumbo,&nbsp;
even while working for the Foundation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:20:55.680 --> 02:21:01.860
but he had learned not to question anything, even&nbsp;
the strangest and most inexplicable of sights.&nbsp;

02:21:03.060 --> 02:21:10.741
Little did he know that beneath his feet, was an&nbsp;
ancient and unknowable horror. A beast, chained&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:21:10.740 --> 02:21:16.740
and lying in wait. Contained in a chamber directly&nbsp;
underneath the pillars, sat an impossibly-large&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:21:16.740 --> 02:21:22.679
creature. Humanoid and obese, its body covered&nbsp;
entirely in scales thicker than armour plating.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:21:23.280 --> 02:21:28.439
Branch-like horns protruded from its jawless&nbsp;
head, pointing up to chains that hung from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:21:28.439 --> 02:21:35.280
seven pillars above, each one hooked into the&nbsp;
entity’s back. All but one of the chains was&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:21:35.280 --> 02:21:41.219
broken, a final, withering shackle keeping the&nbsp;
Devourer of Worlds in its underground prison.&nbsp;

02:21:42.000 --> 02:21:48.479
Ever since 1894 BCE, when Erikeshan mystics&nbsp;
imprisoned it, the Devourer has been waiting&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:21:48.479 --> 02:21:54.000
patiently for its inevitable freedom. It knows,&nbsp;
as well as the Foundation, that nothing can be&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:21:54.000 --> 02:22:00.180
done to prevent the final chain from one day&nbsp;
breaking. Even Procedure 220-Calabasas won’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:22:00.180 --> 02:22:06.360
keep the creature contained, it’s nothing more&nbsp;
than a smokescreen, an act, designed to create&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:22:06.359 --> 02:22:11.939
an illusion of active containment and maintain&nbsp;
Foundation morale until a permanent solution&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:22:11.939 --> 02:22:20.639
can be devised to keep SCP-2317 imprisoned.
Of course, if the guard had known this, it would&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:22:20.640 --> 02:22:25.201
have also explained the need for a one-kiloton&nbsp;
nuclear device as part of this staged ritual.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:22:25.859 --> 02:22:31.380
Procedure 220-Calabasas has all the components&nbsp;
to trick everyone below the O5 Council,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:22:31.380 --> 02:22:36.480
emulating religious and occult rituals, the&nbsp;
increased level of security surrounding the&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:22:36.479 --> 02:22:42.179
procedure and its purpose, and telling staff&nbsp;
that any failure to correctly, and completely,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:22:42.180 --> 02:22:49.201
perform the 220-Calabasas procedure will result&nbsp;
in an XK-Class End of the World Scenario.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:22:50.100 --> 02:22:55.380
All these elements work together to conceal&nbsp;
the truth: that one day, the Devourer will&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:22:55.380 --> 02:23:02.580
escape and lay waste to our dimension.
Knowledge is power, and maybe knowing too&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:23:02.580 --> 02:23:08.280
much truly is deadly. Perhaps if the guard had&nbsp;
learned any of this, he’d have understood why&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:23:08.280 --> 02:23:13.679
his predecessor never made it out of psychological&nbsp;
evaluation. Maybe if he had questioned the purpose&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:23:13.680 --> 02:23:21.060
of Procedure 220-Calabasas, he'd have learned the&nbsp;
true nature of SCP-2317, and what that doorway&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:23:21.060 --> 02:23:27.661
kept out. But he was loyal to the Foundation,&nbsp;
through and through. As the team finished&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:23:27.660 --> 02:23:33.359
performing 220-Calabasas and returned though the&nbsp;
wooden door, the guard took one last glance over&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:23:33.359 --> 02:23:40.740
his shoulder at the vast salt plane. The entire&nbsp;
dimension was calm, silent, but not peaceful:&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:23:40.740 --> 02:23:47.460
it was patient. The entity had waited centuries&nbsp;
for its time, and now all it would take was the&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:23:47.460 --> 02:23:54.960
breaking of the seventh and final chain. One day.
The door was closed behind the guard as he,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:23:54.960 --> 02:23:59.580
the celebrant, the assistant and his fellow&nbsp;
security officer stepped back through,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:24:00.600 --> 02:24:06.000
their work done and, as far as they knew,&nbsp;
preventing catastrophe for another day.&nbsp;

02:24:06.899 --> 02:24:12.179
Only the Foundation higher-ups, the Overseer&nbsp;
Council, are aware of the true danger posed&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:24:12.180 --> 02:24:19.320
by SCP-2317 and its sole inhabitant. Current&nbsp;
predictions are that at some point within the&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:24:19.319 --> 02:24:25.439
next thirty years, the Devourer of Worlds will&nbsp;
be freed. Any and all attempts to repair or&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:24:25.439 --> 02:24:32.040
recreate the chains holding it in place have so&nbsp;
far failed. As such, the O5 Council has elected&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:24:32.040 --> 02:24:37.859
to continue providing Foundation personnel with&nbsp;
the ignorant hope that Procedure 220-Calabasas&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:24:37.859 --> 02:24:44.580
is an effective strategy for containment.
As we’ve said, sometimes the most interesting&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:24:44.580 --> 02:24:51.660
thing about a closed door isn’t where it leads,&nbsp;
it’s what it keeps out. In the case of SCP-2317,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:24:51.660 --> 02:24:56.580
the unassuming wooden door holds at bay&nbsp;
an ancient creature of untold power,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:24:57.300 --> 02:25:03.720
that will one day break free and wreak havoc in&nbsp;
our dimension. Nothing the Foundation does can&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:25:03.720 --> 02:25:09.480
prevent it, or keep it contained behind the&nbsp;
Door to Another World, and only the Overseer&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:25:09.479 --> 02:25:15.599
Council knows that any and all efforts to&nbsp;
do so are futile. With all that in mind,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:25:15.600 --> 02:25:23.820
we can only hope that the doorway of SCP-2317&nbsp;
stays closed, at least for a little while longer.

02:25:24.660 --> 02:25:29.099
It was November 3rd, 1991 and Blake Newsom
loved his job.

02:25:29.100 --> 02:25:34.621
He had a passion for organization, an undying
love of American political history, and was

02:25:34.620 --> 02:25:36.420
a life-long member of the Republican party.

02:25:36.420 --> 02:25:39.000
That’s why he took great pride in his position&nbsp;

02:25:39.000 --> 02:25:41.700
as a filing clerk at the&nbsp;
Ronald Reagan Presidential

02:25:41.700 --> 02:25:42.000
Library.

02:25:42.000 --> 02:25:48.060
Or at least, he did, until his horrifying
encounter with SCP – 1981.

02:25:48.060 --> 02:25:51.540
The worst day of Blake’s life began like
any other.

02:25:51.540 --> 02:25:57.060
He was taking inventory of the archive’s
wide array of Betamax tapes, and making sure

02:25:57.060 --> 02:26:00.480
they were all arranged carefully and conformed
with the filing system.

02:26:00.479 --> 02:26:06.479
One by one, he checked footage of speeches
and addresses off of his list, until he came

02:26:06.479 --> 02:26:09.719
upon a strange tape that had no business being
there.

02:26:09.720 --> 02:26:14.460
The tape looked to be completely normal, but
it hadn’t been recorded on the archive inventory.

02:26:14.460 --> 02:26:16.980
And there was something else off about it.

02:26:16.979 --> 02:26:21.359
A single white sticker was on the front of
the tape with “RONALD REGAN CUT UP WHILE

02:26:21.359 --> 02:26:24.540
TALKING" scrawled hastily with what was probably
a felt-tipped marker.

02:26:25.200 --> 02:26:29.399
Blake was shocked and appalled – they hadn’t
even spelled the President’s name correctly!

02:26:30.180 --> 02:26:34.500
What poor Mr. Newsom didn’t know was that
he was about to see something so disturbing

02:26:34.500 --> 02:26:38.819
that he’d look back on that misspelling
like it was a treasured childhood memory.

02:26:39.660 --> 02:26:43.620
Standard policy for tapes like this would
be to review and catalogue, or even throw

02:26:43.620 --> 02:26:44.580
it out if necessary.

02:26:44.580 --> 02:26:49.200
Typically, a lowly filing clerk like Blake
would need to seek approval from his superiors,

02:26:49.200 --> 02:26:51.359
but curiosity got the better of him.

02:26:51.359 --> 02:26:56.219
He commandeered one of the library’s televisions
and Betamax cassette players, and started

02:26:56.220 --> 02:26:57.060
watching the footage.

02:26:57.060 --> 02:27:02.460
For the first minute or so nothing seemed
out of the ordinary, just the president standing

02:27:02.460 --> 02:27:07.680
at a podium giving his iconic “Evil Empire”
speech to the National Association of Evangelicals

02:27:07.680 --> 02:27:12.540
at Sheraton Twin Towers Hotel, Orlando, Florida,
on March 8th, 1983.

02:27:13.319 --> 02:27:18.719
However, the second the tape hit the one minute
and ten seconds mark, something unnatural

02:27:18.720 --> 02:27:19.620
began to occur.

02:27:19.620 --> 02:27:24.359
President Reagan’s speech began to veer
off, as the topic of conversation shifted

02:27:24.359 --> 02:27:29.160
from the importance of family values to the
exquisite taste of human flesh.

02:27:29.160 --> 02:27:31.439
Blake was taken aback.

02:27:31.439 --> 02:27:32.639
Surely, he was hearing things?

02:27:32.640 --> 02:27:35.220
But the tape only got worse.

02:27:35.220 --> 02:27:40.020
President Reagan began to divulge the fact
that he enjoyed the taste of young flesh the

02:27:40.020 --> 02:27:42.480
best, particularly that of infants.

02:27:42.479 --> 02:27:47.280
As Reagan began to go into detail about how
exactly one should best cook an infant if

02:27:47.280 --> 02:27:51.240
you want to seal in the flavour, the crowd
erupted into modest applause.

02:27:51.240 --> 02:27:53.040
Blake started to feel sick.

02:27:53.040 --> 02:27:57.600
He’d remembered watching this speech, and
President Reagan had said nothing of the sort!

02:27:58.380 --> 02:28:03.300
Things only got weirder as the President’s
cheek suddenly opened up into a long, bleeding

02:28:03.300 --> 02:28:07.440
gash, as though someone had cut into his face
with an invisible knife.

02:28:07.439 --> 02:28:13.259
As the speech continued, and Reagan’s words
became more nonsensical and incoherent, the

02:28:13.260 --> 02:28:14.700
injuries got worse, too.

02:28:14.700 --> 02:28:18.179
His face developed puncture wounds, like he
was being stabbed.

02:28:18.180 --> 02:28:20.880
Skin in some areas rotted and peeled off.

02:28:20.880 --> 02:28:26.280
Reagan showed no awareness of the horrifying
injuries that seemed to be occurring spontaneously

02:28:26.280 --> 02:28:26.819
on his body.

02:28:26.819 --> 02:28:28.740
This was a living nightmare!

02:28:28.740 --> 02:28:34.620
The tape came to a merciful end 22 minutes
in, after President Reagan’s throat appeared

02:28:34.620 --> 02:28:38.399
to be slashed open and his insane speech was
reduced to quiet gurgles.

02:28:39.000 --> 02:28:43.740
It fizzled out into static shortly after,
and Blake politely retired to the bathroom

02:28:43.740 --> 02:28:44.580
to throw up.

02:28:45.300 --> 02:28:48.840
Was this some sick prank or tampering or camera
trickery, perhaps?

02:28:48.840 --> 02:28:54.960
He didn’t know but that tape was disgusting,
and whoever was responsible had to be punished.

02:28:54.960 --> 02:28:59.640
Newsom contacted the police, hoping obscenity
charges could be pressed against the creator

02:28:59.640 --> 02:29:00.900
of the tape once they were found.

02:29:00.899 --> 02:29:06.179
The tape was taken into evidence, and a low-level
police investigation into the possible culprits

02:29:06.180 --> 02:29:06.420
began.

02:29:06.420 --> 02:29:10.980
While the police officers who viewed the tape
reported nightmares in the weeks following,

02:29:10.979 --> 02:29:13.019
the creator of the tape was never found.

02:29:13.020 --> 02:29:15.960
The investigation truly came to an end when&nbsp;

02:29:15.960 --> 02:29:18.540
a superior closed the case&nbsp;
and the tape disappeared

02:29:18.540 --> 02:29:19.740
from the evidence locker.

02:29:19.740 --> 02:29:24.899
This, as you probably could have guessed,
was the work of a field agent from The SCP

02:29:24.899 --> 02:29:25.379
Foundation.

02:29:25.380 --> 02:29:30.060
Amnestics were then used to erase the memories
of everyone unlucky enough to witness the

02:29:30.060 --> 02:29:35.220
tape, including Blake Newsom, who could finally
rest easy and return to his filing work.

02:29:35.760 --> 02:29:38.460
The anomalous tape was now in responsible
hands.

02:29:38.460 --> 02:29:44.100
It was given the designation SCP – 1981,
and given the object class “Safe” due

02:29:44.100 --> 02:29:46.621
to its easily controlled and self-contained
nature.

02:29:46.620 --> 02:29:50.939
Proper research and testing was now able to
begin and while nothing about the construction

02:29:50.939 --> 02:29:56.160
of the tape suggested anything inherently
anomalous, repeat viewings of the video made

02:29:56.160 --> 02:30:00.300
it clear that this went far beyond mere doctored
footage of a Presidential speech.

02:30:00.300 --> 02:30:05.400
Every single time the tape is played, both
the speech made and the injuries received

02:30:05.399 --> 02:30:06.780
by President Reagan change.

02:30:06.780 --> 02:30:12.179
The few rules the tape seems to always follow
are that Reagan never reacts to the injuries

02:30:12.180 --> 02:30:17.520
he’s receiving, it always has the same beginning
and total runtime, and the speech is always

02:30:17.520 --> 02:30:18.121
corrupted.

02:30:18.120 --> 02:30:22.859
These speeches have been described as “mostly
incoherent, lacking any sort of underlying

02:30:22.859 --> 02:30:28.139
thematic structure and largely being composed
of nonsensical anecdotes and parables”,

02:30:28.140 --> 02:30:33.180
so not that dissimilar from a regular Reagan
speech, but the topics always turn incredibly

02:30:33.180 --> 02:30:39.960
dark and have included torture, mutilation,
death, cannibalism, ritual sacrifice, genocide,

02:30:39.960 --> 02:30:40.560
and more.

02:30:41.100 --> 02:30:45.720
The range of injuries shown on President Reagan
in the videos have included, but are by no

02:30:45.720 --> 02:30:50.640
means limited to, impalement, mutilation,
flaying, and some tortures so gruesome that

02:30:50.640 --> 02:30:53.100
the details have been redacted from official
files.

02:30:53.100 --> 02:30:58.500
On several occasions, the details of President
Reagan’s speech have also eerily predicted

02:30:58.500 --> 02:30:58.920
the future.

02:30:58.920 --> 02:31:04.680
These include successfully predicting the
September 11th attacks in 2001 and the outcome

02:31:04.680 --> 02:31:07.080
of the 2008 Russian presidential election.

02:31:07.080 --> 02:31:10.500
Incidentally, this isn’t&nbsp;
even the only Reagan-related&nbsp;

02:31:10.500 --> 02:31:12.120
SCP to predict the future.

02:31:13.020 --> 02:31:20.281
No, there’s another entry in this incredibly
specific niche: SCP – 095, a highly degraded

02:31:20.280 --> 02:31:23.519
copy of a comic known as “The Atomic Adventures
of Ronnie Ray-Gun.”

02:31:24.120 --> 02:31:28.859
The title character bears a striking resemblance
to President Reagan, despite the fact that

02:31:28.859 --> 02:31:33.179
the comic is confirmed by Foundation tests
to have been written in the early 1930s.

02:31:33.780 --> 02:31:38.700
The comic is set in the far-off future world
of the 1980s, and follows a number of Ronnie’s

02:31:38.700 --> 02:31:40.019
exploits in three stories.

02:31:40.620 --> 02:31:45.240
The first, titled “Ronnie vs. Space Admiral
Carter”, seems to perfectly describe the

02:31:45.240 --> 02:31:47.460
events of the 1980 presidential election.

02:31:49.140 --> 02:31:53.880
The second, “Space Assassin!”, mirrors
the attempted assassination of President Reagan

02:31:53.880 --> 02:31:55.560
by John Hinckley Jr.

02:31:55.560 --> 02:32:01.260
And the third, titled “Jungle Planet!”,
retells the Iran-Contra controversies of 1986.

02:32:01.920 --> 02:32:06.180
These comics were produced under the mysterious
and apparently non-existent company, “Future

02:32:06.180 --> 02:32:06.720
Funnies.”

02:32:06.720 --> 02:32:11.220
The Foundation hopes to track down the other
comics from this company whenever possible,

02:32:11.220 --> 02:32:13.440
but they’ve had no luck on that front.

02:32:13.439 --> 02:32:16.799
For now, there’s only SCP – 095.

02:32:16.800 --> 02:32:22.500
During initial testing, Foundation staff watched
the tape frequently in case this strange,

02:32:22.500 --> 02:32:26.700
corrupted version of President Reagan had
any other valuable predictions for the future.

02:32:27.420 --> 02:32:32.160
However, during one of these screenings, one
of the D-Class observation personnel pointed

02:32:32.160 --> 02:32:34.260
and yelled at the screen in horror.

02:32:34.260 --> 02:32:39.420
Upon further examination of recorded footage,
researchers could see exactly what had concerned

02:32:39.420 --> 02:32:41.040
the D-Class observer so much.

02:32:42.060 --> 02:32:46.140
While, in other viewings of the tape, President
Reagan’s press detail had appeared totally

02:32:46.140 --> 02:32:49.201
normal, in this one something was clearly
amiss.

02:32:49.200 --> 02:32:54.120
Standing among the other dull, suit-wearing
political aides was a tall figure dressed

02:32:54.120 --> 02:32:58.140
in a midnight-black cloak with a large, conical
hood obscuring his face.

02:32:58.140 --> 02:33:03.000
The figure didn’t appear to move in the
footage – it just stood there, menacingly.

02:33:03.000 --> 02:33:08.040
A later survey indicated that this figure
would appear in roughly one in seven viewings

02:33:08.040 --> 02:33:08.640
of the tape.

02:33:09.600 --> 02:33:16.020
This cloaked figure was designated SCP – 1981
– 1, and he became part of the recurring

02:33:16.020 --> 02:33:20.281
imagery in the nightmares that often followed
a viewing of SCP – 1981.

02:33:20.880 --> 02:33:25.740
Naturally, despite containment and preservation
attempts, the Foundation was aware that just

02:33:25.740 --> 02:33:28.740
like any normal tape,&nbsp;
natural magnetic interference&nbsp;

02:33:28.740 --> 02:33:30.540
would eventually degrade it beyond use.

02:33:31.380 --> 02:33:35.640
Attempts to copy the footage onto another
Betamax tape failed to reproduce the anomalous

02:33:35.640 --> 02:33:36.120
effects.

02:33:36.120 --> 02:33:41.340
That’s why the Foundation has painstakingly
recorded any video and audio they could via

02:33:41.340 --> 02:33:43.200
a standard commercial camcorder.

02:33:43.200 --> 02:33:50.040
In one particularly terrifying playback, SCP
– 1981 – 1 took the president’s place

02:33:50.040 --> 02:33:53.040
at the podium, staring directly into the camera.

02:33:53.040 --> 02:33:57.479
The words “I SEE YOU” appeared over a
black screen shortly after.

02:33:57.479 --> 02:34:01.679
Staff members were ordered never to make an
attempt at communicating with the figure,

02:34:01.680 --> 02:34:06.840
and instead contact a Level 4 superior if
such an event occurs during a playback again.

02:34:07.500 --> 02:34:13.080
The frightening and unfortunate effects of
SCP – 1981 would come to their logical conclusion

02:34:13.080 --> 02:34:19.080
under the watchful eye of Dr. James Kyle Robinson,
Managing Archivist of Inert Safe-Class Objects

02:34:19.080 --> 02:34:21.540
and Anomalous Items at Site 73.

02:34:21.540 --> 02:34:27.359
He was contacted by Special Agent Arnold Rodriguez
and Special Agent Ethan Tate, members of secret

02:34:27.359 --> 02:34:30.059
service with a duty of care to President Reagan.

02:34:30.060 --> 02:34:34.140
Word had gotten to Reagan that there was an
anomalous artefact in the possession of the

02:34:34.140 --> 02:34:38.040
Foundation that directly pertained to him,
and he wanted to see it.

02:34:38.700 --> 02:34:43.979
Dr. Robinson obtained files and transcripts
pertaining to SCP – 1981 and handed them

02:34:43.979 --> 02:34:49.139
over to the Agents, but refused to allow President
Reagan to see the tape directly without approval

02:34:49.140 --> 02:34:50.220
from O5 Command.

02:34:50.220 --> 02:34:52.980
But Reagan and the agents were persistent.

02:34:52.979 --> 02:34:58.500
Eventually, O5 Command ordered a private screening
of the tape for President Reagan at the Sanford

02:34:58.500 --> 02:35:03.420
Chemical Processing Plant – a front business
owned and operated by the Foundation for Amnestic

02:35:03.420 --> 02:35:03.780
production.

02:35:03.780 --> 02:35:08.700
Dr. Robinson offered President Reagan the
use of Amnestics after the session completed,

02:35:08.700 --> 02:35:10.019
but Reagan declined.

02:35:10.020 --> 02:35:14.340
The screening took place in Conference Room
B, and the tape was re-played three times.

02:35:14.340 --> 02:35:18.240
It was on the third playback that things took
an interesting turn.

02:35:18.240 --> 02:35:22.620
As the mutilated Reagan on the screen began
to rant about drinking the blood of a child

02:35:22.620 --> 02:35:27.180
from the skull of Vladimir Putin, Reagan began
to silently mouth along to the words, as though

02:35:27.180 --> 02:35:28.080
he remembered them.

02:35:28.080 --> 02:35:32.939
He spoke about beings known as “The Destroyers”,
and potential apocalyptic events to come.

02:35:33.540 --> 02:35:37.979
After the screening, Reagan once again refused
the offer of Amnestics, and departed.

02:35:38.580 --> 02:35:41.100
It seemed as though all was well, until a&nbsp;

02:35:41.100 --> 02:35:43.440
violent break-in at the&nbsp;
Sanford Chemical Processing

02:35:43.439 --> 02:35:45.000
Plant that left the night guard dead.

02:35:45.660 --> 02:35:49.559
A large number of Amnestics had been stolen
during the break-in, and security footage

02:35:49.560 --> 02:35:52.320
showed that Agents Tate and Rodriguez had
been responsible.

02:35:52.319 --> 02:35:56.580
The two agents were tracked down and traced
to the residence of Ronald Reagan, where the

02:35:56.580 --> 02:36:00.960
Foundation came upon a disturbing sight: The
agents had pillaged large quantities of Class

02:36:00.960 --> 02:36:06.000
A and B Amnestics and supplied them to President
Reagan, who – at some point after observing

02:36:06.000 --> 02:36:10.140
SCP – 1981 – had been driven into a dangerous
madness.

02:36:10.140 --> 02:36:14.940
The two agents wanted to cure him before he
caused harm to himself or others, but their

02:36:14.939 --> 02:36:17.219
bungling had come with severe consequences.

02:36:17.220 --> 02:36:21.660
Misapplying such a high quantity of Amnestics
had essentially destroyed Reagan’s mind,

02:36:21.660 --> 02:36:26.399
and while the Foundation was able to stabilize
his condition, his impaired memory and cognitive

02:36:26.399 --> 02:36:29.519
function would leave him unable to care for
himself independently.

02:36:30.540 --> 02:36:35.519
In order to cover up for this grievous mistake,
a cover story was concocted about Reagan falling

02:36:35.520 --> 02:36:39.121
victim to Alzheimer’s and facing severe
cognitive decline as a result.

02:36:39.840 --> 02:36:44.160
Both Agents Tate and Rodriguez were fired
for their actions, had their memories wiped

02:36:44.160 --> 02:36:46.620
by the Foundation, and were&nbsp;
assigned new identities.

02:36:46.620 --> 02:36:51.660
Dr. Robinson, for his part in the disaster,
had to face a Foundation Ethics Committee

02:36:51.660 --> 02:36:52.740
Disciplinary Hearing.

02:36:53.520 --> 02:36:58.680
While SCP – 1981 continues to be classified
as“Safe” due to its unlikeliness to ever

02:36:58.680 --> 02:37:03.060
breach containment, when you consider the
havoc it wrought on the mind of its singular

02:37:03.060 --> 02:37:06.241
target, “safe” is hardly the word that
comes to mind.

02:37:06.240 --> 02:37:10.740
It’s enough to make you wonder what other
tapes are lurking out there, just waiting

02:37:10.740 --> 02:37:11.639
to be found

02:37:11.640 --> 02:37:18.480
The Young Girl stood silently in a room full&nbsp;
of corpses, staring off into the distance.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:37:19.200 --> 02:37:23.580
She was in a trance, seemingly&nbsp;
unaware of the carnage that’d&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:37:23.580 --> 02:37:28.319
just unfolded around her. Some of the&nbsp;
men were shot or stabbed or beaten,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:37:28.319 --> 02:37:35.340
others had no apparent cause of death whatsoever.&nbsp;
But the Young Girl was unscathed. She was wearing&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:37:35.340 --> 02:37:39.120
a yellow summer dress and looked like she&nbsp;
couldn’t have been more than three years&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:37:39.120 --> 02:37:45.420
old. She awoke from her trance, still paying&nbsp;
no heed to the violence in the room, and left.

02:37:45.420 --> 02:37:51.060
This is the story of SCP - 053, the Young Girl.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:37:51.060 --> 02:37:56.400
Her strange and terrifying life before&nbsp;
containment, her thrilling capture,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:37:57.120 --> 02:38:03.599
and the part she played in one of the most&nbsp;
dangerous SCP Foundation cross-tests of all time.

02:38:03.600 --> 02:38:09.060
She had no name. The Young Girl could&nbsp;
never spend enough time around someone&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:38:09.060 --> 02:38:15.060
to be given one. It was her terrible curse that&nbsp;
she could never stay in one place for too long,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:38:15.060 --> 02:38:20.880
or something truly awful would happen to everyone&nbsp;
around her. She’d been drifting for years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:38:20.880 --> 02:38:27.720
but never grew to look older than a child.&nbsp;
Her memories were long but formless - divided&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:38:27.720 --> 02:38:34.080
mostly into ten-minute increments. The Young&nbsp;
Girl kept on moving. It was all she could do.

02:38:34.080 --> 02:38:40.680
In 1993, when the Young Girl had already been&nbsp;
alive for a very long time, she found herself in&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:38:40.680 --> 02:38:45.900
Illinois after days of trekking on the roadside.&nbsp;
She would scavenge what little food she needed&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:38:45.899 --> 02:38:52.139
from the trash, and drink from lakes, rivers,&nbsp;
or even puddles when she needed to. Deep down,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:38:52.140 --> 02:38:57.540
the Young Girl knew that even if she grew&nbsp;
hungry or thirsty, she would not die.

02:38:57.540 --> 02:39:02.399
In her travels, the Young Girl had managed&nbsp;
to scrounge together a few dollars,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:39:02.399 --> 02:39:05.759
and though she knew her contact&nbsp;
with people had to be limited,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:39:06.359 --> 02:39:12.540
there was one thing she wanted that felt worth&nbsp;
the risk: A candy bar. It’d been a long time&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:39:12.540 --> 02:39:17.340
since she tasted chocolate, and she found&nbsp;
the idea of tasting it again too enticing&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:39:17.340 --> 02:39:23.100
to resist. When she reached Chicago, she entered&nbsp;
a small corner store with her handful of dollars,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:39:23.100 --> 02:39:28.140
selected a candy bar from the rack, and&nbsp;
approached the counter. For reasons even&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:39:28.140 --> 02:39:33.241
she didn’t fully understand, she kept her eyes&nbsp;
down as she placed the money on the counter.

02:39:33.240 --> 02:39:39.599
You see, SCP - 053 was always a special&nbsp;
child. As we briefly mentioned earlier,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:39:39.600 --> 02:39:44.340
you might even say she was cursed. Whenever&nbsp;
she was around other people for too long,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:39:44.340 --> 02:39:51.540
terrible things tended to happen. Unspeakable&nbsp;
things. And as a component of this strange,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:39:51.540 --> 02:39:56.220
unexplainable curse - or perhaps as a&nbsp;
means of keeping her safe from it - the&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:39:56.220 --> 02:40:01.380
Young Girl was doomed to never understand&nbsp;
the nature of her predicament. It was like&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:40:01.380 --> 02:40:05.819
there was a mental wall between her and&nbsp;
the horrors her presence could cause.

02:40:06.540 --> 02:40:12.120
All she knew was that it was best to avoid eye&nbsp;
contact, stay away from large groups of people&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:40:12.120 --> 02:40:19.979
at all costs, and never spend any longer than&nbsp;
ten minutes around anyone. Ever. That’s why,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:40:19.979 --> 02:40:25.319
as she waited for her chocolate bar at the cash&nbsp;
register, she kept her head down and waited to go.

02:40:25.319 --> 02:40:30.599
The cashier looked down upon this strange girl&nbsp;
with apparent concern. It’d been a slow day,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:40:30.600 --> 02:40:35.580
all in all. A few listless patrons milled&nbsp;
around the store, window shopping. His&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:40:35.580 --> 02:40:42.240
brain was practically on autopilot, until he saw&nbsp;
this child. She looked filthy, in a dishevelled&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:40:42.240 --> 02:40:48.420
dress and was totally alone. What on earth had&nbsp;
happened to this child? The more he looked at her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:40:48.420 --> 02:40:54.960
the more he sensed a creepy vibe exuding from&nbsp;
her. Something about this girl was wrong.

02:40:54.960 --> 02:41:01.080
He spoke softly to her, introducing himself&nbsp;
as Miles, and asking her where her mommy&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:41:01.080 --> 02:41:06.479
and daddy were. The Young Girl hesitated for&nbsp;
just a few seconds too long for his liking,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:41:06.479 --> 02:41:11.280
before simply saying that they were at home.&nbsp;
Any parent who’d let their three-year-old kid&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:41:11.280 --> 02:41:17.040
just wander around the South Side of Chicago&nbsp;
alone was either crazy, neglectful, or both.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:41:17.880 --> 02:41:22.260
He asked her politely to remain in the&nbsp;
store, while he gave the police a quick call.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:41:23.040 --> 02:41:25.979
He’d even let her have the candy&nbsp;
bar for free while she waited.

02:41:25.979 --> 02:41:31.379
Immediately, the little girl became uncomfortable.&nbsp;
She’d already been in here for a few minutes now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:41:31.380 --> 02:41:35.520
and while Miles called the police he&nbsp;
expected her to wait around even longer.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:41:36.359 --> 02:41:41.099
Again, she couldn’t even tell you why she knew&nbsp;
waiting around like this would be so dangerous,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:41:41.100 --> 02:41:47.400
but she had a nagging, instinctual awareness&nbsp;
that she needed to get out. Around the store,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:41:47.399 --> 02:41:54.179
the few patrons still inside started to get a&nbsp;
strange feeling, like someone was watching them.

02:41:54.180 --> 02:42:00.000
Soon, what seemed like mild paranoia was&nbsp;
quickly becoming white-hot anger. Pure&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:42:00.000 --> 02:42:05.280
rage. They felt almost like they had&nbsp;
to kill someone. But not just anyone.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:42:06.300 --> 02:42:10.800
Someone particular. They&nbsp;
had to kill the little girl.

02:42:10.800 --> 02:42:16.620
It wasn’t long until the police arrived. Two&nbsp;
officers, Holiday and DeWitt, entered to collect&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:42:16.620 --> 02:42:22.319
the apparently neglected little girl. It was&nbsp;
a story they’d sadly heard all too often - a&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:42:22.319 --> 02:42:26.700
tragically common occurrence in the big city.&nbsp;
When the two of them approached the Young Girl,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:42:26.700 --> 02:42:31.800
she was looking down at the ground. They tried&nbsp;
to speak to her but she was unresponsive. Miles&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:42:31.800 --> 02:42:37.080
looked on, concerned, but deep down, he&nbsp;
felt the same bizarre progression all the&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:42:37.080 --> 02:42:44.819
other store-goers were feeling: Confusion,&nbsp;
irritability, and finally... violent rage.

02:42:44.819 --> 02:42:49.920
The corner store was a powder keg,&nbsp;
all it needed now was a spark.

02:42:49.920 --> 02:42:56.340
And that spark came when Officer Holiday reached&nbsp;
down, and took the Young Girl by the arm. His bare&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:42:56.340 --> 02:43:02.819
skin touched her’s, and it was all over. The&nbsp;
cop twitched, his mind washed out in murderous&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:43:02.819 --> 02:43:08.819
insanity, as he reached for his side-arm. Officer&nbsp;
DeWitt opened his mouth to protest, but he didn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:43:08.819 --> 02:43:14.519
manage to get a syllable out before Holiday turned&nbsp;
and shot him. In a fraction of a second, the quiet&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:43:14.520 --> 02:43:19.980
corner store exploded into a violent bloodbath,&nbsp;
as the patrons and cops slaughtered each other.

02:43:19.979 --> 02:43:23.639
All the while, the Young Girl&nbsp;
just stood there in a trance.

02:43:23.640 --> 02:43:30.120
Everyone was dead within minutes, except Miles&nbsp;
and the Young Girl. He shakily rose to his feet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:43:30.120 --> 02:43:35.760
his mind carved out by madness, and reached&nbsp;
for Officer Holiday’s discarded pistol.

02:43:36.479 --> 02:43:39.299
Outside of the store, The Young Girl appeared,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:43:39.300 --> 02:43:44.460
walking out as if nothing had happened.&nbsp;
Inside, Miles’s body was sprawled over&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:43:44.460 --> 02:43:48.480
the counter, clutching his chest&nbsp;
as if his heart had just exploded.

02:43:48.479 --> 02:43:54.780
This was the true nature of the Young Girl’s&nbsp;
curse. Anyone who meets her eye, touches her skin,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:43:54.780 --> 02:43:59.759
or spends over ten minutes around her is&nbsp;
destined to slip into a state of murderous&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:43:59.760 --> 02:44:06.840
insanity. They’ll go into a kill-crazy frenzy,&nbsp;
and attack anyone around them, until all that’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:44:06.840 --> 02:44:12.840
left is them and the Young Girl. At which point,&nbsp;
they’ll try to kill her, too - but the mere act of&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:44:12.840 --> 02:44:18.960
attempting to kill her is also fatal, killing its&nbsp;
victims with a massive heart attack or a seizure.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:44:19.620 --> 02:44:24.059
The second part of the girl’s curse&nbsp;
is that she herself can never die.

02:44:24.060 --> 02:44:30.781
She keeps coming back, unknowingly causing&nbsp;
more misery and death along the way. Until,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:44:30.780 --> 02:44:35.639
of course, a certain secret&nbsp;
organization took notice.

02:44:35.640 --> 02:44:40.560
That night, the Young Girl sat in the cavernous&nbsp;
interior of a local abandoned warehouse,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:44:40.560 --> 02:44:46.320
quietly eating her hard-earned candy bar.&nbsp;
Suddenly, she heard a quiet “crack” in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:44:46.319 --> 02:44:51.299
distance. She tried to move her left arm, but&nbsp;
found it was numb. She could barely move it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:44:51.300 --> 02:44:56.460
The Girl turned her head, and saw a tranquilizer&nbsp;
dart sticking out of her skin. Instinctively,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:44:56.460 --> 02:45:01.439
she got up and began to run, limping as her&nbsp;
left leg started to lose all feeling too.

02:45:01.439 --> 02:45:06.660
Suddenly, she was surrounded by footsteps,&nbsp;
as masked men in SWAT uniforms emerged out&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:45:06.660 --> 02:45:12.240
of the darkness on all sides. The last thing she&nbsp;
remembered before slipping out of consciousness&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:45:12.240 --> 02:45:18.840
was a blindfold being pulled over her eyes, and&nbsp;
tiny metal handcuffs clasping over her wrists.

02:45:18.840 --> 02:45:25.260
When she woke up, she was in the nicest room she’d&nbsp;
slept in in years. It was sixteen feet by sixteen&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:45:25.260 --> 02:45:31.740
feet, with toys, books, and games. Standing&nbsp;
across the room from her was a stranger in&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:45:31.740 --> 02:45:37.559
a full hazmat suit, connected to a long, steel&nbsp;
cable leading out of the room. He spoke calmly&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:45:37.560 --> 02:45:43.260
and politely. A timer on his wrist counted down&nbsp;
from ten minutes. The stranger explained to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:45:43.260 --> 02:45:47.520
Young Girl that they would be taking care of&nbsp;
her now, and would provide her with all the&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:45:47.520 --> 02:45:54.480
toys and games and treats she wanted, provided she&nbsp;
cooperated and submitted willingly to some tests.

02:45:55.260 --> 02:45:58.440
Compared to living out on the&nbsp;
streets with no food or comfort,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:45:58.439 --> 02:46:03.899
this seemed like an excellent compromise.&nbsp;
She would live in what seemed like luxury,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:46:03.899 --> 02:46:09.719
and every so often, she’d be taken to a testing&nbsp;
room with a stranger in an orange jumpsuit.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:46:10.439 --> 02:46:14.160
After a few minutes of waiting, the&nbsp;
stranger would inevitably go feral,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:46:14.160 --> 02:46:19.859
and attempt to kill her - and then always die in&nbsp;
the process. The strangers in the hazmat suits&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:46:19.859 --> 02:46:24.299
told her that all of these tests were helping&nbsp;
them learn extremely valuable things about her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:46:24.300 --> 02:46:30.840
and that soon, they’d have a very special job&nbsp;
for her. It would be a wonderful surprise.

02:46:30.840 --> 02:46:37.440
It was in the spring of 1994 that the Young&nbsp;
Girl, now officially designated SCP - 053,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:46:37.439 --> 02:46:43.859
finally received her special mission. Several&nbsp;
strangers in full hazmat suits, wielding rifles,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:46:43.859 --> 02:46:49.439
escorted her out of her usual bedroom. She asked&nbsp;
where she was being taken, and was told she was&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:46:49.439 --> 02:46:54.419
going to meet a new friend. She was taken&nbsp;
to one of the recreational testing rooms,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:46:54.420 --> 02:47:02.880
and pushed inside. Out in front of her, she saw&nbsp;
something terrifying: A giant, reptilian creature.

02:47:02.880 --> 02:47:08.220
She retreated from it instinctually, hiding&nbsp;
behind a chair in the containment area. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:47:08.220 --> 02:47:13.680
giant reptile didn’t move. It just sat there.&nbsp;
Eventually, she plucked up the courage to go&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:47:13.680 --> 02:47:18.420
and touch the creature, before retreating&nbsp;
again. No reaction. Little by little,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:47:18.420 --> 02:47:23.940
the Young Girl gained confidence, and continued&nbsp;
to approach and pat the creature. It exhaled&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:47:23.939 --> 02:47:28.019
through its huge nostrils, and the Young Girl&nbsp;
literally jumped for joy in her amusement.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:47:28.560 --> 02:47:33.900
She began to play with the docile monster,&nbsp;
hugging it, even drawing on it with a crayon.

02:47:33.899 --> 02:47:38.519
The observers were truly baffled. What the&nbsp;
Young Girl didn’t know was that she was&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:47:38.520 --> 02:47:45.060
playing with SCP - 682, one of the most hateful&nbsp;
and aggressive anomalies under the Foundation’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:47:45.060 --> 02:47:51.180
watchful eye. And yet, in her presence, the&nbsp;
creature was like an overgrown puppy dog.

02:47:51.180 --> 02:47:56.220
After the test phase, the Young Girl was removed&nbsp;
from the Hard-To-Kill Reptile’s presence,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:47:56.220 --> 02:48:01.620
immediately causing the creature to become&nbsp;
violent and murderous once again. After&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:48:01.620 --> 02:48:06.660
being separated from her strange new friend, the&nbsp;
Young Girl was seen crying for several minutes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:48:07.319 --> 02:48:11.759
According to all accounts, the Young Girl&nbsp;
is eager to see her friend again some day,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:48:11.760 --> 02:48:15.540
though considering the Reptile killed&nbsp;
several guards after their separation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:48:15.540 --> 02:48:18.840
the Foundation isn’t eager to grant her that wish.

02:48:18.840 --> 02:48:24.420
SCP-053 was classified as Euclid and&nbsp;
continues to be held in containment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:48:24.420 --> 02:48:30.660
with her toys, books, and games rotated&nbsp;
out on a regular basis. Seeing as she&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:48:30.660 --> 02:48:35.220
shows no sign of aging, this ongoing&nbsp;
containment is likely to be the sad,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:48:35.220 --> 02:48:41.400
strange fate of the Young Girl. An anomaly that&nbsp;
never wanted to hurt anyone - but an important&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:48:41.399 --> 02:48:47.759
and cruel reminder that what we want doesn’t&nbsp;
always influence the world in the way we want.

02:48:47.760 --> 02:48:50.940
Joseph and Frank were two life-long Squatchers.

02:48:50.939 --> 02:48:56.339
No, that isn’t an insult – that’s a
self-given title for Bigfoot enthusiasts who

02:48:56.340 --> 02:49:00.720
are willing to head out into the woods and
search for the legendary Sasquatch first-hand.

02:49:00.720 --> 02:49:05.100
While most Squatchers will go their whole
lives without ever encountering one, Joseph

02:49:05.100 --> 02:49:08.640
and Frank were about to get lucky – they
just didn’t know what kind of luck.

02:49:08.640 --> 02:49:12.900
During a journey through the forests of the
Pacific Northwest, Frank spotted something

02:49:12.899 --> 02:49:18.059
moving in the distance: A huge, ape-like creature
with greyish fur and human-like movements.

02:49:18.060 --> 02:49:22.800
Frank thought he was finally laying eyes on
the mighty Bigfoot after decades of searching.

02:49:22.800 --> 02:49:26.040
What he didn’t know was that he’d just
made a deadly mistake.

02:49:26.040 --> 02:49:29.519
He had looked directly at SCP – 1000.

02:49:29.520 --> 02:49:32.161
And there would be terrible consequences.

02:49:32.160 --> 02:49:36.720
Frank was excited – he’d just achieved
the life goal of any Squatcher.

02:49:36.720 --> 02:49:40.620
He tapped Joseph on the shoulder and directed
him to look in the direction of the creature.

02:49:40.620 --> 02:49:43.500
Joseph followed Frank’s direction and stared
into the distance.

02:49:43.500 --> 02:49:47.939
When his eyes finally came into focus on the
ape-like beast... he froze.

02:49:47.939 --> 02:49:49.859
His brain just short-circuited.

02:49:49.859 --> 02:49:54.780
One second, he was about to encounter the
Holy Grail of his hobby, and the next, he

02:49:54.780 --> 02:49:56.160
was literally brain dead.

02:49:56.160 --> 02:49:57.720
Joseph collapsed.

02:49:57.720 --> 02:50:01.741
In the distance, the ape-like creature disappeared
back into the woods.

02:50:01.740 --> 02:50:06.599
Not that Frank even noticed – he was too
busy trying to wake Joseph but it was no use.

02:50:07.200 --> 02:50:10.319
Joseph was gone, and Frank had no idea why.

02:50:10.319 --> 02:50:13.019
The headlines read, “BIGFOOT KILLED MY FRIEND.”

02:50:13.020 --> 02:50:15.541
Most people either ignored it or laughed it
off.

02:50:15.540 --> 02:50:19.439
Just a couple of cranks goofing off in a forest
and one of them had dropped dead.

02:50:19.439 --> 02:50:20.460
Who cares?

02:50:20.460 --> 02:50:24.420
Well, one organization cared – The SCP Foundation.

02:50:24.420 --> 02:50:30.660
Mobile Task Force Zeta-1000, the Foundation’s
specialized SCP – 1000 detail, were alerted

02:50:30.660 --> 02:50:31.439
to the reports.

02:50:31.439 --> 02:50:35.280
They sprang into action, tracking down and
detaining Frank for questioning.

02:50:35.280 --> 02:50:39.960
They process a million loony bigfoot lovers
every year, and usually find nothing, but

02:50:39.960 --> 02:50:43.620
the death of Frank’s friend made it all
too clear – they hadn’t encountered a

02:50:43.620 --> 02:50:47.580
bigfoot but a real, genuine example of SCP
– 1000.

02:50:48.359 --> 02:50:54.660
SCP – 1000 rarely ranks among the scariest
or most dangerous SCPs, but underestimating

02:50:54.660 --> 02:50:59.819
the creature is a terrible mistake because
just looking at it gives you a 2% chance of

02:50:59.819 --> 02:51:01.019
dropping dead on the spot.

02:51:01.020 --> 02:51:04.440
Frank, despite losing his friend, was one
of the lucky ones.

02:51:04.439 --> 02:51:09.479
The Foundation debriefed him before administering
amnestics, and making sure that he’d never

02:51:09.479 --> 02:51:13.200
venture back to those mysterious forests in
the Pacific Northwest again.

02:51:13.200 --> 02:51:18.179
Director Jones, the site director charged
with the management of SCP – 1000 populations,

02:51:18.180 --> 02:51:23.100
was given the information on this latest case
of a SCP – 1000-related fatality.

02:51:23.100 --> 02:51:25.440
It was a story he’d heard many times before.

02:51:25.439 --> 02:51:28.620
For Director Jones, they all seemed to bleed
into one another.

02:51:28.620 --> 02:51:31.680
So, what exactly is SCP – 1000?

02:51:31.680 --> 02:51:34.440
And how did it leave poor Joseph dead in the
woods?

02:51:34.439 --> 02:51:39.059
SCP – 1000 is a whole species of large,
hominid ape-like creatures.

02:51:39.060 --> 02:51:42.960
They’re largely nocturnal, but sightings
of the creature during the day aren’t unheard

02:51:42.960 --> 02:51:43.140
of.

02:51:43.140 --> 02:51:47.820
They’re omnivorous, mostly seeming to consume
plants and insects and their fur is usually

02:51:47.819 --> 02:51:51.120
grey, brown, black, red, or occasionally white.

02:51:51.960 --> 02:51:54.899
The creatures have large&nbsp;
eyes capable of impressive&nbsp;

02:51:54.899 --> 02:51:57.779
vision nestled underneath a&nbsp;
pronounced, Neanderthal-like

02:51:57.779 --> 02:51:58.019
brow.

02:51:58.020 --> 02:52:02.880
Another defining feature is the ridge of bone
on the forehead, much like that of a gorilla,

02:52:02.880 --> 02:52:04.560
that is present in both sexes.

02:52:04.560 --> 02:52:09.661
According to Foundation studies, the creatures
exhibit a level of intelligence on par with

02:52:09.660 --> 02:52:13.139
that of the common chimpanzee, but nowhere
near that of us humans.

02:52:13.140 --> 02:52:16.500
What they lack in intelligence, though, they
more than make up for in size.

02:52:16.500 --> 02:52:21.000
The adults can be as large as ten feet tall,
and weigh up to 600 pounds.

02:52:21.000 --> 02:52:23.819
Despite their great size and impressive strength,&nbsp;

02:52:23.819 --> 02:52:26.399
the creatures are neither&nbsp;
aggressive nor territorial.

02:52:26.399 --> 02:52:31.139
In fact, they seem to instinctively avoid
humans, mostly residing deep in the forests

02:52:31.140 --> 02:52:34.380
of the American Pacific Northwest and in the
Himalayan Alps.

02:52:34.380 --> 02:52:38.640
There have been sightings of SCP – 1000
on every continent, though the Foundation

02:52:38.640 --> 02:52:43.920
has taken pains to exterminate all SCP – 1000
populations situated near human population

02:52:43.920 --> 02:52:46.920
centres to prevent a potential&nbsp;
disaster, considering&nbsp;

02:52:46.920 --> 02:52:49.800
the 2% chance of instantaneous death upon

02:52:49.800 --> 02:52:50.520
visual contact.

02:52:50.520 --> 02:52:55.500
That brings us to our second question: What
is it that makes these seemingly harmless

02:52:55.500 --> 02:52:56.640
creatures so dangerous?

02:52:56.640 --> 02:53:02.161
Sadly, for both these unfortunate creatures
and us humans, the danger is beyond the control

02:53:02.160 --> 02:53:03.599
of SCP – 1000.

02:53:04.200 --> 02:53:09.779
According to Foundation research, SCP – 1000
likely evolved alongside us homo sapiens,

02:53:09.779 --> 02:53:13.200
until a tragedy occurred&nbsp;
between ten and fifteen-thousand&nbsp;

02:53:13.200 --> 02:53:13.740
years ago.

02:53:13.740 --> 02:53:18.779
A mysterious extinction event eliminated the
vast majority of their species, leaving only

02:53:18.779 --> 02:53:21.059
one to five percent alive in the aftermath.

02:53:21.060 --> 02:53:22.081
What happened?

02:53:22.080 --> 02:53:27.120
It’s believed that around this time, SCP
– 1000 contracted what the Foundation refers

02:53:27.120 --> 02:53:29.099
to as an “anomalous pseudo-disease.”

02:53:29.100 --> 02:53:36.180
Meet SCP-1000-f1, a disease that is passed
along at the genetic level, and is so durable

02:53:36.180 --> 02:53:38.880
that it persists in the species to this day.

02:53:38.880 --> 02:53:43.500
The tiny fraction of the population that are
immune to its effects manage to survive, but

02:53:43.500 --> 02:53:46.020
the majority who aren’t immune die shortly
after birth.

02:53:46.020 --> 02:53:49.800
This is why the overall population remains
relatively low to this day.

02:53:49.800 --> 02:53:54.600
It’s a disease that only appears to affect
hominids – including humans, chimpanzees,

02:53:54.600 --> 02:53:58.260
bonobos, and non-immune instances of SCP-1000.

02:53:58.260 --> 02:54:00.660
Any hominid that lays eyes on a carrier of&nbsp;

02:54:00.660 --> 02:54:03.359
the disease has a two percent&nbsp;
chance of experiencing

02:54:03.359 --> 02:54:04.859
immediate brain death.

02:54:04.859 --> 02:54:09.359
While a two percent chance of instant death
may not seem all that threatening, at least

02:54:09.359 --> 02:54:14.399
when compared to some other nightmare inducing
SCPs, the truly scary part is that the percentage

02:54:14.399 --> 02:54:15.299
is cumulative.

02:54:15.300 --> 02:54:21.360
In other words, the longer one observes a
carrier of SCP-1000-f1, the higher that percentage

02:54:21.359 --> 02:54:25.380
rises and the greater your chance of experiencing
an abrupt death.

02:54:25.380 --> 02:54:31.080
According to Foundation studies, the percentage
rises by around one percent every twenty minutes.

02:54:31.080 --> 02:54:36.720
And the percentage also varies between specimens,
with some exhibiting a terrifyingly high death

02:54:36.720 --> 02:54:39.060
chance of 90% upon viewing.

02:54:39.060 --> 02:54:41.340
This death chance continues to occur in dead&nbsp;

02:54:41.340 --> 02:54:43.860
specimens if they carried&nbsp;
the anomalous pseudo-virus

02:54:43.859 --> 02:54:48.059
while alive – though thankfully the risk
doesn’t appear to apply to small fur or

02:54:48.060 --> 02:54:48.900
tissue samples.

02:54:48.899 --> 02:54:53.819
The Foundation’s true concern actually goes
far beyond SCP – 1000 themselves.

02:54:53.819 --> 02:54:59.819
Because of the species’ close relation to
homo sapiens, there’s a worry that SCP-1000-f1

02:54:59.819 --> 02:55:04.920
could transmit to humans, causing our own
species to meet a similar fate.

02:55:04.920 --> 02:55:08.760
If humans did indeed become&nbsp;
carriers of SCP-1000-f1,&nbsp;

02:55:08.760 --> 02:55:11.340
it’s extremely likely that humanity would

02:55:11.340 --> 02:55:16.380
undergo an unprecedented extinction event,
with billions across the globe dropping dead

02:55:16.380 --> 02:55:18.540
as brain death sets in en masse.

02:55:18.540 --> 02:55:23.640
While full extermination of the entire species
has been deemed unlikely, the existential

02:55:23.640 --> 02:55:29.340
threat they pose to humanity more than justifies
the occasional culling of SCP – 1000 populations.

02:55:30.180 --> 02:55:31.741
That was a lot to take in, right?

02:55:31.740 --> 02:55:36.059
First, the creature we thought was Bigfoot
was actually a new species of SCP out in the

02:55:36.060 --> 02:55:36.241
wild.

02:55:36.240 --> 02:55:41.399
And second, these creatures could end human
life as we know it if they made it into a

02:55:41.399 --> 02:55:42.059
population center.

02:55:42.060 --> 02:55:46.621
But what you’re about to hear next – a
dark secret only available to people with

02:55:46.620 --> 02:55:52.260
Level 3 SCP Foundation clearance – is the
most shocking SCP - 1000 fact of all...

02:55:52.260 --> 02:55:53.160
Are you ready?

02:55:53.160 --> 02:55:58.439
The true secret of SCP - 1000 is that what
you’ve just heard is a lie.

02:55:58.439 --> 02:56:04.019
There is no anomalous pseudo-disease, and
SCP – 1000 poses no pathogenic threat to

02:56:04.020 --> 02:56:05.340
humanity whatsoever.

02:56:05.340 --> 02:56:07.200
Who would spread such a thing?

02:56:07.200 --> 02:56:09.179
The SCP Foundation, of course.

02:56:09.180 --> 02:56:15.180
Strictly speaking, the Foundation has disseminated
two direct lies about the nature of SCP – 1000.

02:56:15.180 --> 02:56:19.800
The first is that of the disease, which does
not exist, nor has it ever existed.

02:56:19.800 --> 02:56:22.440
The second lie is about&nbsp;
the creature’s intelligence&nbsp;

02:56:22.439 --> 02:56:24.299
level – they’re far smarter than the average

02:56:24.300 --> 02:56:24.960
chimp.

02:56:24.960 --> 02:56:27.960
In fact, they’re every bit as intelligent
as human beings.

02:56:27.960 --> 02:56:33.060
These were all lies formulated by Director
Jones and the Foundation, as was the very

02:56:33.060 --> 02:56:35.040
existence of the Bigfoot myth.

02:56:35.040 --> 02:56:39.060
The Foundation has been spreading information
that makes the very concept of the Sasquatch

02:56:39.060 --> 02:56:45.060
out to be a joke for decades, all to discredit
and further push the very concept of SCP – 1000

02:56:45.060 --> 02:56:46.440
into the shadows.

02:56:46.979 --> 02:56:47.819
But…why?

02:56:47.819 --> 02:56:52.080
The Foundation is no stranger to coming up
with cover stories, but why would they put

02:56:52.080 --> 02:56:56.040
intentional lies into their own files to anyone
below a Level 3 clearance?

02:56:56.040 --> 02:57:01.028
Well, that all comes down to the horrifying
truth behind the origins of today’s SCP

02:57:01.028 --> 02:57:02.279
– 1000 population.

02:57:02.279 --> 02:57:06.960
The creatures were first brought to the attention
of the Foundation by outcast members of the

02:57:06.960 --> 02:57:11.340
Serpent’s Hand, an organization dedicated
to defying the Foundation’s activities.

02:57:11.340 --> 02:57:17.400
These members, known as the Children of the
Sun, told them the secret history of SCP – 1000.

02:57:17.399 --> 02:57:21.719
While at first, Foundation personnel like
Director Jones didn’t want to believe what

02:57:21.720 --> 02:57:25.200
they were hearing, they soon came to terms
with the horrifying truth.

02:57:25.200 --> 02:57:30.779
Humans and SCP – 1000 did evolve alongside
each other, with humans occupying the day

02:57:30.779 --> 02:57:32.639
and SCP – 1000 the night.

02:57:32.640 --> 02:57:35.820
However, while humans were&nbsp;
still basic hunter-gatherers,&nbsp;

02:57:35.819 --> 02:57:39.240
SCP – 1000 were undergoing vast intellectual

02:57:39.240 --> 02:57:40.620
and societal development.

02:57:40.620 --> 02:57:44.220
They were able to create&nbsp;
tools, weapons, agriculture,&nbsp;

02:57:44.220 --> 02:57:46.560
stable settlements, domesticated animals,

02:57:46.560 --> 02:57:48.960
and eventually even fully developed cities.

02:57:48.960 --> 02:57:54.180
It was like nothing the world had ever seen,
and wouldn’t see for thousands of years

02:57:54.180 --> 02:57:54.720
to come.

02:57:54.720 --> 02:57:59.520
Their numbers swelled into the tens of billions,
as they created culture and technology hitherto

02:57:59.520 --> 02:58:02.760
unimagined – including weapons of devastating
power.

02:58:02.760 --> 02:58:07.320
Meanwhile, humanity was pushed to the brink
of destruction by their competitor’s rapid

02:58:07.319 --> 02:58:09.719
and seemingly unstoppable growth.

02:58:09.720 --> 02:58:14.460
It looked as though the human species had
lost the evolutionary arms race, and would

02:58:14.460 --> 02:58:19.380
have to bow out, but according to the Children
of the Sun, a trickster forest god smiled

02:58:19.380 --> 02:58:24.779
upon humanity, and gave them the power to
use SCP – 1000’s weapons and technology

02:58:24.779 --> 02:58:25.559
against them.

02:58:25.560 --> 02:58:31.980
70% of SCP – 1000’s population were wiped
out in a single horrific day, known to the

02:58:31.979 --> 02:58:36.779
Children of the Sun as “The Day of the Flowers”
– as every flower supposedly bloomed that

02:58:36.779 --> 02:58:38.580
day during the massacre.

02:58:38.580 --> 02:58:44.220
Humanity destroyed the entire civilization,
and with the same technology they stole from

02:58:44.220 --> 02:58:48.060
these unfortunate creatures, the vengeful
humans drove the apes mad.

02:58:48.060 --> 02:58:53.100
Their higher consciousnesses were blocked
out, reducing them back into the states of

02:58:53.100 --> 02:58:54.000
mere animals.

02:58:54.000 --> 02:58:58.800
Once the massacre was done and everything
that was built had been destroyed, we – the

02:58:58.800 --> 02:59:04.260
human race – used the SCP – 1000 weapons
to wipe any memory of the atrocity from our

02:59:04.260 --> 02:59:05.040
own minds.

02:59:05.040 --> 02:59:09.240
The advanced civilization of SCP – 1000
had been wiped from history.

02:59:09.240 --> 02:59:13.559
Humans returned to their plodding path of
evolution, none the wiser.

02:59:13.560 --> 02:59:18.720
For thousands of years, all the way up until
today, this time remained a mystery to us.

02:59:18.720 --> 02:59:21.360
So again, why did the Foundation lie to us?

02:59:21.359 --> 02:59:25.380
What did they have to gain, by convincing
us all that it was dangerous to even look

02:59:25.380 --> 02:59:26.220
at these creatures?

02:59:26.220 --> 02:59:30.540
Well, as the frequency of sightings and the
attempts at communication increased, people

02:59:30.540 --> 02:59:35.760
like Director Jones became aware of a frightening
possibility: What if the pendulum was swinging

02:59:35.760 --> 02:59:36.120
back?

02:59:36.120 --> 02:59:41.700
What if the apes were regaining their lost
intelligence, and worse, still harboured feelings

02:59:41.700 --> 02:59:45.559
of revenge for what we did to their species
thousands of years ago?

02:59:45.560 --> 02:59:50.880
Even the mere possibility that they could
do to us what we once did to them is a chance

02:59:50.880 --> 02:59:56.279
that the Foundation simply cannot take, and
thus, limiting contact between humans and

02:59:56.279 --> 02:59:59.819
SCP - 1000 at all costs is an absolute must.

02:59:59.819 --> 03:00:05.399
However, in spite of the Foundation’s fears,
one intercepted message from the apes suggests

03:00:05.399 --> 03:00:07.439
that their paranoia may be misplaced.

03:00:07.439 --> 03:00:12.479
This message, translated from an attempt at
communicating with Foundation personnel, reads

03:00:12.479 --> 03:00:14.700
simply as follows:
“we forgive you;

03:00:14.700 --> 03:00:19.080
given choice for now, not forever;
let us back in.”

03:00:19.080 --> 03:00:23.580
It’s enough to make you wonder what species
the Foundation should really be keeping tabs

03:00:23.580 --> 03:00:23.939
on here.

03:00:23.939 --> 03:00:28.439
After all, when it comes to meting out violence
and death, humanity has a track record to

03:00:28.439 --> 03:00:31.740
rival the worst creatures in the Foundation
containment cells.

03:00:31.740 --> 03:00:37.319
And few examples illustrate that better than
the tragic case of SCP – 1000.

